,"sha":"88635831d129cc86061b510a330c58e8787f0828","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/88635831d129cc86061b510a330c58e8787f0828"}],"sha":"e0e1c2a37f281384a8e5fc1ef18d2890c4d941d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/e0e1c2a37f281384a8e5fc1ef18d2890c4d941d4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83631045?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/naveen-egov","id":83631045,"login":"naveen-egov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNjMxMDQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/88635831d129cc86061b510a330c58e8787f0828/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T06:51:16Z","email":"83631045+naveen-egov@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Naveen J"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T06:51:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"BUGFIX/HCMPRE-0000 : Accessibility fixes for the App Configuration screen (#4514)\n\n* BUGFIX/HCMPRE-0000 : Accessibility fixes for the App Configuration screen\n\nAddresses the App Configuration findings from the 21 Sep 2026 UAT\naccessibility scan (DIGIT Accessibility Scanner, axe-core):\n\n- Buttons have no readable name (severe): aria-label + type=\"button\" on\n  the three icon-only panel close buttons; decorative SVGs hidden.\n- Form fields missing labels: aria-label + type=\"search\" on the flow\n  search and form-element search inputs.\n- Page missing a main heading: the flow name in the header bar is an h1\n  (health CSS resets heading sizes, so visuals are unchanged).\n- Keyboard operability: sidebar menu items, flow items, category\n  headers, page tabs, field-type cards and the preview arrows were\n  clickable divs; they now have role=\"button\", are focusable, expose\n  pressed/expanded/disabled state and respond to Enter and Space via a\n  single helper that re-dispatches the element''s own click.\n- Toggle controls: switches rendered with an empty label now pass an\n  ariaLabel (requires digit-ui-components Switch with ariaLabel support);\n  the delete-field icon control gets a name and keyboard handling.\n\nNew i18n keys: APP_CONFIG_CLOSE_PANEL, APP_CONFIG_PREVIOUS_PAGE,\nAPP_CONFIG_NEXT_PAGE, APP_CONFIG_TOGGLE_FIELD_VISIBILITY,\nAPP_CONFIG_DELETE_FIELD (en_IN messages to be added to\nhcm-campaignmanager).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* BUGFIX/HCMPRE-0000 : App Configuration - main landmark and named drawer inputs\n\nFollow-up from a live axe-core run against the App Configuration page\n(UAT baseline vs local build):\n\n- Page heading / description fields in the properties drawer had no\n  accessible name (axe \"label\", reported as \"Form fields are missing\n  labels\"): pass the visible label text to TextInput / TextArea.\n- The employee layout renders no <main>, so every element on the page\n  failed axe \"region\" and the page failed \"landmark-one-main\". The\n  wrapper now renders a <main> with display: contents, which exposes the\n  landmark without changing the flex layout.\n\nResult on the TRANSIT_POST flow of CMP-2026-09-17-006672 (with the\ncompanion digit-ui-components change): 13 rule violations -> 2\n(color-contrast on design-system token colours, and 3 \"region\" nodes in\nthe core top bar).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* BUGFIX/HCMPRE-0000 : Accessibility fixes for campaign home, create and setup campaign\n\nExtends the App Configuration work to the other pages in the UAT\naccessibility report, driven by live axe-core runs on each page:\n\n- Campaign home: the three method cards used tabIndex 0/1/2, forcing an\n  artificial tab order (axe tabindex, \"Tab order is forced into an\n  unnatural sequence\"); all are now 0 and all three respond to Enter /\n  Space. The page title is an h1 and the screen declares a <main>\n  landmark (display: contents keeps layout unchanged).\n- Create campaign and setup campaign: the step wrappers declare a <main>\n  landmark the same way, so page content is no longer outside every\n  landmark (axe region / landmark-one-main, \"Page has no main content\n  area\", \"Page sections are not labelled\").\n- Delivery rule attribute rows (setup-campaign step 8): the Attribute,\n  Operator and Value dropdowns and the From / To / Value inputs receive\n  their visible label as an accessible name (axe label /\n  label-title-only, \"Form fields are missing labels\", \"Form field is\n  labelled only by a title or hidden text\"). The delivery step title is\n  an h1.\n\nDepends on digit-ui-components changes in DIGIT-UI-LIBRARIES#443\n(Dropdown combobox semantics, TextInput ariaLabel, TextArea label).\n\nResult (local build with #443): campaign-home 5 -> 2 rule violations,\ncreate-campaign 5 -> 3, setup-campaign step 8 7 -> 2. What remains on\neach is color-contrast on design-system token colours and the core top\nbar / footer sitting outside any landmark.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* BUGFIX/HCMPRE-0000 : Breadcrumb bar as a navigation landmark\n\nThe campaign module''s breadcrumb / help bar (.wbh-header-container) was a\nplain div outside every landmark, flagged by axe \"region\" on every\ncampaign page. It is now a <nav aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\">; same class, so\nstyling is unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* BUGFIX/HCMPRE-0000 : Bump digit-ui-components, components-css and module-core\n\n- @egovernments/digit-ui-components 2.0.0-dev-64 -> 2.0.0-dev-65 (root and all\n  five module packages)\n- @egovernments/digit-ui-module-core 2.0.0-dev-35 -> 2.0.0-dev-37\n- @egovernments/digit-ui-components-css 2.0.0-dev-13 -> 2.0.0-dev-14 (unpkg\n  link in public/index.html and every builds/*/public/index.html)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e49deff3409139ad31cea97511217e3d60a36a28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/git/trees/e49deff3409139ad31cea97511217e3d60a36a28"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/git/commits/88635831d129cc86061b510a330c58e8787f0828","verification":{"payload":"tree e49deff3409139ad31cea97511217e3d60a36a28\nparent 5b31b5f873ba7c9923ccbac7c844c12e368a2330\nauthor Naveen J <83631045+naveen-egov@users.noreply.github.com> 1790059876 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790059876 +0530\n\nBUGFIX/HCMPRE-0000 : Accessibility fixes for the App Configuration screen (#4514)\n\n* BUGFIX/HCMPRE-0000 : Accessibility fixes for the App Configuration screen\n\nAddresses the App Configuration findings from the 21 Sep 2026 UAT\naccessibility scan (DIGIT Accessibility Scanner, axe-core):\n\n- Buttons have no readable name (severe): aria-label + type=\"button\" on\n  the three icon-only panel close buttons; decorative SVGs hidden.\n- Form fields missing labels: aria-label + type=\"search\" on the flow\n  search and form-element search inputs.\n- Page missing a main heading: the flow name in the header bar is an h1\n  (health CSS resets heading sizes, so visuals are unchanged).\n- Keyboard operability: sidebar menu items, flow items, category\n  headers, page tabs, field-type cards and the preview arrows were\n  clickable divs; they now have role=\"button\", are focusable, expose\n  pressed/expanded/disabled state and respond to Enter and Space via a\n  single helper that re-dispatches the element''s own click.\n- Toggle controls: switches rendered with an empty label now pass an\n  ariaLabel (requires digit-ui-components Switch with ariaLabel support);\n  the delete-field icon control gets a name and keyboard handling.\n\nNew i18n keys: APP_CONFIG_CLOSE_PANEL, APP_CONFIG_PREVIOUS_PAGE,\nAPP_CONFIG_NEXT_PAGE, APP_CONFIG_TOGGLE_FIELD_VISIBILITY,\nAPP_CONFIG_DELETE_FIELD (en_IN messages to be added to\nhcm-campaignmanager).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* BUGFIX/HCMPRE-0000 : App Configuration - main landmark and named drawer inputs\n\nFollow-up from a live axe-core run against the App Configuration page\n(UAT baseline vs local build):\n\n- Page heading / description fields in the properties drawer had no\n  accessible name (axe \"label\", reported as \"Form fields are missing\n  labels\"): pass the visible label text to TextInput / TextArea.\n- The employee layout renders no <main>, so every element on the page\n  failed axe \"region\" and the page failed \"landmark-one-main\". The\n  wrapper now renders a <main> with display: contents, which exposes the\n  landmark without changing the flex layout.\n\nResult on the TRANSIT_POST flow of CMP-2026-09-17-006672 (with the\ncompanion digit-ui-components change): 13 rule violations -> 2\n(color-contrast on design-system token colours, and 3 \"region\" nodes in\nthe core top bar).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* BUGFIX/HCMPRE-0000 : Accessibility fixes for campaign home, create and setup campaign\n\nExtends the App Configuration work to the other pages in the UAT\naccessibility report, driven by live axe-core runs on each page:\n\n- Campaign home: the three method cards used tabIndex 0/1/2, forcing an\n  artificial tab order (axe tabindex, \"Tab order is forced into an\n  unnatural sequence\"); all are now 0 and all three respond to Enter /\n  Space. The page title is an h1 and the screen declares a <main>\n  landmark (display: contents keeps layout unchanged).\n- Create campaign and setup campaign: the step wrappers declare a <main>\n  landmark the same way, so page content is no longer outside every\n  landmark (axe region / landmark-one-main, \"Page has no main content\n  area\", \"Page sections are not labelled\").\n- Delivery rule attribute rows (setup-campaign step 8): the Attribute,\n  Operator and Value dropdowns and the From / To / Value inputs receive\n  their visible label as an accessible name (axe label /\n  label-title-only, \"Form fields are missing labels\", \"Form field is\n  labelled only by a title or hidden text\"). The delivery step title is\n  an h1.\n\nDepends on digit-ui-components changes in DIGIT-UI-LIBRARIES#443\n(Dropdown combobox semantics, TextInput ariaLabel, TextArea label).\n\nResult (local build with #443): campaign-home 5 -> 2 rule violations,\ncreate-campaign 5 -> 3, setup-campaign step 8 7 -> 2. What remains on\neach is color-contrast on design-system token colours and the core top\nbar / footer sitting outside any landmark.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* BUGFIX/HCMPRE-0000 : Breadcrumb bar as a navigation landmark\n\nThe campaign module''s breadcrumb / help bar (.wbh-header-container) was a\nplain div outside every landmark, flagged by axe \"region\" on every\ncampaign page. It is now a <nav aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\">; same class, so\nstyling is unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* BUGFIX/HCMPRE-0000 : Bump digit-ui-components, components-css and module-core\n\n- @egovernments/digit-ui-components 2.0.0-dev-64 -> 2.0.0-dev-65 (root and all\n  five module packages)\n- @egovernments/digit-ui-module-core 2.0.0-dev-35 -> 2.0.0-dev-37\n- @egovernments/digit-ui-components-css 2.0.0-dev-13 -> 2.0.0-dev-14 (unpkg\n  link in public/index.html and every builds/*/public/index.html)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsiVkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9dAQAHiYLSCOVlrsbb4Uz0mMqHeG\nbh9flWhPI04MaaWH9vh9EVFYFmdbUudW2d7LL2XHDq31f1isO79gnu1mjdjE7njq\nFsXprftcCjPqY1NuuNgjyICtT4QZ4MuScwg4gGwYdyeYgK2MBIC2IhSLmsmraq55\nUdS5rHM234Z9mFMzZOw6DVAGaaMcvtDs9YKwldFAN9eWpdSmXAclmvhTeqy0oQx+\nrkf2ZEp4ucFLiF/02tqfL+uVlHSyIQqqgrE1/jevEZi0JlO4vkUPTO0RCqxlx6VW\nG6PJJUUFXZMCA4CUh42OjAzDBzygC0JVgODa8UnNEL/9eaSfE5aYGklnlhzD1g1l\nZeKny4HWip58NJlU86W6ccIWJXHQrmUIBRYhLAUdfUN8NbWK/Nq4dJhACbA4y8lM\ne4rr6+YR7e+/1NxS5pNDTyDOvU+r1mrlI/BXSB8nfcuIvnM4glnG/b/Xqd3/evo0\nkZ42Xl6YlM9WxZLXQT4Oc7+lvy6gwcd60p6g/H7APRJCYjTGHhfcYr5bOxdLTcxS\nxVGMD0CGG9qaK7epIws+8Cr/unGGxow4sOyGleWYMWOPVJvkIm2wb4CH6+PjPfeE\ngHMjUYqo+6hWbVe3XyHAZTlQ0XxpoY2BNpDv3PMqcrT+Geu9PEevA1IHAL/hKwRt\ncyVOzxiTEy0JShWIHdJX\n=kN41\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T06:51:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commit/88635831d129cc86061b510a330c58e8787f0828","node_id":"C_kwDOKSe0RtoAKDg4NjM1ODMxZDEyOWNjODYwNjFiNTEwYTMzMGM1OGU4Nzg3ZjA4Mjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commit/5b31b5f873ba7c9923ccbac7c844c12e368a2330","sha":"5b31b5f873ba7c9923ccbac7c844c12e368a2330","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/5b31b5f873ba7c9923ccbac7c844c12e368a2330"}],"sha":"88635831d129cc86061b510a330c58e8787f0828","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/88635831d129cc86061b510a330c58e8787f0828"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/137176788?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Swathi-eGov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Swathi-eGov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Swathi-eGov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Swathi-eGov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Swathi-eGov","id":137176788,"login":"Swathi-eGov","node_id":"U_kgDOCC0m1A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Swathi-eGov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Swathi-eGov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Swathi-eGov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Swathi-eGov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Swathi-eGov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Swathi-eGov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/5b31b5f873ba7c9923ccbac7c844c12e368a2330/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T09:04:55Z","email":"137176788+Swathi-eGov@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Swathi-eGov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T09:04:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"BUGFIX/HCMPRE-4444 : Fix zero-attendance erasing worker pay rates and missing payable rows (#4458)\n\n* BUGFIX/HCMPRE-4444 : Fix zero-attendance erasing worker pay rates\n\n* BUGFIX/HCMPRE-4444 : Fix zero-attendance erasing worker pay rates and missing payable rows\n\n* updated core versions","tree":{"sha":"aaae0482af3fd7c593932adfd771c25ac8487278","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/git/trees/aaae0482af3fd7c593932adfd771c25ac8487278"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/git/commits/5b31b5f873ba7c9923ccbac7c844c12e368a2330","verification":{"payload":"tree aaae0482af3fd7c593932adfd771c25ac8487278\nparent 63e6feb4aa2dfe890f8b3b68ef4af61b249758b5\nauthor Swathi-eGov <137176788+Swathi-eGov@users.noreply.github.com> 1789031095 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789031095 +0530\n\nBUGFIX/HCMPRE-4444 : Fix zero-attendance erasing worker pay rates and missing payable rows (#4458)\n\n* BUGFIX/HCMPRE-4444 : Fix zero-attendance erasing worker pay rates\n\n* BUGFIX/HCMPRE-4444 : Fix zero-attendance erasing worker pay rates and missing payable rows\n\n* updated core versions","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqonK3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjcAQAGZCPJRbdDuqXwk2333PMVAO\n6JqWBh5geAh8dfvg6teHMWfkvQsdNG9dSs646cVjEIse2AVBrwoUgW8KtfUsrsBT\nNwqJYQp5ddVsDllYnhZ1n7s7/1YNGAm2iMpwvLz5E2JtXeGa+1v4rEo5FLqLZhB3\no0axkEuLanax0qOwUKMKEFZNedsmLddieeaA/4qZBuAOOGTVz0ZNkwKfyis35mJ8\nuuJsFSAO4AYvWxEkETkMu6Lxs3AV111cQ6AZXC0g2x2UKx/ur1HRUn6aIP54oPAA\njYnUdD7fz1hnLbT20bAFx6/0m705oqTtClmPWUEk5wZRPWtZ46Z6vQbKkoh6MGTZ\npAW4nK3Tdwc1dHDvd37WxRlgFIw0tcU6Sl6t8I+Y8n9Ecph3xd0ZURP+O89V08Dg\nWDjb5RPr+SMWT337k22kL4EgrN5SqZHOa88fu+Wc6JVHn5ir67WZ1mQCXqvoxSIf\nF79pRlo6fIedA9/OBsQYTTLKxzWoCRX8U2TR07ESiAAfklTiClnvtUYB16IQqH8V\nJY8YlcBHhPuwrp7yss8BUPKRwRMCD2TTFaab2RK69lIZtUqUIDC5GdWYZ6BvlCie\nx57D8oKf5Sgs+OLp3tWFimZOZ71r9TLedqdu5EqFe8HXSJzOCZv51TaW4dk2vxIl\nxdNP0qbo0aD3upBtyOA9\n=0SCe\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-10T09:04:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commit/5b31b5f873ba7c9923ccbac7c844c12e368a2330","node_id":"C_kwDOKSe0RtoAKDViMzFiNWY4NzNiYTdjOTkyM2NjYmFjN2M4NDRjMTJlMzY4YTIzMzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commit/63e6feb4aa2dfe890f8b3b68ef4af61b249758b5","sha":"63e6feb4aa2dfe890f8b3b68ef4af61b249758b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/63e6feb4aa2dfe890f8b3b68ef4af61b249758b5"}],"sha":"5b31b5f873ba7c9923ccbac7c844c12e368a2330","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/5b31b5f873ba7c9923ccbac7c844c12e368a2330"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83631045?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/naveen-egov","id":83631045,"login":"naveen-egov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNjMxMDQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/63e6feb4aa2dfe890f8b3b68ef4af61b249758b5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T08:51:49Z","email":"83631045+naveen-egov@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Naveen J"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T08:51:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Hcm appconfig textarea panel item (#4454)\n\n* Render textarea panel items in the field-properties drawer\n\nThe noResultCard supplemental panel item (\"Household not found\" description on\nthe search screens) is declared with fieldType \"textarea\", but RenderField''s\nswitch had no textarea case, so it fell through to `default: return null` —\nthe drawer showed an empty property box and the card''s description could not\nbe edited at all. The FieldTypeMappingConfig master maps the card to\nfieldType noResultCard correctly and the panel item was already merged in;\nonly the renderer was missing.\n\nRoute \"textarea\" through the existing text case, passing the fieldType to\nFieldV1, which already renders a TextArea for type=\"textarea\". Also include\ntextarea in the local-value seeding effect, which was gated to text/number —\nwithout that the new control rendered but came up blank instead of pre-filled\nwith the current localized description.\n\nVerified locally against the running console: the Description textarea now\nappears under Title for the Household-not-found card and edits persist via\nthe same localisation path as Title.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Centre the QR code in the app-config popup preview\n\nThe QR icon rendered left of centre in the actionPopup preview. QRView already\nset justifyContent:center, but the centring was scoped to the wrong box.\n\nEvery field in the preview is wrapped by renderTemplateComponent in\n.template-field-wrapper, and that class is `width:100%; display:flex` with the\ndefault justify-content:flex-start (campaign.scss). QRView''s container set no\nwidth, so as a flex item it took the default `flex: 0 1 auto` and shrank to fit\nits content — a narrow box pinned to the left edge. Its own justifyContent then\nonly centred the icon inside that narrow box, leaving the QR sitting left of\nthe popup''s centre line.\n\nGive the container an explicit width:100% so it fills the flex line and the\nexisting centring applies against the popup width. `flex: 1` would work too;\nwidth is preferred because it stays local to QRView and cannot affect other\ncomponents sharing the same wrapper.\n\nOther field types were unaffected because they either stretch naturally or have\nexplicit rules (e.g. .template-field-wrapper .digit-text-input-field in\nappConfiguration.scss). QRView was the one that set no width at all.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Skip computed {{fn:...}} label keys in labelPairList properties panel\n\nThe Transaction Details labelPairList config uses runtime-computed keys like\n{{fn:getSecondPagePartyLabel(...)}}; the Elements panel ran them through t()\nand printed the raw expression as the field label (issue #4262 pt 10). These\nlabels are resolved in the app at runtime and have no editable localisation,\nso skip rendering a LocalizationInput for them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Make popup description editable and render it in the popup preview\n\nPopup label fields in the field-properties drawer (PopupLabelField) display\nuseCustomT(code) and write edits via updateLocalizationEntry under that code.\nSeeded templates carry popupConfig.description as an empty string, and\nuseCustomT(\"\") short-circuits to \"\" — so the description input rendered but\nnever reflected a single keystroke, and edits were stored under the empty\ncode. The title only worked because it has a real localization code\n(e.g. INSUFFICIENT_STOCK_TITLE).\n\nTwo further problems surfaced while fixing it:\n\n- Typing straight against redux scrambled fast input (\"ererSelecdeet…\"):\n  each keystroke re-rendered the controlled input from the store before the\n  next key landed.\n- The phone preview never showed the description at all: NewLayoutRenderer\n  passed only alertMessage, which the DIGIT PopUp component ignores for\n  default-type popups; PopUp renders a separate `description` prop.\n\nFixes, verified against the running console (Filter popup on Search\nHouseholds and Insufficient stock popup on Delivery Summary):\n\n- On first edit of a label with no code, mint POPUP_<PATH>_<timestamp>\n  (same convention as NewDrawerFieldComposer), persist it into popupConfig\n  via updateSelectedField, and store the message under it. The minted code\n  stays stable across keystrokes via a ref.\n- Hold the input value in local state with an isEditingRef guard (the\n  composer''s localValue pattern) so typing is smooth; redux stays the\n  source of truth when not editing.\n- Pass description={t(popupConfig.description)} to the preview PopUp so the\n  description renders under the popup title and updates live while typing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Tighten label column on the Add new resource screen\n\nThe Resource name/type/variant labels sat in a fixed 19rem column while the\ntext is ~8rem, leaving a large gap between each label and its input. Reduce\nthe column to 10rem so inputs sit next to their labels.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Do not double-render the popup description for alert-type popups\n\nThe preview PopUp received both alertMessage and description. The DIGIT PopUp\ncomponent renders alertMessage inside its alert section when type=\"alert\",\nand it also renders the description prop for every popup type — so alert\npopups showed the description twice.\n\nPass description only for non-alert popups: alert popups keep alertMessage,\ndefault popups keep description, each rendering exactly once. Verified on the\nFilter popup (default type) in the running console.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Close the label-to-field gap in the Add Resource to Deliver popup\n\nBoth LabelFieldPairs in the popup stack the label above the field, but the\ncomponent class ships a horizontal-layout gap (spacer6), leaving ~2.5rem\nbetween \"Resources to be delivered\"/\"Count\" and their inputs. Override with\nthe vertical-layout gap (0.5rem, spacer2).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Seed Edit Boundaries from the saved draft when session selection is empty\n\nClicking Edit Boundaries after visiting other setup steps in the same SPA\nsession showed empty dropdowns: a leftover session entry with an empty\nselectedData both disabled the draft search (enabled: !hasSessionData) and\nwon the seeding branch. Treat an empty selection as \"no session data\" so the\nsaved draft populates the boundary screen; a hard refresh already behaved\nthis way because the in-memory store starts empty.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Name the boundary and delivery-strategy steps in the setup breadcrumb\n\nThe boundary (key 5-6) and delivery-strategy (key 7-9) steps are entered from\nseparate campaign-home cards but shared the generic \"Setup campaign\" crumb.\nPick the label from the step key so the trail names where the user actually is\n(CAMPAIGN_BREADCRUMB_SET_BOUNDARY / CAMPAIGN_BREADCRUMB_DELIVERY_STRATEGY).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Drop the \"Add Label:\" prefix from popup option rows in the properties panel\n\nFilter-popup option rows read \"Add Label: Administered Successfully\" etc.;\nthe prefix is editor chrome, not part of the option name. Show just the\nlocalised option name; table columns keep their \"Column:\" prefix.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* List MDMS-driven popup options from the master, matching the preview\n\nFor fields with isMdms + schemaCode (e.g. the Search Households filter,\nHCM.SEARCH_HOUSEHOLD_FILTERS) the runtime and preview resolve options from\nthe MDMS master, but the panel rendered the config''s stale 2-entry enums.\nFetch the same master and list every active option; hide the per-option\ntoggles for these since the option set lives in a shared master, not the\ncampaign config. Label localisation stays editable per option.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Keep show/hide toggles for MDMS-driven popup options\n\nThe app renders the config enums filtered by isActive, so the per-option\ntoggle is a real feature. Merge the master option set with the existing\nenums (preserving label codes and isActive), list every option with its\ntoggle, and materialise the merged list back into enums so the app receives\nthe full set instead of the stale two-entry leftover.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Treat config enums as the per-campaign selection of MDMS popup options\n\nenums is the mapping the app actually renders (filtered by isActive); the\nmaster only defines the available pool. Panel: list every master option with\nits show/hide toggle, defaulting unmapped options to OFF so behaviour is\nunchanged until enabled. Preview: render the enums selection like the device\ndoes, falling back to the master list only when no selection exists yet.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Group body/template buttons under a Buttons section in the page drawer\n\nHousehold Overview and the success screens carry their CTAs in the page body,\nso they rendered as ordinary rows in the Template elements list while other\npages show footer buttons under a dedicated \"Buttons\" section. Render button\nrows after the same subheader; the rows keep their combined-list index so the\nexisting card/field index math and toggle rules are unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Render a single Buttons section when button rows and footer labels coexist\n\nWhen body/template button rows already open a Buttons subheader, the footer\nlabel inputs join that section instead of opening a second identical heading.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Hide the Required toggle for read-only fields\n\nA read-only field (e.g. Refer Beneficiary -> Referred By, auto-filled with\nthe logged-in user) cannot be edited in the app, so a Required control is\nmeaningless; the drawer showed it permanently locked instead. Skip rendering\nit for readOnly fields.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Present the page-level info card as an element, matching body infoCards\n\nMark Closed Household models its info card as page-level conditions.infoCardText,\nwhich the drawer rendered as a bare textarea in the page-header block — while\nReferral pages show their infoCard body field as a Template element with an\nInfocard tag. Render the page-level info card in the elements area with the\nsame element styling and tag so both patterns look alike; the message stays\neditable in place.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Add a show/hide toggle to the page-level info card element\n\nParity with body infoCard elements: toggling off stashes the localisation\ncode in conditions.infoCardTextDisabled and nulls infoCardText (the only key\nthe app checks), toggling on restores it. The message textarea shows only\nwhile the card is on.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Drop the duplicated inner label on the info card element\n\nThe element row already carries the \"Info card\" title and Infocard tag; the\ntextarea rendered its own identical label beneath. Add a hideLabel prop to\nHeaderFieldWrapper and use it there.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Open Field properties when clicking the page-level info card element\n\nConsole-only interaction parity with body infoCard fields: clicking the\nelement selects a pseudo-field so the regular Field-properties view opens,\nwith only the message (description) editable — the title item is skipped\nsince the app hardcodes it. Message edits flow through the localisation\nslice exactly as before; the config and app payload shapes are untouched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Skip Required panel item wrapper for read-only fields to avoid empty card\n\nThe toggle case in RenderField already returns null for bindTo=required on\nread-only fields, but the drawer-toggle-field-container wrapper still\nrendered, leaving a blank grey card in the drawer (seen on Stock in Hand).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Re-apply boundary selection when session or draft data arrives late\n\nThe load effect only ran on [isFetching, campaignNumber], so a session entry\nhydrating after mount (or rewritten while navigating back through setup\nsteps) was never applied and Edit Boundary showed an empty selection.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Don''t let an empty session entry clobber seeded boundaries in update flow\n\nThe session-sync effect in UpdateBoundaryWrapper overwrote the selection on\nany boundaryType reference change, including entries with an empty\nselectedData (left behind by other setup steps or written by the save effect\nbefore CampaignData seeded), blanking the Update/Edit Boundary screen.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Always refetch campaign draft when seeding Edit Boundaries\n\nThe project-type search was cached with a 10-minute staleTime, so after\nsubmitting a boundary change (which clears the setup session) reopening Edit\nBoundaries re-seeded from the cached pre-submit draft and showed the old\nselection.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Seed boundary selection once to stop session write-back render loop\n\nThe parent recreates the session object on every save, so re-applying\nsession data whenever its reference changed looped seed → save → session\nchange → seed (Maximum update depth exceeded) and the boundary levels never\nrendered. Seed from draft or session exactly once; after that the user''s\nlocal edits own the state.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Hide footer label inputs when footer buttons render as element rows\n\nOn template pages the footer buttons already appear as clickable rows in\nthe Buttons section (label editable via Field properties), so the\nper-footer \"Primary action button label\" inputs duplicated that. Form\npages keep the inputs — they have no button rows.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Group all footer rows under the Buttons section, not just format=button\n\nFooter entries all render in the app''s bottom action bar, but the drawer\nonly grouped format=button rows there — Scan QR (qrScanner) and Download\nBeneficiary IDs (actionPopup) landed among the template elements instead.\nFooter-originated rows now always join the Buttons section, and count for\nthe last-visible-button guard and the footer-label dedupe.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Block hiding the last visible menu card on a menu screen\n\nA menu screen like Manage Stock with every menu card switched off would be\na dead end in the app, so the last visible menu card keeps the same\nguard-with-toast the last button already has.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Raise app-config toast above the phone preview and footer bar\n\nThe library toast is fixed-position with z-index 20, so on the app-config\nscreen it slid beneath the preview canvas (z-index 40-100) and the save\nfooter (1000), clipping the start of guard messages.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Render the app-config toast outside the clipping preview container\n\nThe toast lived inside full-config-wrapper__container, whose\ncenter-content/preview-area scroll areas (overflow hidden/auto) clip\nfixed descendants in Chrome — the message was cut off at the canvas\nleft edge. Rendered as a sibling of the container instead; together\nwith the z-index raise it now sits fully above the preview.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Portal the app-config toast to body to escape preview clipping\n\nAppConfigurationWrapper''s toast (the one window.__appConfig_showToast\nactually drives) mounts inside the preview area, whose overflow\nhidden/auto containers clip fixed descendants — messages were cut off at\nthe canvas left edge. Rendering it through a portal to document.body\nshows the full message above the preview.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Group popup-opening actions under the Buttons section\n\nactionPopup and qrScanner rows render as buttons in the app (View QR,\nFilter, Sort, Download IDs), so they now join the Buttons section like\nplain buttons and footer rows do.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Card-style the footer button label editor on form pages\n\nForm pages rendered the Buttons section as a bare label + input while\ntemplate pages show grey element-row cards — the footer label editor now\nsits in the same card with a Button tag, unifying the section styling\nacross Record Stock, Record Less/Excess, Household Registration and the\nother form pages.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Match the footer button card to field cards, edit label on click\n\nThe Buttons section''s footer label editor rendered as a card with the\nButton tag beside the title and an always-visible text input, unlike the\nfield cards (title with the type tag beneath, editor opens on click).\nThe card now shares the field-card anatomy — the button label as the\ntitle, Button tag under it — and clicking the card reveals the\nautofocused label input, closing again on blur.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix required-field error message traps on seeded checklist pages\n\nSeeded configs (e.g. the Delivery Checklist) mark fields required\nwithout an error message, and the mandatory-error-message validation\nthen blocked every navigation away from a page the user never touched.\nRequired fields loaded without a message now get a deterministic\nlocalization code (keyed off the field''s label so sibling checklist\nitems sharing a fieldName stay independent) seeded with the drawer''s\nconfig-driven default text (the Error message input''s innerLabel from\nFieldPropertiesPanelConfig).\n\nAlso key ConditionalField on the selected field: the component holds a\npending debounce plus refs to the field''s localization code, so reusing\none instance across field switches flushed text typed on one field into\nthe code of the next field selected — error messages typed on one\nchecklist item leaked into its siblings.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bfdc4eba65a54cb7e352b1c7472a379ef008e263","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/git/trees/bfdc4eba65a54cb7e352b1c7472a379ef008e263"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/git/commits/63e6feb4aa2dfe890f8b3b68ef4af61b249758b5","verification":{"payload":"tree bfdc4eba65a54cb7e352b1c7472a379ef008e263\nparent 89df4c71fa01c16393426c7d9ae7d3bdc0a44c07\nauthor Naveen J <83631045+naveen-egov@users.noreply.github.com> 1788943909 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788943909 +0530\n\nHcm appconfig textarea panel item (#4454)\n\n* Render textarea panel items in the field-properties drawer\n\nThe noResultCard supplemental panel item (\"Household not found\" description on\nthe search screens) is declared with fieldType \"textarea\", but RenderField''s\nswitch had no textarea case, so it fell through to `default: return null` —\nthe drawer showed an empty property box and the card''s description could not\nbe edited at all. The FieldTypeMappingConfig master maps the card to\nfieldType noResultCard correctly and the panel item was already merged in;\nonly the renderer was missing.\n\nRoute \"textarea\" through the existing text case, passing the fieldType to\nFieldV1, which already renders a TextArea for type=\"textarea\". Also include\ntextarea in the local-value seeding effect, which was gated to text/number —\nwithout that the new control rendered but came up blank instead of pre-filled\nwith the current localized description.\n\nVerified locally against the running console: the Description textarea now\nappears under Title for the Household-not-found card and edits persist via\nthe same localisation path as Title.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Centre the QR code in the app-config popup preview\n\nThe QR icon rendered left of centre in the actionPopup preview. QRView already\nset justifyContent:center, but the centring was scoped to the wrong box.\n\nEvery field in the preview is wrapped by renderTemplateComponent in\n.template-field-wrapper, and that class is `width:100%; display:flex` with the\ndefault justify-content:flex-start (campaign.scss). QRView''s container set no\nwidth, so as a flex item it took the default `flex: 0 1 auto` and shrank to fit\nits content — a narrow box pinned to the left edge. Its own justifyContent then\nonly centred the icon inside that narrow box, leaving the QR sitting left of\nthe popup''s centre line.\n\nGive the container an explicit width:100% so it fills the flex line and the\nexisting centring applies against the popup width. `flex: 1` would work too;\nwidth is preferred because it stays local to QRView and cannot affect other\ncomponents sharing the same wrapper.\n\nOther field types were unaffected because they either stretch naturally or have\nexplicit rules (e.g. .template-field-wrapper .digit-text-input-field in\nappConfiguration.scss). QRView was the one that set no width at all.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Skip computed {{fn:...}} label keys in labelPairList properties panel\n\nThe Transaction Details labelPairList config uses runtime-computed keys like\n{{fn:getSecondPagePartyLabel(...)}}; the Elements panel ran them through t()\nand printed the raw expression as the field label (issue #4262 pt 10). These\nlabels are resolved in the app at runtime and have no editable localisation,\nso skip rendering a LocalizationInput for them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Make popup description editable and render it in the popup preview\n\nPopup label fields in the field-properties drawer (PopupLabelField) display\nuseCustomT(code) and write edits via updateLocalizationEntry under that code.\nSeeded templates carry popupConfig.description as an empty string, and\nuseCustomT(\"\") short-circuits to \"\" — so the description input rendered but\nnever reflected a single keystroke, and edits were stored under the empty\ncode. The title only worked because it has a real localization code\n(e.g. INSUFFICIENT_STOCK_TITLE).\n\nTwo further problems surfaced while fixing it:\n\n- Typing straight against redux scrambled fast input (\"ererSelecdeet…\"):\n  each keystroke re-rendered the controlled input from the store before the\n  next key landed.\n- The phone preview never showed the description at all: NewLayoutRenderer\n  passed only alertMessage, which the DIGIT PopUp component ignores for\n  default-type popups; PopUp renders a separate `description` prop.\n\nFixes, verified against the running console (Filter popup on Search\nHouseholds and Insufficient stock popup on Delivery Summary):\n\n- On first edit of a label with no code, mint POPUP_<PATH>_<timestamp>\n  (same convention as NewDrawerFieldComposer), persist it into popupConfig\n  via updateSelectedField, and store the message under it. The minted code\n  stays stable across keystrokes via a ref.\n- Hold the input value in local state with an isEditingRef guard (the\n  composer''s localValue pattern) so typing is smooth; redux stays the\n  source of truth when not editing.\n- Pass description={t(popupConfig.description)} to the preview PopUp so the\n  description renders under the popup title and updates live while typing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Tighten label column on the Add new resource screen\n\nThe Resource name/type/variant labels sat in a fixed 19rem column while the\ntext is ~8rem, leaving a large gap between each label and its input. Reduce\nthe column to 10rem so inputs sit next to their labels.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Do not double-render the popup description for alert-type popups\n\nThe preview PopUp received both alertMessage and description. The DIGIT PopUp\ncomponent renders alertMessage inside its alert section when type=\"alert\",\nand it also renders the description prop for every popup type — so alert\npopups showed the description twice.\n\nPass description only for non-alert popups: alert popups keep alertMessage,\ndefault popups keep description, each rendering exactly once. Verified on the\nFilter popup (default type) in the running console.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Close the label-to-field gap in the Add Resource to Deliver popup\n\nBoth LabelFieldPairs in the popup stack the label above the field, but the\ncomponent class ships a horizontal-layout gap (spacer6), leaving ~2.5rem\nbetween \"Resources to be delivered\"/\"Count\" and their inputs. Override with\nthe vertical-layout gap (0.5rem, spacer2).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Seed Edit Boundaries from the saved draft when session selection is empty\n\nClicking Edit Boundaries after visiting other setup steps in the same SPA\nsession showed empty dropdowns: a leftover session entry with an empty\nselectedData both disabled the draft search (enabled: !hasSessionData) and\nwon the seeding branch. Treat an empty selection as \"no session data\" so the\nsaved draft populates the boundary screen; a hard refresh already behaved\nthis way because the in-memory store starts empty.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Name the boundary and delivery-strategy steps in the setup breadcrumb\n\nThe boundary (key 5-6) and delivery-strategy (key 7-9) steps are entered from\nseparate campaign-home cards but shared the generic \"Setup campaign\" crumb.\nPick the label from the step key so the trail names where the user actually is\n(CAMPAIGN_BREADCRUMB_SET_BOUNDARY / CAMPAIGN_BREADCRUMB_DELIVERY_STRATEGY).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Drop the \"Add Label:\" prefix from popup option rows in the properties panel\n\nFilter-popup option rows read \"Add Label: Administered Successfully\" etc.;\nthe prefix is editor chrome, not part of the option name. Show just the\nlocalised option name; table columns keep their \"Column:\" prefix.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* List MDMS-driven popup options from the master, matching the preview\n\nFor fields with isMdms + schemaCode (e.g. the Search Households filter,\nHCM.SEARCH_HOUSEHOLD_FILTERS) the runtime and preview resolve options from\nthe MDMS master, but the panel rendered the config''s stale 2-entry enums.\nFetch the same master and list every active option; hide the per-option\ntoggles for these since the option set lives in a shared master, not the\ncampaign config. Label localisation stays editable per option.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Keep show/hide toggles for MDMS-driven popup options\n\nThe app renders the config enums filtered by isActive, so the per-option\ntoggle is a real feature. Merge the master option set with the existing\nenums (preserving label codes and isActive), list every option with its\ntoggle, and materialise the merged list back into enums so the app receives\nthe full set instead of the stale two-entry leftover.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Treat config enums as the per-campaign selection of MDMS popup options\n\nenums is the mapping the app actually renders (filtered by isActive); the\nmaster only defines the available pool. Panel: list every master option with\nits show/hide toggle, defaulting unmapped options to OFF so behaviour is\nunchanged until enabled. Preview: render the enums selection like the device\ndoes, falling back to the master list only when no selection exists yet.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Group body/template buttons under a Buttons section in the page drawer\n\nHousehold Overview and the success screens carry their CTAs in the page body,\nso they rendered as ordinary rows in the Template elements list while other\npages show footer buttons under a dedicated \"Buttons\" section. Render button\nrows after the same subheader; the rows keep their combined-list index so the\nexisting card/field index math and toggle rules are unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Render a single Buttons section when button rows and footer labels coexist\n\nWhen body/template button rows already open a Buttons subheader, the footer\nlabel inputs join that section instead of opening a second identical heading.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Hide the Required toggle for read-only fields\n\nA read-only field (e.g. Refer Beneficiary -> Referred By, auto-filled with\nthe logged-in user) cannot be edited in the app, so a Required control is\nmeaningless; the drawer showed it permanently locked instead. Skip rendering\nit for readOnly fields.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Present the page-level info card as an element, matching body infoCards\n\nMark Closed Household models its info card as page-level conditions.infoCardText,\nwhich the drawer rendered as a bare textarea in the page-header block — while\nReferral pages show their infoCard body field as a Template element with an\nInfocard tag. Render the page-level info card in the elements area with the\nsame element styling and tag so both patterns look alike; the message stays\neditable in place.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Add a show/hide toggle to the page-level info card element\n\nParity with body infoCard elements: toggling off stashes the localisation\ncode in conditions.infoCardTextDisabled and nulls infoCardText (the only key\nthe app checks), toggling on restores it. The message textarea shows only\nwhile the card is on.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Drop the duplicated inner label on the info card element\n\nThe element row already carries the \"Info card\" title and Infocard tag; the\ntextarea rendered its own identical label beneath. Add a hideLabel prop to\nHeaderFieldWrapper and use it there.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Open Field properties when clicking the page-level info card element\n\nConsole-only interaction parity with body infoCard fields: clicking the\nelement selects a pseudo-field so the regular Field-properties view opens,\nwith only the message (description) editable — the title item is skipped\nsince the app hardcodes it. Message edits flow through the localisation\nslice exactly as before; the config and app payload shapes are untouched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Skip Required panel item wrapper for read-only fields to avoid empty card\n\nThe toggle case in RenderField already returns null for bindTo=required on\nread-only fields, but the drawer-toggle-field-container wrapper still\nrendered, leaving a blank grey card in the drawer (seen on Stock in Hand).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Re-apply boundary selection when session or draft data arrives late\n\nThe load effect only ran on [isFetching, campaignNumber], so a session entry\nhydrating after mount (or rewritten while navigating back through setup\nsteps) was never applied and Edit Boundary showed an empty selection.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Don''t let an empty session entry clobber seeded boundaries in update flow\n\nThe session-sync effect in UpdateBoundaryWrapper overwrote the selection on\nany boundaryType reference change, including entries with an empty\nselectedData (left behind by other setup steps or written by the save effect\nbefore CampaignData seeded), blanking the Update/Edit Boundary screen.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Always refetch campaign draft when seeding Edit Boundaries\n\nThe project-type search was cached with a 10-minute staleTime, so after\nsubmitting a boundary change (which clears the setup session) reopening Edit\nBoundaries re-seeded from the cached pre-submit draft and showed the old\nselection.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Seed boundary selection once to stop session write-back render loop\n\nThe parent recreates the session object on every save, so re-applying\nsession data whenever its reference changed looped seed → save → session\nchange → seed (Maximum update depth exceeded) and the boundary levels never\nrendered. Seed from draft or session exactly once; after that the user''s\nlocal edits own the state.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Hide footer label inputs when footer buttons render as element rows\n\nOn template pages the footer buttons already appear as clickable rows in\nthe Buttons section (label editable via Field properties), so the\nper-footer \"Primary action button label\" inputs duplicated that. Form\npages keep the inputs — they have no button rows.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Group all footer rows under the Buttons section, not just format=button\n\nFooter entries all render in the app''s bottom action bar, but the drawer\nonly grouped format=button rows there — Scan QR (qrScanner) and Download\nBeneficiary IDs (actionPopup) landed among the template elements instead.\nFooter-originated rows now always join the Buttons section, and count for\nthe last-visible-button guard and the footer-label dedupe.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Block hiding the last visible menu card on a menu screen\n\nA menu screen like Manage Stock with every menu card switched off would be\na dead end in the app, so the last visible menu card keeps the same\nguard-with-toast the last button already has.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Raise app-config toast above the phone preview and footer bar\n\nThe library toast is fixed-position with z-index 20, so on the app-config\nscreen it slid beneath the preview canvas (z-index 40-100) and the save\nfooter (1000), clipping the start of guard messages.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Render the app-config toast outside the clipping preview container\n\nThe toast lived inside full-config-wrapper__container, whose\ncenter-content/preview-area scroll areas (overflow hidden/auto) clip\nfixed descendants in Chrome — the message was cut off at the canvas\nleft edge. Rendered as a sibling of the container instead; together\nwith the z-index raise it now sits fully above the preview.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Portal the app-config toast to body to escape preview clipping\n\nAppConfigurationWrapper''s toast (the one window.__appConfig_showToast\nactually drives) mounts inside the preview area, whose overflow\nhidden/auto containers clip fixed descendants — messages were cut off at\nthe canvas left edge. Rendering it through a portal to document.body\nshows the full message above the preview.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Group popup-opening actions under the Buttons section\n\nactionPopup and qrScanner rows render as buttons in the app (View QR,\nFilter, Sort, Download IDs), so they now join the Buttons section like\nplain buttons and footer rows do.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Card-style the footer button label editor on form pages\n\nForm pages rendered the Buttons section as a bare label + input while\ntemplate pages show grey element-row cards — the footer label editor now\nsits in the same card with a Button tag, unifying the section styling\nacross Record Stock, Record Less/Excess, Household Registration and the\nother form pages.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Match the footer button card to field cards, edit label on click\n\nThe Buttons section''s footer label editor rendered as a card with the\nButton tag beside the title and an always-visible text input, unlike the\nfield cards (title with the type tag beneath, editor opens on click).\nThe card now shares the field-card anatomy — the button label as the\ntitle, Button tag under it — and clicking the card reveals the\nautofocused label input, closing again on blur.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix required-field error message traps on seeded checklist pages\n\nSeeded configs (e.g. the Delivery Checklist) mark fields required\nwithout an error message, and the mandatory-error-message validation\nthen blocked every navigation away from a page the user never touched.\nRequired fields loaded without a message now get a deterministic\nlocalization code (keyed off the field''s label so sibling checklist\nitems sharing a fieldName stay independent) seeded with the drawer''s\nconfig-driven default text (the Error message input''s innerLabel from\nFieldPropertiesPanelConfig).\n\nAlso key ConditionalField on the selected field: the component holds a\npending debounce plus refs to the field''s localization code, so reusing\none instance across field switches flushed text typed on one field into\nthe code of the next field selected — error messages typed on one\nchecklist item leaked into its siblings.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoR4lCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIRoQAIEte+hJy4pJAkU7zpdttYOk\npIFuoK1pfNnkhnqsWJDAizKU0is0mLdim+zFO19PZrIfx7WFvsyJ2omiwml+/Y8p\nTEkW0v0wAul39ZdtHeF550GDptYN2xbz9O2/mTdTqDpISqiGwcP3+M8jyQd2rI4h\nTp6mvh9HMA/KIaAbHJmxI4cxaYnnWaGaqkSpibcz9AAnXwdCX94qaNzDMJq7IxAO\nSdx6EmI5g5yPSsaWRxdt1jC6R9TOoqiBFj3jby4qJ4MQT2Q3XdOZaRExITx6PITO\nIARU2700GP+Yn9hcjVEPEwAZFgMeVaHAFVwx4quTeQ24re1jmEJwsasgmXg2ZUuQ\niu5F1LIRXwB9p8rIBkAAdGpYqx1JzofKd0nx1lX//5MbJKMXd+y4V6QD0iJL4LHm\n6Em+I5fV7lwSGW3xchGGtOHIRvUD4Kjj91DsB2+k2RPb1PIZiu2MxCcvoh2WKfeo\nsnk6Z23653z6hltrfYki45P7z0naxNqrqMG4xdTgIFo59Tr0Ua3+vXnmfLcMVL3v\nwZrCsM2nmyuvqNDurK7BPZyDGGEYkx5sdo637889QDpmkQjZZRo0c7DZP0dIjtGQ\n3yqbU6cOBbVs28+ShcIELlvKOhciLm8fAxnenej6QTQxEsR2H/utA0KmlyQJvkpn\nfFD6JFTUXgy8bbYbEtyh\n=bSOM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T08:51:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.co