/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/42a5a19040ecf9eb7268202d1a1127f0bcfcd562"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83631045?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/naveen-egov","id":83631045,"login":"naveen-egov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNjMxMDQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/d24acb0bcbefbbd2e608214b60295d0af12ff536/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T12:47:49Z","email":"83631045+naveen-egov@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Naveen J"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T12:47:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"FEATURE : Status tag grouping with simulated preview states in AppConfig v2 (#4274)\n\n* FEATURE : Simulate runtime visibility states in AppConfig preview\n\nThe mobile app decides element visibility with device-side expressions\n(fn:isDelivered(...) == true && ...), so the preview showed every status\ntag and action button stacked - a screen that never exists on device.\n\nAdds a Preview state switcher above the phone frame: scenarios are\nderived from the page''s own visible expressions, picking one fixes its\nfn-terms and every other conditional element is shown or hidden by\nlogical consistency. ''All states'' (default) keeps the full inventory,\nnow marked with a dashed outline so authors can tell which elements are\nruntime-conditional. The selected field is always rendered so it stays\neditable, and unparseable expressions are never hidden.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FEATURE : Group status tags and buttons under an Actions tab in page properties\n\nTemplate pages split page properties into Elements and Actions tabs.\nThe Actions tab groups the runtime-conditional items - status tags\n(with a note that only one shows at a time on the device) and action\nbuttons/popups - so authors are no longer misled by a flat list where\nevery status appears equal. Elements keeps page heading, description,\ndisplay fields and privacy controls. Form pages are unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Revert \"FEATURE : Simulate runtime visibility states in AppConfig preview\"\n\nThis reverts commit 252e016af959d9dd7ce07432e5d083d70fc3cc95.\n\n* Revert \"Revert \"FEATURE : Simulate runtime visibility states in AppConfig preview\"\"\n\nThis reverts commit 745d3e66ecf58a736bd41e5bab19df465566dbcc.\n\n* FEATURE : Default preview state with nav stepper for conditional states\n\nThe phone preview now opens in a Default state showing only elements\nwithout visibility conditions; a prev/next stepper above the frame walks\nthrough each condition-derived state (status + matching actions),\nmirroring how the device resolves visible expressions at runtime.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FEATURE : Inline status tag grouping and readable condition chips in preview\n\nPage properties stays a single list (no tab split): display elements,\nthen a Status tags group with a note that only one shows at runtime,\nthen the action buttons group. Under the preview state stepper, the\nactive state''s visible expression is rendered as human-readable chips\n(e.g. ''Shown when Is delivered = true AND Has redose for current cycle\n= false''), mirroring the Display Logic design language.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FEATURE : Show readable visibility conditions on page property rows\n\nEach conditional element row in page properties now renders its visible\nexpression as human-readable chips (Shown when Is delivered = true AND\n...), matching the Display Logic design language, so authors can see\nwhy an element is conditional without opening it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FEATURE : View tag state selector in status tags group\n\nAdds a ''View tag state'' dropdown inside the page properties status tags\ngroup; changing it switches the phone preview to that tag''s simulated\nstate. Preview state moved to the remoteConfig slice so the panel\nselector and the stepper above the frame stay in sync, resetting on\npage change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FEATURE : Preview state controlled only from page properties\n\nRemoves the state stepper and condition chips from above the phone\nframe - the View tag state selector in the status tags group is the\nsingle control; the preview just reflects the selected state.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FEATURE : Drop per-row condition chips in page properties\n\nThe View tag state selector is the single conditional-state surface;\nrows keep just their label, type tag and toggle.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FEATURE : Restore prev/next state stepper above the preview\n\nThe stepper stays in sync with the View tag state selector via the\nshared previewStateId; only the condition chips remain removed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FEATURE : Show selected tag state''s condition under View tag state\n\nWhen a tag state is chosen, its visible expression renders as readable\nchips (Shown when ... AND ...) directly below the selector.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FEATURE : Replace View tag state dropdown with selectable chips\n\nTag states render as clickable chips (Default + each status); the\nactive chip is filled and drives the shared preview state.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b28ef5a06871d59a0434a07cedca745addd3b0a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/git/trees/b28ef5a06871d59a0434a07cedca745addd3b0a7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/git/commits/d24acb0bcbefbbd2e608214b60295d0af12ff536","verification":{"payload":"tree b28ef5a06871d59a0434a07cedca745addd3b0a7\nparent 7bcb93671dbf9038bf5e94f505e376c845eadbd2\nauthor Naveen J <83631045+naveen-egov@users.noreply.github.com> 1788353269 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788353269 +0530\n\nFEATURE : Status tag grouping with simulated preview states in AppConfig v2 (#4274)\n\n* FEATURE : Simulate runtime visibility states in AppConfig preview\n\nThe mobile app decides element visibility with device-side expressions\n(fn:isDelivered(...) == true && ...), so the preview showed every status\ntag and action button stacked - a screen that never exists on device.\n\nAdds a Preview state switcher above the phone frame: scenarios are\nderived from the page''s own visible expressions, picking one fixes its\nfn-terms and every other conditional element is shown or hidden by\nlogical consistency. ''All states'' (default) keeps the full inventory,\nnow marked with a dashed outline so authors can tell which elements are\nruntime-conditional. The selected field is always rendered so it stays\neditable, and unparseable expressions are never hidden.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FEATURE : Group status tags and buttons under an Actions tab in page properties\n\nTemplate pages split page properties into Elements and Actions tabs.\nThe Actions tab groups the runtime-conditional items - status tags\n(with a note that only one shows at a time on the device) and action\nbuttons/popups - so authors are no longer misled by a flat list where\nevery status appears equal. Elements keeps page heading, description,\ndisplay fields and privacy controls. Form pages are unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Revert \"FEATURE : Simulate runtime visibility states in AppConfig preview\"\n\nThis reverts commit 252e016af959d9dd7ce07432e5d083d70fc3cc95.\n\n* Revert \"Revert \"FEATURE : Simulate runtime visibility states in AppConfig preview\"\"\n\nThis reverts commit 745d3e66ecf58a736bd41e5bab19df465566dbcc.\n\n* FEATURE : Default preview state with nav stepper for conditional states\n\nThe phone preview now opens in a Default state showing only elements\nwithout visibility conditions; a prev/next stepper above the frame walks\nthrough each condition-derived state (status + matching actions),\nmirroring how the device resolves visible expressions at runtime.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FEATURE : Inline status tag grouping and readable condition chips in preview\n\nPage properties stays a single list (no tab split): display elements,\nthen a Status tags group with a note that only one shows at runtime,\nthen the action buttons group. Under the preview state stepper, the\nactive state''s visible expression is rendered as human-readable chips\n(e.g. ''Shown when Is delivered = true AND Has redose for current cycle\n= false''), mirroring the Display Logic design language.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FEATURE : Show readable visibility conditions on page property rows\n\nEach conditional element row in page properties now renders its visible\nexpression as human-readable chips (Shown when Is delivered = true AND\n...), matching the Display Logic design language, so authors can see\nwhy an element is conditional without opening it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FEATURE : View tag state selector in status tags group\n\nAdds a ''View tag state'' dropdown inside the page properties status tags\ngroup; changing it switches the phone preview to that tag''s simulated\nstate. Preview state moved to the remoteConfig slice so the panel\nselector and the stepper above the frame stay in sync, resetting on\npage change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FEATURE : Preview state controlled only from page properties\n\nRemoves the state stepper and condition chips from above the phone\nframe - the View tag state selector in the status tags group is the\nsingle control; the preview just reflects the selected state.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FEATURE : Drop per-row condition chips in page properties\n\nThe View tag state selector is the single conditional-state surface;\nrows keep just their label, type tag and toggle.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FEATURE : Restore prev/next state stepper above the preview\n\nThe stepper stays in sync with the View tag state selector via the\nshared previewStateId; only the condition chips remain removed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FEATURE : Show selected tag state''s condition under View tag state\n\nWhen a tag state is chosen, its visible expression renders as readable\nchips (Shown when ... AND ...) directly below the selector.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FEATURE : Replace View tag state dropdown with selectable chips\n\nTag states render as clickable chips (Default + each status); the\nactive chip is filled and drives the shared preview state.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signatur