,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/854808a5cfb4dec1a3591a358fa42259efb63846"}],"sha":"5be3e6b4a64e36ac4aa3b42713de16ba739590f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/5be3e6b4a64e36ac4aa3b42713de16ba739590f9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83631045?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/naveen-egov","id":83631045,"login":"naveen-egov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNjMxMDQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/854808a5cfb4dec1a3591a358fa42259efb63846/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T04:52:01Z","email":"83631045+naveen-egov@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Naveen J"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T04:52:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Drawer: Buttons section, read-only Required handling, info card as a template element (#4379)\n\n* Group body/template buttons under a Buttons section in the page drawer\n\nHousehold Overview and the success screens carry their CTAs in the page body,\nso they rendered as ordinary rows in the Template elements list while other\npages show footer buttons under a dedicated \"Buttons\" section. Render button\nrows after the same subheader; the rows keep their combined-list index so the\nexisting card/field index math and toggle rules are unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Render a single Buttons section when button rows and footer labels coexist\n\nWhen body/template button rows already open a Buttons subheader, the footer\nlabel inputs join that section instead of opening a second identical heading.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Hide the Required toggle for read-only fields\n\nA read-only field (e.g. Refer Beneficiary -> Referred By, auto-filled with\nthe logged-in user) cannot be edited in the app, so a Required control is\nmeaningless; the drawer showed it permanently locked instead. Skip rendering\nit for readOnly fields.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Present the page-level info card as an element, matching body infoCards\n\nMark Closed Household models its info card as page-level conditions.infoCardText,\nwhich the drawer rendered as a bare textarea in the page-header block — while\nReferral pages show their infoCard body field as a Template element with an\nInfocard tag. Render the page-level info card in the elements area with the\nsame element styling and tag so both patterns look alike; the message stays\neditable in place.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Add a show/hide toggle to the page-level info card element\n\nParity with body infoCard elements: toggling off stashes the localisation\ncode in conditions.infoCardTextDisabled and nulls infoCardText (the only key\nthe app checks), toggling on restores it. The message textarea shows only\nwhile the card is on.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Drop the duplicated inner label on the info card element\n\nThe element row already carries the \"Info card\" title and Infocard tag; the\ntextarea rendered its own identical label beneath. Add a hideLabel prop to\nHeaderFieldWrapper and use it there.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Open Field properties when clicking the page-level info card element\n\nConsole-only interaction parity with body infoCard fields: clicking the\nelement selects a pseudo-field so the regular Field-properties view opens,\nwith only the message (description) editable — the title item is skipped\nsince the app hardcodes it. Message edits flow through the localisation\nslice exactly as before; the config and app payload shapes are untouched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Skip Required panel item wrapper for read-only fields to avoid empty card\n\nThe toggle case in RenderField already returns null for bindTo=required on\nread-only fields, but the drawer-toggle-field-container wrapper still\nrendered, leaving a blank grey card in the drawer (seen on Stock in Hand).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Swathi-eGov <137176788+Swathi-eGov@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"4b8dfb8e5b28088980664fbdb9578f2c1e53737c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/git/trees/4b8dfb8e5b28088980664fbdb9578f2c1e53737c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/git/commits/854808a5cfb4dec1a3591a358fa42259efb63846","verification":{"payload":"tree 4b8dfb8e5b28088980664fbdb9578f2c1e53737c\nparent 0d81b4f7c339b03fb6466c31871fb4dcd7ee243d\nauthor Naveen J <83631045+naveen-egov@users.noreply.github.com> 1788324721 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788324721 +0530\n\nDrawer: Buttons section, read-only Required handling, info card as a template element (#4379)\n\n* Group body/template buttons under a Buttons section in the page drawer\n\nHousehold Overview and the success screens carry their CTAs in the page body,\nso they rendered as ordinary rows in the Template elements list while other\npages show footer buttons under a dedicated \"Buttons\" section. Render button\nrows after the same subheader; the rows keep their combined-list index so the\nexisting card/field index math and toggle rules are unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Render a single Buttons section when button rows and footer labels coexist\n\nWhen body/template button rows already open a Buttons subheader, the footer\nlabel inputs join that section instead of opening a second identical heading.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Hide the Required toggle for read-only fields\n\nA read-only field (e.g. Refer Beneficiary -> Referred By, auto-filled with\nthe logged-in user) cannot be edited in the app, so a Required control is\nmeaningless; the drawer showed it permanently locked instead. Skip rendering\nit for readOnly fields.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Present the page-level info card as an element, matching body infoCards\n\nMark Closed Household models its info card as page-level conditions.infoCardText,\nwhich the drawer rendered as a bare textarea in the page-header block — while\nReferral pages show their infoCard body field as a Template element with an\nInfocard tag. Render the page-level info card in the elements area with the\nsame element styling and tag so both patterns look alike; the message stays\neditable in place.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Add a show/hide toggle to the page-level info card element\n\nParity with body infoCard elements: toggling off stashes the localisation\ncode in conditions.infoCardTextDisabled and nulls infoCardText (the only key\nthe app checks), toggling on restores it. The message textarea shows only\nwhile the card is on.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Drop the duplicated inner label on the info card element\n\nThe element row already carries the \"Info card\" title and Infocard tag; the\ntextarea rendered its own identical label beneath. Add a hideLabel prop to\nHeaderFieldWrapper and use it there.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Open Field properties when clicking the page-level info card element\n\nConsole-only interaction parity with body infoCard fields: clicking the\nelement selects a pseudo-field so the regular Field-properties view opens,\nwith only the message (description) editable — the title item is skipped\nsince the app hardcodes it. Message edits flow through the localisation\nslice exactly as before; the config and app payload shapes are untouched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Skip Required panel item wrapper for read-only fields to avoid empty card\n\nThe toggle case in RenderField already returns null for bindTo=required on\nread-only fields, but the drawer-toggle-field-container wrapper still\nrendered, leaving a blank grey card in the drawer (seen on Stock in Hand).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Swathi-eGov <137176788+Swathi-eGov@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJql6txCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEmQQABgqZv11rNNSHDLSH39mM/5r\nWmanI3GcvDF7XMMpWy6CFvaazGK5/gcQze47muO2oJOnLQdb/s4i9eu+LOD7KlEN\nhOYOeKgHDtxe1ZQd41SIKa3vM2BJ8d1jaw6yOhgFZRNmX2n/g6NvN+vaoyWIV3X6\nXwWc1I4gUn3SglCD50aV+sJnc1bunPQyyR6INJXH3slkq3LrAqzRR/F6UMfgjzkK\n1ZS01ZwPJUdjeUD6WYqZOhzUFVVp1I+7Ubmnbk2PIFvq9j85f9tpcTkRra8h4d6+\nbziXS6TMXH3brEuMeBmcv/Qde6Q1Ln+w6LJpRMN6mf68sIYWOspqscFu0TTdVwwg\njjEFFaEEsk4CXATtcHUUMRpUFy7Q+qOUDRiywaVUrbYys4O9VhznKzr2tKaFhdtY\n9eqf8WwGhJ20RCGq4Vu/7gjlwJ9htqpwqRP/lEtOnWvbg90JXSZCl1/q6zhM88bG\nDEDOaIOu8zg6M3lEcMiQLrpu2hF49w+hQMoMgPrS/YZwrhVJynvky0puQ3BnKIcw\nV1FqYvZKJvho9/ub8vcYwQXmVsKwOS8RZKfSozAs/6zwtDWPM+ytn15Y6RiiSg8o\nfqR1g5/e3YclXNitW2wTy3hTNOemxBEfpC07L6htn3hjfwNsFO+G+L8R+/ZnEzqI\nf3lYzzCBG5EcPB9P7prc\n=QbVw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T04:52:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"M