ptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/0d81b4f7c339b03fb6466c31871fb4dcd7ee243d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T04:48:14Z","email":"83631045+naveen-egov@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Naveen J"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T04:48:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Filter popup options: drop \"Add Label:\" prefix, list MDMS master options with show/hide toggles (#4378)\n\n* Drop the \"Add Label:\" prefix from popup option rows in the properties panel\n\nFilter-popup option rows read \"Add Label: Administered Successfully\" etc.;\nthe prefix is editor chrome, not part of the option name. Show just the\nlocalised option name; table columns keep their \"Column:\" prefix.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* List MDMS-driven popup options from the master, matching the preview\n\nFor fields with isMdms + schemaCode (e.g. the Search Households filter,\nHCM.SEARCH_HOUSEHOLD_FILTERS) the runtime and preview resolve options from\nthe MDMS master, but the panel rendered the config''s stale 2-entry enums.\nFetch the same master and list every active option; hide the per-option\ntoggles for these since the option set lives in a shared master, not the\ncampaign config. Label localisation stays editable per option.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Keep show/hide toggles for MDMS-driven popup options\n\nThe app renders the config enums filtered by isActive, so the per-option\ntoggle is a real feature. Merge the master option set with the existing\nenums (preserving label codes and isActive), list every option with its\ntoggle, and materialise the merged list back into enums so the app receives\nthe full set instead of the stale two-entry leftover.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Treat config enums as the per-campaign selection of MDMS popup options\n\nenums is the mapping the app actually renders (filtered by isActive); the\nmaster only defines the available pool. Panel: list every master option with\nits show/hide toggle, defaulting unmapped options to OFF so behaviour is\nunchanged until enabled. Preview: render the enums selection like the device\ndoes, falling back to the master list only when no selection exists yet.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Swathi-eGov <137176788+Swathi-eGov@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"1a179efb1857e02fb5b033ef10c807003eaf4b99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/git/trees/1a179efb1857e02fb5b033ef10c807003eaf4b99"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/git/commits/0d81b4f7c339b03fb6466c31871fb4dcd7ee243d","verification":{"payload":"tree 1a179efb1857e02fb5b033ef10c807003eaf4b99\nparent 6cf50809856fe5fed8701fb4a7e563675ad6d4d7\nauthor Naveen J <83631045+naveen-egov@users.noreply.github.com> 1788324494 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788324494 +0530\n\nFilter popup options: drop \"Add Label:\" prefix, list MDMS master options with show/hide toggles (#4378)\n\n* Drop the \"Add Label:\" prefix from popup option rows in the properties panel\n\nFilter-popup option rows read \"Add Label: Administered Successfully\" etc.;\nthe prefix is editor chrome, not part of the option name. Show just the\nlocalised option name; table columns keep their \"Column:\" prefix.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* List MDMS-driven popup options from the master, matching the preview\n\nFor fields with isMdms + schemaCode (e.g. the Search Households filter,\nHCM.SEARCH_HOUSEHOLD_FILTERS) the runtime and preview resolve options from\nthe MDMS master, but the panel rendered the config''s stale 2-entry enums.\nFetch the same master and list every active option; hide the per-option\ntoggles for these since the option set lives in a shared master, not the\ncampaign config. Label localisation stays editable per option.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Keep show/hide toggles for MDMS-driven popup options\n\nThe app renders the config enums filtered by isActive, so the per-option\ntoggle is a real feature. Merge the master option set with the existing\nenums (preserving label codes and isActive), list every option with its\ntoggle, and materialise the merged list back into enums so the app receives\nthe full set instead of the stale two-entry leftover.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Treat config enums as the per-campaign selection of MDMS popup options\n\nenums is the mapping the app actually renders (filtered by isActive); the\nmaster only defines the available pool. Panel: list every master option with\nits show/hide toggle, defaulting unmapped options to OFF so behaviour is\nunchanged until enabled. Preview: render the enums selection like the device\ndoes, falling back to the master list only when no selection exists yet.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Swathi-eGov <137176788+Swathi-eGov@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJql6qOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYfQQAKUZ3ORf8S+Rh49Q58nkAwHL\nCMqUDZ+IyQW/LUYevzFLzjjP03+538scT+jQxuBaKLAv+YBBoFmPGV3PS70vQ7Rl\nrM7yztLJ3tgVF5wRtE313ymgq3zXx62RCD+BEu7VDnBV2Mh4s1Iroz8ik3T/d3PO\nU2o+0tTtbimjnZxILIxQNlih08yy79dRs6vCu9xGAxQ965GeTAGcEf1uOZXMrgsG\nVf2rJLs/lu71bWmvzPHG0ZeukUMgOv6TDYX+Gub8qe6nvRRXwgkKsxaoo3+tPPp6\nyRwTrxZOOadfVzIK+sCh3k7TAqB3Z9leJbkx+F8KJZa7x4F3lij2nZQjriCCzF0k\nTABA4X5hD6eNgOBbgKEfnpM58jhwqU5nLcK7gOv63ZDXPySTAt++KiiVsx/MW0F2\nA9Y1g8f42igMiHDlWr9J5nyGCWxj07vIWk3qZbuAdcUdsyVvggcXhzRRNrRHTkmk\nrhgnxl1wRnZCUI71Ei66+lcV3nhRlmQJpvehWRpVC0wyOEPOWy+UQkwE7whtkiOC\nsA3gA7KwUZJlZ1WoAGeSsu3c9hymDgt+e8iaivuqyj9VDcyNePYZkUYXLkGlJoqz\nC4LxIbfxiiKNyTk2oUFlannt7f6dQ5M2L/O/R3rFFVaymOwrIEv1qJuFRe10aOms\n8M1OwKh+NyKjeP+TsJar\n=QASg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T04:48:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commit/0d81b4f7c339b03fb6466c31871fb4dcd7ee243d","node_id":"C_kwDOKSe0RtoAKDBkODFiNGY3YzMzOWIwM2ZiNjQ2NmMzMTg3MWZiNGRjZDdlZTI0M2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commit/6cf50809856fe5fed8701fb4a7e563675ad6d4d7","sha":"6cf50809856fe5fed8701fb4a7e563675ad6d4d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/6cf50809856fe5fed8701fb4a7e563675ad6d4d7"}],"sha":"0d81b4f7c339b03fb6466c31871fb4dcd7ee243d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/0d81b4f7c339b03fb6466c31871fb4dcd7ee243d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83631045?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/naveen-egov","id":83631045,"login":"naveen-egov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNjMxMDQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/6cf50809856fe5fed8701fb4a7e563675ad6d4d7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T04:44:05Z","email":"83631045+naveen-egov@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Naveen J"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T04:44:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix Edit Boundary reopening with stale or empty selection (#4376)\n\n* Re-apply boundary selection when session or draft data arrives late\n\nThe load effect only ran on [isFetching, campaignNumber], so a session entry\nhydrating after mount (or rewritten while navigating back through setup\nsteps) was never applied and Edit Boundary showed an empty selection.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Don''t let an empty session entry clobber seeded boundaries in update flow\n\nThe session-sync effect in UpdateBoundaryWrapper overwrote the selection on\nany boundaryType reference change, including entries with an empty\nselectedData (left behind by other setup steps or written by the save effect\nbefore CampaignData seeded), blanking the Update/Edit Boundary screen.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Always refetch campaign draft when seeding Edit Boundaries\n\nThe project-type search was cached with a 10-minute staleTime, so after\nsubmitting a boundary change (which clears the setup session) reopening Edit\nBoundaries re-seeded from the cached pre-submit draft and showed the old\nselection.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Seed boundary selection once to stop session write-back render loop\n\nThe parent recreates the session object on every save, so re-applying\nsession data whenever its reference changed looped seed → save → session\nchange → seed (Maximum update depth exceeded) and the boundary levels never\nrendered. Seed from draft or session exactly once; after that the user''s\nlocal edits own the state.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"07704fea0be7c4103d18f54c90b859856e44bfd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/git/trees/07704fea0be7c4103d18f54c90b859856e44bfd0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/git/commits/6cf50809856fe5fed8701fb4a7e563675ad6d4d7","verification":{"payload":"tree 07704fea0be7c4103d18f54c90b859856e44bfd0\nparent 48d2dc02271f3cf503ef4dde51084c0f600679ef\nauthor Naveen J <83631045+naveen-egov@users.noreply.github.com> 1788324245 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788324245 +0530\n\nFix Edit Boundary reopening with stale or empty selection (#4376)\n\n* Re-apply boundary selection when session or draft data arrives late\n\nThe load effect only ran on [isFetching, campaignNumber], so a session entry\nhydrating after mount (or rewritten while navigating back through setup\nsteps) was never applied and Edit Boundary showed an empty selection.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Don''t let an empty session entry clobber seeded boundaries in update flow\n\nThe session-sync effect in UpdateBoundaryWrapper overwrote the selection on\nany boundaryType reference change, including entries with an empty\nselectedData (left behind by other setup steps or written by the save effect\nbefore CampaignData seeded), blanking the Update/Edit Boundary screen.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Always refetch campaign draft when seeding Edit Boundaries\n\nThe project-type search was cached with a 10-minute staleTime, so after\nsubmitting a boundary change (which clears the setup session) reopening Edit\nBoundaries re-seeded from the cached pre-submit draft and showed the old\nselection.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Seed boundary selection once to stop session write-back render loop\n\nThe parent recreates the session object on every save, so re-applying\nsession data whenever its reference changed looped seed → save → session\nchange → seed (Maximum update depth exceeded) and the boundary levels never\nrendered. Seed from draft or session exactly once; after that the user''s\nlocal edits own the state.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJql6mVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJIgQAEC/MKzP/6iG53MeUwaLEvK4\n1PXdEKZAJZvSlf8B/iq6CaMYWk5OSwAIOP4f0YswKhQhvt1L8lQQVHPhaIZKNRz+\nmb0EzQZo9d5/IkdvJwfK4BmcBy+Tjm9Kol/fg6Y/AAa7Kv21sdWIec2VHTSwdqat\n76kyzj1svJGdfMb3DLF/CeUBLNEpmO88EYQ1bOqR2aPJXvfR2du2wiSdpW9gtg3G\nMqAwAoumKeckatGd8WroLrnnFyteRf/iD+peqqHVIJZDbkWpVFAwv01JXEJTG5Pa\nXMJ1//PZREWKiVPUd1mj3sRr4Z3eDtsCTG7TnrZhmXTJZMw6NeAoUW2j3GuwvjKd\n/Av3OfeMp/MT+i6NAONSy4Y1IhTR3I5gzXCzsD/tdO/VINC5l1v7x2Kda6RTl9DM\nQcLbKc4CZ4xhN9QHsJa7ejmIV5yXgMJl6ijoGZzE411Sp57TWWDqEi6XRPytT23j\nALT77D7NNoLqTNIP/EVMZBqSIFNK2AtqONlXI9G39ZlT3lmYOixzT4gG6XvwMmee\nkixYDTIOGk7ssahJQEas8PjjNbCPSe9HJmmbQ07vwRqx9Qwp3VxCxzfeCnLTHBw3\nqQOF2FJdWU8vWh64HhYKt5ZU/7kr9ZxcDeUPU91zDgUkIt2zwn1SwnbNYpF3sr2E\na1/Pmt9LQLlSV9pLcfJt\n=5y+1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T04:44:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flo