os/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/6e504647607d867f786c1b051b1dcb2d8471b498"}],"sha":"a44b8dae7aa6a89bfffd6c3dc9f5164197cbd22f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/a44b8dae7aa6a89bfffd6c3dc9f5164197cbd22f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83631045?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/naveen-egov","id":83631045,"login":"naveen-egov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNjMxMDQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/6e504647607d867f786c1b051b1dcb2d8471b498/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T16:02:40Z","email":"83631045+naveen-egov@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Naveen J"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T16:02:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Hcm appconfig textarea panel item (#4369)\n\n* Render textarea panel items in the field-properties drawer\n\nThe noResultCard supplemental panel item (\"Household not found\" description on\nthe search screens) is declared with fieldType \"textarea\", but RenderField''s\nswitch had no textarea case, so it fell through to `default: return null` —\nthe drawer showed an empty property box and the card''s description could not\nbe edited at all. The FieldTypeMappingConfig master maps the card to\nfieldType noResultCard correctly and the panel item was already merged in;\nonly the renderer was missing.\n\nRoute \"textarea\" through the existing text case, passing the fieldType to\nFieldV1, which already renders a TextArea for type=\"textarea\". Also include\ntextarea in the local-value seeding effect, which was gated to text/number —\nwithout that the new control rendered but came up blank instead of pre-filled\nwith the current localized description.\n\nVerified locally against the running console: the Description textarea now\nappears under Title for the Household-not-found card and edits persist via\nthe same localisation path as Title.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Centre the QR code in the app-config popup preview\n\nThe QR icon rendered left of centre in the actionPopup preview. QRView already\nset justifyContent:center, but the centring was scoped to the wrong box.\n\nEvery field in the preview is wrapped by renderTemplateComponent in\n.template-field-wrapper, and that class is `width:100%; display:flex` with the\ndefault justify-content:flex-start (campaign.scss). QRView''s container set no\nwidth, so as a flex item it took the default `flex: 0 1 auto` and shrank to fit\nits content — a narrow box pinned to the left edge. Its own justifyContent then\nonly centred the icon inside that narrow box, leaving the QR sitting left of\nthe popup''s centre line.\n\nGive the container an explicit width:100% so it fills the flex line and the\nexisting centring applies against the popup width. `flex: 1` would work too;\nwidth is preferred because it stays local to QRView and cannot affect other\ncomponents sharing the same wrapper.\n\nOther field types were unaffected because they either stretch naturally or have\nexplicit rules (e.g. .template-field-wrapper .digit-text-input-field in\nappConfiguration.scss). QRView was the one that set no width at all.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Skip computed {{fn:...}} label keys in labelPairList properties panel\n\nThe Transaction Details labelPairList config uses runtime-computed keys like\n{{fn:getSecondPagePartyLabel(...)}}; the Elements panel ran them through t()\nand printed the raw expression as the field label (issue #4262 pt 10). These\nlabels are resolved in the app at runtime and have no editable localisation,\nso skip rendering a LocalizationInput for them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Make popup description editable and render it in the popup preview\n\nPopup label fields in the field-properties drawer (PopupLabelField) display\nuseCustomT(code) and write edits via updateLocalizationEntry under that code.\nSeeded templates carry popupConfig.description as an empty string, and\nuseCustomT(\"\") short-circuits to \"\" — so the description input rendered but\nnever reflected a single keystroke, and edits were stored under the empty\ncode. The title only worked because it has a real localization code\n(e.g. INSUFFICIENT_STOCK_TITLE).\n\nTwo further problems surfaced while fixing it:\n\n- Typing straight against redux scrambled fast input (\"ererSelecdeet…\"):\n  each keystroke re-rendered the controlled input from the store before the\n  next key landed.\n- The phone preview never showed the description at all: NewLayoutRenderer\n  passed only alertMessage, which the DIGIT PopUp component ignores for\n  default-type popups; PopUp renders a separate `description` prop.\n\nFixes, verified against the running console (Filter popup on Search\nHouseholds and Insufficient stock popup on Delivery Summary):\n\n- On first edit of a label with no code, mint POPUP_<PATH>_<timestamp>\n  (same convention as NewDrawerFieldComposer), persist it into popupConfig\n  via updateSelectedField, and store the message under it. The minted code\n  stays stable across keystrokes via a ref.\n- Hold the input value in local state with an isEditingRef guard (the\n  composer''s localValue pattern) so typing is smooth; redux stays the\n  source of truth when not editing.\n- Pass description={t(popupConfig.description)} to the preview PopUp so the\n  description renders under the popup title and updates live while typing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Tighten label column on the Add new resource screen\n\nThe Resource name/type/variant labels sat in a fixed 19rem column while the\ntext is ~8rem, leaving a large gap between each label and its input. Reduce\nthe column to 10rem so inputs sit next to their labels.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Do not double-render the popup description for alert-type popups\n\nThe preview PopUp received both alertMessage and description. The DIGIT PopUp\ncomponent renders alertMessage inside its alert section when type=\"alert\",\nand it also renders the description prop for every popup type — so alert\npopups showed the description twice.\n\nPass description only for non-alert popups: alert popups keep alertMessage,\ndefault popups keep description, each rendering exactly once. Verified on the\nFilter popup (default type) in the running console.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Close the label-to-field gap in the Add Resource to Deliver popup\n\nBoth LabelFieldPairs in the popup stack the label above the field, but the\ncomponent class ships a horizontal-layout gap (spacer6), leaving ~2.5rem\nbetween \"Resources to be delivered\"/\"Count\" and their inputs. Override with\nthe vertical-layout gap (0.5rem, spacer2).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"af0fc41db9eb2d46b3dc38b3e2b8c10935397ae8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/git/trees/af0fc41db9eb2d46b3dc38b3e2b8c10935397ae8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/git/commits/6e504647607d867f786c1b051b1dcb2d8471b498","verification":{"payload":"tree af0fc41db9eb2d46b3dc38b3e2b8c10935397ae8\nparent 201bee02d17ec183ea110dabf343534f28624357\nauthor Naveen J <83631045+naveen-egov@users.noreply.github.com> 1788192160 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788192160 +0530\n\nHcm appconfig textarea panel item (#4369)\n\n* Render textarea panel items in the field-properties drawer\n\nThe noResultCard supplemental panel item (\"Household not found\" description on\nthe search screens) is declared with fieldType \"textarea\", but RenderField''s\nswitch had no textarea case, so it fell through to `default: return null` —\nthe drawer showed an empty property box and the card''s description could not\nbe edited at all. The FieldTypeMappingConfig master maps the card to\nfieldType noResultCard correctly and the panel item was already merged in;\nonly the renderer was missing.\n\nRoute \"textarea\" through the existing text case, passing the fieldType to\nFieldV1, which already renders a TextArea for type=\"textarea\". Also include\ntextarea in the local-value seeding effect, which was gated to text/number —\nwithout that the new control rendered but came up blank instead of pre-filled\nwith the current localized description.\n\nVerified locally against the running console: the Description textarea now\nappears under Title for the Household-not-found card and edits persist via\nthe same localisation path as Title.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Centre the QR code in the app-config popup preview\n\nThe QR icon rendered left of centre in the actionPopup preview. QRView already\nset justifyContent:center, but the centring was scoped to the wrong box.\n\nEvery field in the preview is wrapped by renderTemplateComponent in\n.template-field-wrapper, and that class is `width:100%; display:flex` with the\ndefault justify-content:flex-start (campaign.scss). QRView''s container set no\nwidth, so as a flex item it took the default `flex: 0 1 auto` and shrank to fit\nits content — a narrow box pinned to the left edge. Its own justifyContent then\nonly centred the icon inside that narrow box, leaving the QR sitting left of\nthe popup''s centre line.\n\nGive the container an explicit width:100% so it fills the flex line and the\nexisting centring applies against the popup width. `flex: 1` would work too;\nwidth is preferred because it stays local to QRView and cannot affect other\ncomponents sharing the same wrapper.\n\nOther field types were unaffected because they either stretch naturally or have\nexplicit rules (e.g. .template-field-wrapper .digit-text-input-field in\nappConfiguration.scss). QRView was the one that set no width at all.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Skip computed {{fn:...}} label keys in labelPairList properties panel\n\nThe Transaction Details labelPairList config uses runtime-computed keys like\n{{fn:getSecondPagePartyLabel(...)}}; the Elements panel ran them through t()\nand printed the raw expression as the field label (issue #4262 pt 10). These\nlabels are resolved in the app at runtime and have no editable localisation,\nso skip rendering a LocalizationInput for them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Make popup description editable and render it in the popup preview\n\nPopup label fields in the field-properties drawer (PopupLabelField) display\nuseCustomT(code) and write edits via updateLocalizationEntry under that code.\nSeeded templates carry popupConfig.description as an empty string, and\nuseCustomT(\"\") short-circuits to \"\" — so the description input rendered but\nnever reflected a single keystroke, and edits were stored under the empty\ncode. The title only worked because it has a real localization code\n(e.g. INSUFFICIENT_STOCK_TITLE).\n\nTwo further problems surfaced while fixing it:\n\n- Typing straight against redux scrambled fast input (\"ererSelecdeet…\"):\n  each keystroke re-rendered the controlled input from the store before the\n  next key landed.\n- The phone preview never showed the description at all: NewLayoutRenderer\n  passed only alertMessage, which the DIGIT PopUp component ignores for\n  default-type popups; PopUp renders a separate `description` prop.\n\nFixes, verified against the running console (Filter popup on Search\nHouseholds and Insufficient stock popup on Delivery Summary):\n\n- On first edit of a label with no code, mint POPUP_<PATH>_<timestamp>\n  (same convention as NewDrawerFieldComposer), persist it into popupConfig\n  via updateSelectedField, and store the message under it. The minted code\n  stays stable across keystrokes via a ref.\n- Hold the input value in local state with an isEditingRef guard (the\n  composer''s localValue pattern) so typing is smooth; redux stays the\n  source of truth when not editing.\n- Pass description={t(popupConfig.description)} to the preview PopUp so the\n  description renders under the popup title and updates live while typing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Tighten label column on the Add new resource screen\n\nThe Resource name/type/variant labels sat in a fixed 19rem column while the\ntext is ~8rem, leaving a large gap between each label and its input. Reduce\nthe column to 10rem so inputs sit next to their labels.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n* Do not double-render the popup description for alert-type popups\n\nThe preview PopUp received both alertMessage and description. The DIGIT PopUp\ncomponent renders alertMessage inside its alert section when type=\"alert\",\nand it also renders the description prop for every popup type — so alert\npopups showed the description twice.\n\nPass description only for non-alert popups: alert popups keep alertMessage,\ndefault popups keep description, each rendering exactly once. Verified on the\nFilter popup (default type) in the running console.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Close the label-to-field gap in the Add Resource to Deliver popup\n\nBoth LabelFieldPairs in the popup stack the label above the field, but the\ncomponent class ships a horizontal-layout gap (spacer6), leaving ~2.5rem\nbetween \"Resources to be delivered\"/\"Count\" and their inputs. Override with\nthe vertical-layout gap (0.5rem, spacer2).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlaWgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARBcQAIeD6xdFjpfApb2/NXrNNloQ\nx+2q21pDADhL7nXKI5//lmUMUV8LKsQUq4AJ7PUhswoWQLJOjcJPmXZeeekfd3Cj\n8/JQlXESuWHtOQ9bk/qlocypDV47lwq0hDztR7UUmLSNHORhV7Vr+Hwp+mcMzuDl\nVUZN8XF+vCF1zJLM3oOZOSxLteVTYfPYusgTqO1lLChb1wPEbVzpcv5V7P5MG56T\nmCGl9AAd7Yfh/lEehvkAs2YgaZ9C5f0bdisMtvjsI0rQAHmTdI1qgz0s0F4MBUCb\n0i94bCg+hfjMV6gekLZILBrgnnWZFtgVrEjiinMvoYlsEaAhH69qq50DZIfY60Cc\nTc0fDkI0otv252WRy7lMFzdwGyMqFrHCDR0JUtX5drWBWKa+rbn354ThZ9JaxjT3\nFiNMco2gJpM3ney+3lgahLxRDZXzSVZ5+9CKLSZk+ldgIhjwM0E5uY06oHzVH+ro\n