ew was the one that set no width at all.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e1cffc52a52a85c974faef866880ed4d49d9429f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/git/trees/e1cffc52a52a85c974faef866880ed4d49d9429f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/git/commits/7d10524c755866ddd3a22da767ad4e42c4c2b285","verification":{"payload":"tree e1cffc52a52a85c974faef866880ed4d49d9429f\nparent 7538689cafe7752d59c987a44819ccbc0712a57f\nauthor Naveen J <83631045+naveen-egov@users.noreply.github.com> 1788182692 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788182692 +0530\n\nCentre the QR code in the app-config popup preview (#4361)\n\nThe QR icon rendered left of centre in the actionPopup preview. QRView already\nset justifyContent:center, but the centring was scoped to the wrong box.\n\nEvery field in the preview is wrapped by renderTemplateComponent in\n.template-field-wrapper, and that class is `width:100%; display:flex` with the\ndefault justify-content:flex-start (campaign.scss). QRView''s container set no\nwidth, so as a flex item it took the default `flex: 0 1 auto` and shrank to fit\nits content — a narrow box pinned to the left edge. Its own justifyContent then\nonly centred the icon inside that narrow box, leaving the QR sitting left of\nthe popup''s centre line.\n\nGive the container an explicit width:100% so it fills the flex line and the\nexisting centring applies against the popup width. `flex: 1` would work too;\nwidth is preferred because it stays local to QRView and cannot affect other\ncomponents sharing the same wrapper.\n\nOther field types were unaffected because they either stretch naturally or have\nexplicit rules (e.g. .template-field-wrapper .digit-text-input-field in\nappConfiguration.scss). QRView was the one that set no width at all.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlYCkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAT5QQAJIplCgdQLJffdIdJ+x2FYzG\nX/Ak6/yUpi+/p4YbqVDGXvMfkOg4G48qo9dUEgPKOeEJtQy28MLztmhejEDuJxFb\nOrwNbyCzbcZ9hSCigE05XxQpIxwmwkl6UTiQjIHL+6dw38lBRr0iSgnIKLRGW5iI\nzwNV/fQl0LablTYMryy/4n6WZw84d+2eBJdm9jwCldpz3GKPWS+J6QjcRK8y8qfi\nChDDDfqpUKwwnhPpsZOmWrusGFU2g/pJMCw8mscT97j0q5MeuSYiyQT9QJ5Qkqp5\nqwDdyBnm3S3zBssAPvGRq6WMGXvHZC0/mlb0iggIFM71UN4DVtCGutyccjpQyN9A\nzvfiQHr002nhnnDSNAFm10ThXEEEEcAFNKw3wpUPal3HSC91M7O6uWc4tz5NDQpH\nYe6Cg9vzBfCo/86a8gWzXF81BGJ8n6QOrY3kjYhJXMOK5kZsMiGXt9xJxgyajA8R\nqSDRB3STZMhIwZWokIeEs7+SLkhFPpYw6q3ZToh86G5oRPbJoohIVX26rrzDgfDI\n12Nh8EooejMY0nD0aUMLr8w4jopaCC4DfCB7bd+aRPYLHo52Fz5FKpvfEMt1d0SV\nE8ueeQbXVFUTgSBeqFruMgoEugtnDFuGWnDDFgegT0520TvLipZ37OFF42wjcPto\nrfNVoNkrNCadSc2ADYq3\n=G+ex\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T13:24:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commit/7d10524c755866ddd3a22da767ad4e42c4c2b285","node_id":"C_kwDOKSe0RtoAKDdkMTA1MjRjNzU1ODY2ZGRkM2EyMmRhNzY3YWQ0ZTQyYzRjMmIyODU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commit/7538689cafe7752d59c987a44819ccbc0712a57f","sha":"7538689cafe7752d59c987a44819ccbc0712a57f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/7538689cafe7752d59c987a44819ccbc0712a57f"}],"sha":"7d10524c755866ddd3a22da767ad4e42c4c2b285","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/7d10524c755866ddd3a22da767ad4e42c4c2b285"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83631045?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/naveen-egov","id":83631045,"login":"naveen-egov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNjMxMDQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/7538689cafe7752d59c987a44819ccbc0712a57f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T13:15:03Z","email":"83631045+naveen-egov@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Naveen J"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T13:15:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Render textarea panel items in the field-properties drawer (#4363)\n\nThe noResultCard supplemental panel item (\"Household not found\" description on\nthe search screens) is declared with fieldType \"textarea\", but RenderField''s\nswitch had no textarea case, so it fell through to `default: return null` —\nthe drawer showed an empty property box and the card''s description could not\nbe edited at all. The FieldTypeMappingConfig master maps the card to\nfieldType noResultCard correctly and the panel item was already merged in;\nonly the renderer was missing.\n\nRoute \"textarea\" through the existing text case, passing the fieldType to\nFieldV1, which already renders a TextArea for type=\"textarea\". Also include\ntextarea in the local-value seeding effect, which was gated to text/number —\nwithout that the new control rendered but came up blank instead of pre-filled\nwith the current localized description.\n\nVerified locally against the running console: the Description textarea now\nappears under Title for the Household-not-found card and edits persist via\nthe same localisation path as Title.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6b85c91bab109c5929b30011a0108775d47e8e12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/git/trees/6b85c91bab109c5929b30011a0108775d47e8e12"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/git/commits/7538689cafe7752d59c987a44819ccbc0712a57f","verification":{"payload":"tree 6b85c91bab109c5929b30011a0108775d47e8e12\nparent 799023e65eee4f650bbf316f3b56efc022e6c1f8\nauthor Naveen J <83631045+naveen-egov@users.noreply.github.com> 1788182103 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788182103 +0530\n\nRender textarea panel items in the field-properties drawer (#4363)\n\nThe noResultCard supplemental panel item (\"Household not found\" description on\nthe search screens) is declared with fieldType \"textarea\", but RenderField''s\nswitch had no textarea case, so it fell through to `default: return null` —\nthe drawer showed an empty property box and the card''s description could not\nbe edited at all. The FieldTypeMappingConfig master maps the card to\nfieldType noResultCard correctly and the panel item was already merged in;\nonly the renderer was missing.\n\nRoute \"textarea\" through the existing text case, passing the fieldType to\nFieldV1, which already renders a TextArea for type=\"textarea\". Also include\ntextarea in the local-value seeding effect, which was gated to text/number —\nwithout that the new control rendered but came up blank instead of pre-filled\nwith the current localized description.\n\nVerified locally against the running console: the Description textarea now\nappears under Title for the Household-not-found card and edits persist via\nthe same localisation path as Title.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlX5XCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAActYQAEtnDG/DAHRtR80eHs0Z27ZF\nXx4m+ntQt3ojK4N9quYd+rXUvdxGEUvhx/fiWqAbyhCQe2iw1DJjKY6bSHwFt1DK\nagd/a4brZq848PoV0Rzx1/okjEhlOqWgKAlusBPZtgijHVh4SM5+PK/D5UlnX/xo\ncTv741RiBzP+/xJxw4yFjrvMT9xnT7fP8BN4DGFpDK6lkOIAhQsR5uFFFaqRueJX\nqjXLr7SnUKKDLK0SdqUdghjacZHZ3hXOmexUrxisGWHCxe1uHKGPxLZKCkezalZv\n6Kyb5u5/Qoh/0Kp/RQFvEy57IELDYjtiYkEBOxFHEbREigVug5ZVQ5herIs82WHh\noxZc0abZr/QPiylFglqggJH52Z6WmbjywrdaPs2mO9yBDswkKcVYDV+yMznN48B/\nPb+H03eo7TB2KZcO0p5HpdbJl/EZXPtFmeSxifxa3P4u3YqPycqvpxydvwCjyh+f\nfbLQBNsP0gx4HvIVNdBV5k3ielaY7uh5mbM8UpFlInDngYQwgADKD30ZWwEtR13M\nXAx+cDQKhhUYj5jMffWUHdqXcBJdZk3KlJkan49hDYU521a3Qxa6JGvC8NuXF4cr\noD1oTAUKdkgqgculPDOf6o7gQQrfYqtAUF2NE1nKUUuGjeEq7/iqZIWVKNY4AbgB\nImBxdBBCPDSM+CpZefO0\n=enMO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T13:15:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commit/7538689cafe7752d59c987a44819ccbc0712a57f","node_id":"C_kwDOKSe0RtoAKDc1Mzg2ODljYWZlNzc1MmQ1OWM5ODdhNDQ4MTljY2JjMDcxMmE1N2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commit/799023e65eee4f650bbf316f3b56efc022e6c1f8","sha":"799023e65eee4f650bbf316f3b56efc022e6c1f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/799023e65eee4f650bbf316f3b56efc022e6c1f8"}],"sha":"7538689cafe7752d59c987a44819ccbc0712a57f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/7538689cafe7752d59c987a44819ccbc0712a57f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83631045?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/naveen-egov","id":83631045,"login":"naveen-egov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNjMxMDQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/799023e65eee4f650bbf316f3b56efc022e6c1f8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T13:14:35Z","email":"83631045+naveen-egov@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Naveen J"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T13:14:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Show the selected campaign on an attendance register, not the first assigned one (#4362)\n\nThe register view and edit screens read `staffProjects` from session storage —\nthe full list of every project the logged-in user is assigned to, written once\nat login — and then rendered index [0] unconditionally. Users assigned to a\nsingle project never noticed. Supervisors (proximity supervisor in particular)\nare assigned to several, so opening any register showed whichever campaign\nhappened to sort first rather than the one the register belongs to.\n\nThe register search itself was already correct: it filters on\n`referenceId: selectedProject?.id`, so the right registers were listed. Only\nthe header labels were wrong, which is why the list looked fine while the\ndetail page misreported its campaign.\n\nResolve the project from `selectedProject` (what the user picked, and what the\nregister search filters on), falling back to the first entry only when nothing\nis selected.\n\nAlso fixes the worker-rates lookup, which used the same index-[0] value as\n`referenceCampaignId` to filter `WORKER_RATES` by `campaignId`. That one is not\ncosmetic: for a multi-project user it could select another campaign''s rates.\n\nAffected: ViewAttendance.js campaign name, project type and worker-rates\nlookup; EditRegister.js campaign name, project type, and campaign start/end\ndates.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"af951a83619aaa80dda6b3142f5926a06b0d6408","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/git/trees/af951a83619aaa80dda6b3142f5926a06b0d6408"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/git/commits/799023e65eee4f650bbf316f3b56efc022e6c1f8","verification":{"payload":"tree af951a83619aaa80dda6b3142f5926a06b0d6408\nparent 789d474884e58ed724e732b030d1a7a594202055\nauthor Naveen J <83631045+naveen-egov@users.noreply.github.com> 1788182075 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788182075 +0530\n\nShow the selected campaign on an attendance register, not the first assigned one (#4362)\n\nThe register view and edit screens read `staffProjects` from session storage —\nthe full list of every project the logged-in user is assigned to, written once\nat login — and then rendered index [0] unconditionally. Users assigned to a\nsingle project never noticed. Supervisors (proximity supervisor in particular)\nare assigned to several, so opening any register showed whichever campaign\nhappened to sort first rather than the one the register belongs to.\n\nThe register search itself was already correct: it filters on\n`referenceId: selectedProject?.id`, so the right registers were listed. Only\nthe header labels were wrong, which is why the list looked fine while the\ndetail page misreported its campaign.\n\nResolve the project from `selectedProject` (what the user picked, and what the\nregister search filters on), falling back to the first entry only when nothing\nis selected.\n\nAlso fixes the worker-rates lookup, which used the same index-[0] value as\n`referenceCampaignId` to filter `WORKER_RATES` by `campaignId`. That one is not\ncosmetic: for a multi-project user it could select another campaign''s rates.\n\nAffected: ViewAttendance.js campaign name, project type and worker-rates\nlookup; EditRegister.js campaign name, project type, and campaign start/end\ndates.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlX47CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5DsQABIp+BSpnlO7pkee4ekbqg8n\nrzFOaBPTQDMAo5XPiCeG3JqqPvXfxYorABxbRfUrpNXrLEDK18VXb4xeM/EXpOwB\nGcs+NmuPAZ66K5y0j9MaME8175XBO7lJLTgJj/KTrriJ3iXnoRQwagaEs+T4ySLK\n9okf56JHpnDH2PhgA6E57MIUY3HB0enVKnxPkA1HLaSkgEc0/hDcbACNzprmT7cE\ncLxrefoTwfwO3QI8LQm49cBGzC65OrcY9Qa9NefI4hDkw5X0qG5IMRbK5WlZCfG/\nv+sZzivOm1/mGQYOiyeds35jMSYX/gGZNZfChvzq/8PrU3en4bXlasS2aHZWGOP+\n+pRlcjrVS8Vrty5RsIo9y8lSbU0jTZOPtxw6pVfcpsP/wGRU6QmUVisEP4yESYw3\nqUnufghnOScSgDZfvYI7FwrUR/31cd5aVzQ1w5Mbq1cwt4lrPrIitDwPOTD5PDt/\nf3v/SiLFI2aHioTclanEP9uB6uUY0w29tJvOL79zr4pEKT9NmmlrsY46crquS78L\noPabWzfmqQqZ/xKWFe8F9L8BngV+vh1f7UMKkRYLvDtJ2IU5ljlMPEyxiTAwvKet\nKjqr7WmWsN4v6pPYQ0XiplB5wv9ulCaENiXqDJ4tNFSwBA/aMVcKUKucKV3xYzy/\niTLRTYbjJ0zBZEIUkOTA\n=XSuD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T13:14:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/