Se0RtoAKGE3ZmI5YWQzZGU1M2U5NDYzMzMxYWQxMDlhNTYwZWFhNTE2ZDRiMjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commit/a2999363f3adb639e2330f2f66ea86fd63372177","sha":"a2999363f3adb639e2330f2f66ea86fd63372177","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/a2999363f3adb639e2330f2f66ea86fd63372177"}],"sha":"a7fb9ad3de53e9463331ad109a560eaa516d4b21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/a7fb9ad3de53e9463331ad109a560eaa516d4b21"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83631045?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/naveen-egov","id":83631045,"login":"naveen-egov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNjMxMDQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/a2999363f3adb639e2330f2f66ea86fd63372177/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T05:55:10Z","email":"83631045+naveen-egov@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Naveen J"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T05:55:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Show the selected campaign on an attendance register, not the first a… (#4354)\n\nShow the selected campaign on an attendance register, not the first assigned one\n\nThe register view and edit screens read `staffProjects` from session storage —\nthe full list of every project the logged-in user is assigned to, written once\nat login — and then rendered index [0] unconditionally. Users assigned to a\nsingle project never noticed. Supervisors (proximity supervisor in particular)\nare assigned to several, so opening any register showed whichever campaign\nhappened to sort first rather than the one the register belongs to.\n\nThe register search itself was already correct: it filters on\n`referenceId: selectedProject?.id`, so the right registers were listed. Only\nthe header labels were wrong, which is why the list looked fine while the\ndetail page misreported its campaign.\n\nResolve the project from `selectedProject` (what the user picked, and what the\nregister search filters on), falling back to the first entry only when nothing\nis selected.\n\nAlso fixes the worker-rates lookup, which used the same index-[0] value as\n`referenceCampaignId` to filter `WORKER_RATES` by `campaignId`. That one is not\ncosmetic: for a multi-project user it could select another campaign''s rates.\n\nAffected: ViewAttendance.js campaign name, project type and worker-rates\nlookup; EditRegister.js campaign name, project type, and campaign start/end\ndates.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Swathi-eGov <137176788+Swathi-eGov@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"713da7acb0c2161b210137250a3fb95f9217d81e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/git/trees/713da7acb0c2161b210137250a3fb95f9217d81e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/git/commits/a2999363f3adb639e2330f2f66ea86fd63372177","verification":{"payload":"tree 713da7acb0c2161b210137250a3fb95f9217d81e\nparent 3034947a7b2f045e2994a8d17d987258dd2eccac\nauthor Naveen J <83631045+naveen-egov@users.noreply.github.com> 1788155710 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788155710 +0530\n\nShow the selected campaign on an attendance register, not the first a… (#4354)\n\nShow the selected campaign on an attendance register, not the first assigned one\n\nThe register view and edit screens read `staffProjects` from session storage —\nthe full list of every project the logged-in user is assigned to, written once\nat login — and then rendered index [0] unconditionally. Users assigned to a\nsingle project never noticed. Supervisors (proximity supervisor in particular)\nare assigned to several, so opening any register showed whichever campaign\nhappened to sort first rather than the one the register belongs to.\n\nThe register search itself was already correct: it filters on\n`referenceId: selectedProject?.id`, so the right registers were listed. Only\nthe header labels were wrong, which is why the list looked fine while the\ndetail page misreported its campaign.\n\nResolve the project from `selectedProject` (what the user picked, and what the\nregister search filters on), falling back to the first entry only when nothing\nis selected.\n\nAlso fixes the worker-rates lookup, which used the same index-[0] value as\n`referenceCampaignId` to filter `WORKER_RATES` by `campaignId`. That one is not\ncosmetic: for a multi-project user it could select another campaign''s rates.\n\nAffected: ViewAttendance.js campaign name, project type and worker-rates\nlookup; EditRegister.js campaign name, project type, and campaign start/end\ndates.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015btqYRAL5QdStuMe3E47dp\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Swathi-eGov <137176788+Swathi-eGov@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlRc+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAauEQAJ1ljghV/ABOwTW+ZICcxzOO\nOtX2QNnt/GM8oiAsSPJ+UJuxMKZS3/b+81fFTKAen1d06PwiMPPKJaCDGokJfstm\nSShdyr9tmdWW