api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/naveen-egov","id":83631045,"login":"naveen-egov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNjMxMDQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/63a4e33a410d269e0f18bf65bfb88f8b1cd815e0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T08:10:09Z","email":"83631045+naveen-egov@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Naveen J"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T08:10:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"FIX/HCMPRE-0000 : ITN review UI batch (empty-state textarea, description cap, status tags, card alignment) (#4340)\n\n* FIX : ITN review UI batch - empty-state textarea, 64-char description cap, status tags, card row alignment\n\n- noResultCard description edits in a textarea instead of a single-line input\n- Page description capped at 64 chars consistently across pages (was 30 default)\n- TagTemplate rendered tags with a white background and no stroke so delivery\n  statuses read as plain text; now renders real tag pills (variant bg + stroke)\n- RowTemplate defaulted alignItems:center, floating lone items (Transaction type,\n  View QR) mid-height beside stacked label pairs in transaction cards; default is\n  now flex-start (identical rendering for equal-height rows)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FIX : ITN review bug batch - localisation upload dedupe, success-screen history, microplan template popup\n\n- Localisation upload: the service rejects a request containing the same code\n  twice (DUPLICATE_RECORDS), so one repeated sheet row failed the entire upload\n  every attempt; dedupe by code+module+locale (bottom-most row wins) and settle\n  per-module so a single failing module is reported by name instead of a\n  generic failure\n- Success screens: browser Back could land on completed flows'' success states;\n  Response now replaces itself in history on exit, and checklist create/update\n  navigate to it with replace:true\n- Microplan campaigns (parentId): the download-template popup defaulted open and\n  auto-showed on ''edit data'' entry even though microplan data is prefilled and\n  there is no template step; popup now starts closed and never auto-opens when\n  parentId is present\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FIX : Bednet cycles - hide start/end date pickers, prefill from campaign dates\n\nBednet (ITN) is a single-round campaign so per-cycle dates should not be asked;\nthe cycle date section is hidden for bednet project types and cycle dates are\nauto-populated from the campaign start/end dates so validation and downstream\npayloads are unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f5767a9773505e4dffdde8afce19698d21d5d4a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/git/trees/f5767a9773505e4dffdde8afce19698d21d5d4a8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/git/commits/63a4e33a410d269e0f18bf65bfb88f8b1cd815e0","verification":{"payload":"tree f5767a9773505e4dffdde8afce19698d21d5d4a8\nparent 2f336a9f5683b7180d698b1a3f66a755f5fa9b96\nauthor Naveen J <83631045+naveen-egov@users.noreply.github.com> 1787818209 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787818209 +0530\n\nFIX/HCMPRE-0000 : ITN review UI batch (empty-state textarea, description cap, status tags, card alignment) (#4340)\n\n* FIX : ITN review UI batch - empty-state textarea, 64-char description cap, status tags, card row alignment\n\n- noResultCard description edits in a textarea instead of a single-line input\n- Page description capped at 64 chars consistently across pages (was 30 default)\n- TagTemplate rendered tags with a white background and no stroke so delivery\n  statuses read as plain text; now renders real tag pills (variant bg + stroke)\n- RowTemplate defaulted alignItems:center, floating lone items (Transaction type,\n  View QR) mid-height beside stacked label pairs in transaction cards; default is\n  now flex-start (identical rendering for equal-height rows)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FIX : ITN review bug batch - localisation upload dedupe, success-screen history, microplan template popup\n\n- Localisation upload: the service rejects a request containing the same code\n  twice (DUPLICATE_RECORDS), so one repeated sheet row failed the entire upload\n  every attempt; dedupe by code+module+locale (bottom-most row wins) and settle\n  per-module so a single failing module is reported by name instead of a\n  generic failure\n- Success screens: browser Back could land on completed flows'' success states;\n  Response now replaces itself in history on exit, and checklist create/update\n  navigate to it with replace:true\n- Microplan campaigns (parentId): the download-template popup defaulted open and\n  auto-showed on ''edit data'' entry even though microplan data is prefilled and\n  there is no template step; popup now starts closed and never auto-opens when\n  parentId is present\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FIX : Bednet cycles - hide start/end date pickers, prefill from campaign dates\n\nBednet (ITN) is a single-round campaign so per-cycle dates should not be asked;\nthe cycle date section is hidden for bednet project types and cycle dates are\nauto-populated from the campaign start/end dates so validation and downstream\npayloads are unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqj/DhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAch0QABOdQloD3zDR1YOxcoTOSsNj\nkpBuVj/FsgmYtZxmzs7Y4zXRZ7rC7LZTjg9PbJxR6Cq96WPAEoHX5lh1Qpp/YPs/\nhoaDjGfzonT0ThNvPKaYmyxsjfQbBnSeHPlZ5Of+utVDczsDPIwUheyYMapxmLar\n+oqNSv4u7Ptsn+Ol/cYZm2Vt1rbxBZX1Vi5W9xFwS4SIOXK+JELoQgad6LU4LpKF\ne2ecDae14aJ3u+11udv2YV9AYkJ+kgkrZ0cCtGu/aWDK3gP4pqcMBQz8LdxhGA3x\nYYaRium8cH61w0PZg85RtQD/bKSr+zolutiqjTCs5uqXCQKAUGYZpRm+0s4EqiuN\nuW9ZUojmvlt/33GIhC7oJnxYxq5gkl3NjYT0ZbzlCGXJcj4iQD2/55CvpbCEcgrV\nWs1byZV+VLqHHz6HJ1qI+S0g4oZKUqnP/2klq1d2kq9hDjZd/0wuji138JZFelfy\nnKEN7gRRlQahcLTME7MFO4biGnee2bihglfTSLoSfF6hSoSubRdxPVxefgKXh/WT\niF58N9g2iPBsQebjPTa7Sby+lbQZ0awIYwd8bG7SiYyaY8iyl05YXMndjUQjw2PD\nMucTwqPSabcfIGcmatYeMF0K/ffEB2PJxKTlpdOx91yFaL9nHJrdZFkdtV9ScgQM\ntDKOy8VuA0NlggvwhEFL\n=pKLP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-27T08:10:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commit/63a4e33a410d269e0f18bf65bfb88f8b1cd815e0","node_id":"C_kwDOKSe0RtoAKDYzYTRlMzNhNDEwZDI2OWUwZjE4YmY2NWJmYjg4ZjhiMWNkODE1ZTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commit/2f336a9f5683b7180d698b1a3f66a755f5fa9b96","sha":"2f336a9f5683b7180d698b1a3f66a755f5fa9b96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/2f336a9f5683b7180d698b1a3f66a755f5fa9b96"}],"sha":"63a4e33a410d269e0f18bf65bfb88f8b1cd815e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/63a4e33a410d269e0f18bf65bfb88f8b1cd815e0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83631045?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/naveen-egov","id":83631045,"login":"naveen-egov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNjMxMDQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/2f336a9f5683b7180d698b1a3f66a755f5fa9b96/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T09:42:11Z","email":"83631045+naveen-egov@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Naveen J"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T09:42:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"FIX/HCMPRE-0000 : Info card full width in template preview; uncategorized flows stay flat (#4336)\n\n* FIX : Info card full width in template preview; uncategorized flows stay flat in nav\n\n- InfoCardTemplate: AlertCard sized to content, leaving the View Transactions\n  empty-state card narrower than sibling cards - now spans full width\n- FullConfigWrapper: flows without a category render flat instead of under a raw\n  ''Uncategorized Category'' header (follow-up to the always-show-header change)\n- Copy: no-transactions description unified across base + campaign modules:\n  ''We couldn''t find any stock transactions to display. Once a transaction is\n  recorded, it will appear here.''\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* RELEASE : digit-ui-health-css 1.0.40 (header double-arrow fix); bump pinned CSS in build templates\n\n- 1.0.40 published to npm (console dist-tag) with the fallback-caret suppression\n  so headers don''t show two arrows when core renders its own dropdown arrow\n- index.html templates across builds updated 1.0.39 -> 1.0.40\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"aa4756e235ae3d93beb7e639f84a347c6e7cb308","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/git/trees/aa4756e235ae3d93beb7e639f84a347c6e7cb308"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/git/commits/2f336a9f5683b7180d698b1a3f66a755f5fa9b96","verification":{"payload":"tree aa4756e235ae3d93beb7e639f84a347c6e7cb308\nparent 1fe4c93c62ad7849132ef51de9d453d5c66b401a\nauthor Naveen J <83631045+naveen-egov@users.noreply.github.com> 1787737331 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787737331 +0530\n\nFIX/HCMPRE-0000 : Info card full width in template preview; uncategorized flows stay flat (#4336)\n\n* FIX : Info card full width in template preview; uncategorized flows stay flat in nav\n\n- InfoCardTemplate: AlertCard sized to content, leaving the View Transactions\n  empty-state card narrower than sibling cards - now spans full width\n- FullConfigWrapper: flows without a category render flat instead of under a raw\n  ''Uncategorized Category'' header (follow-up to the always-show-header change)\n- Copy: no-transactions description unified across base + campaign modules:\n  ''We couldn''t find any stock transactions to display. Once a transaction is\n  recorded, it will appear here.''\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* RELEASE : digit-ui-health-css 1.0.40 (header double-arrow fix); bump pinned CSS in build templates\n\n- 1.0.40 published to npm (console dist-tag) with the fallback-caret suppression\n  so headers don''t show two arrows when core renders its own dropdown arrow\n- index.html templates across builds updated 1.0.39 -> 1.0.40\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjrTzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7UgQAAheuYsYt6G3bcc3dUh6xVXU\nJ/eFYneT5xnzV3tnpCpjuDNJ0x9MneNKjLsuBBCQ9bym7lUNx8gnCACDJztou9jI\nnMaXUrfaE8nYTbj8jRMNMjBkmRChT8f8EIHZBfhZ+8IwjWdGlo1NcRfvwPXaNECz\nR6YtCUc+0MxlCbYQabUWI6Vze2R0YWyNU4E3cvwSnCoZrWCqr+v5R9YYPveEbBrj\nnwGyRxn53H7Os2wD84gjtD2G62sh++x0fg43EylvytqZzDqZmmY3mIr5HngUX5Ud\nQADWFlM3NEf0lU4ofcrisVDQvWJL4LbslZ7FF1BSCuxML2eJqb0YHPBroQ9AJ37P\nOzI3Xvu+5+5jqxnF06/2tIeildPvThhPLZR2X7VDnIuHUaI9CQM0pMIDVouXaxpf\nBLH3OywYpDAlGr6Jzn40tgYLdj2e0yUgI+j3+sg5fp4DKX3l9mBHvp7yV/sZOlKC\n08eGt+f8OzJgPJWcLePfNmsYNyMEc7S7H2nhrM5mprsTMn7aAsqeleENKEEJwaTy\ndo0rJu7bD1mS9pqb4NkbqRBp/rQeDaL+Gp1XsBHc3ZGUprDfTelSQeQ59YviDSim\nupwJWm1rSSrpSd//tRfuuvMC68cmRCyznk/8vGMeArQ/DsUPjWlrZ/9T3noLsG3R\n3UPzWkgXpkl9Eo8kNSvR\n=Yybv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T09:42:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commit/2f336a9f5683b7180d698b1a3f66a755f5fa9b96","node_id":"C_kwDOKSe0RtoAKDJmMzM2YTlmNTY4M2I3MTgwZDY5OGIxYTNmNjZhNzU1ZjVmYTliOTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commit/1fe4c93c62ad7849132ef51de9d453d5c66b401a","sha":"1fe4c93c62ad7849132ef51de9d453d5c66b401a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/1fe4c93c62ad7849132ef51de9d453d5c66b401a"}],"sha":"2f336a9f5683b7180d698b1a3f66a755f5fa9b96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/2f336a9f5683b7180d698b1a3f66a755f5fa9b96"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83631045?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/naveen-egov","id":83631045,"login":"naveen-egov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNjMxMDQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/1fe4c93c62ad7849132ef51de9d453d5c66b401a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T07:28:36Z","email":"83631045+naveen-egov@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Naveen J"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T07:28:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"FIX/HCMPRE-0000 : Design-system audit follow-up (tokens, layout, content standards) (#4334)\n\n* FIX : Error heading token and employeeCard disabled variant\n\nModule audits surfaced the app-config error heading using Material red\n#d32f2f (now error token #B91900) and the inventory Warehouse Details\npage''s disabled input hint using library #9E9E9E (now disabled token\n#C5C5C5 via the existing override group).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FIX : Token colors for campaign home badge and upload drag-drop area\n\nFull-sweep audit additions: campaign home count badge #F5F2F2 -> generic\nbg #EEEEEE, drag-drop hint text #b1b4b6 -> disabled token #C5C5C5, and\nthe upload container''s off-scale 5px radius -> 4px.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FIX : Hide campaign tag when no campaign name is available\n\nThe tag rendered as an empty pill above the Upload Microplan Data\nheading (and anywhere else the name is absent); skip rendering instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FIX : Keep upload-screen action buttons right-aligned without campaign tag\n\nThe header row uses space-between with [tag][buttons]; when the tag is\nhidden (no campaign name) the buttons jumped to the left. Anchor the\nbutton group with margin-left auto so alignment holds either way.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FIX : Anchor primary Search action to the right of the filter row\n\nThe library search bar renders [Search][Clear][Sort]; per the design\nsystem''s primary-action-right convention (footers, popups, wizards),\nreverse the row so Search sits right-most with Sort/Clear beside it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FIX : Pack search actions to the card''s right edge\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* DOCS : Design system audit report and content-audit localization changes\n\n- DESIGN_SYSTEM_AUDIT_REPORT.md: full audit scope, fixes, whitelists,\n  and upstream recommendations for DIGIT-UI-LIBRARIES.\n- localization-changes-2026-08-26-content-audit.json: the 97 en_DEMO\n  copy fixes applied on hcm-demo per the DIGIT content guidelines\n  (spelling, exclamation marks, double spaces, button Title Case,\n  heading sentence case), for replay on other environments.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* DOCS : Add Permission Handler casing fixes to the localization replay set\n\n29 entries (console modules, hcm-base-* templates, and the current\ncampaign) aligning the module/flow name to Title Case; the mixed casing\noriginated in the base templates themselves.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* DOCS : Add breadcrumb casing fix (VIEW_DETAILS) to localization replay set\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* DOCS : Breadcrumb audit fixes in localization replay set\n\n14 entries: 12 breadcrumbs normalized to sentence case, 2 missing\nbreadcrumb keys created (bulk stock upload, commodity campaigns) that\npreviously rendered as raw codes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* DOCS : Semantic label fixes in localization replay set\n\n- CREATE_CHECKLIST breadcrumb ''Configure'' -> ''Create checklist''\n- MAP_ATTENDEES breadcrumb ''Create register workers'' -> ''Map attendees''\n- ACTION_LABEL_VIEW_TIMELINE ''User credentials'' -> ''View Timeline''\n  (verified in UICustomizations.js: the action opens the campaign\n  timeline, so the credentials label was wrong)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* DOCS : Rewrite all ''Invalid ...'' error messages per content guidelines\n\n22 error messages rewritten to say what went wrong and what to do next,\nwithout the word ''invalid'' or user blame (e.g. ''Invalid file format.\nPlease upload .xlsx or .xls file'' -> ''This file type is not supported.\nUpload an .xlsx or .xls file.'').\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FIX : Restore Title Case for Upload Translations button\n\nThe heading sentence-case batch over-reached onto the button key\n(HCM_UPLOAD_LOCALIZATIONS_DATA_BUTTON); buttons take Title Case per the\ncontent guide. The heading key stays sentence case.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* DOCS : Privacy controls section heading to sentence case\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* DOCS : Page heading/description labels to sentence case\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* DOCS : Info card label to sentence case (both keys)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* DOCS : Editor field labels to sentence case (error message, custom logic, page header, navigation logic, current version)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FIX : Version tag reads ''(Version 1)'' instead of ''(AppConfig Version - 1)''\n\nUnify APPCONFIG_VERSION to ''Version'' across both console modules (it\nwas ''AppConfig Version'' in one and ''Current Version'' in the other) and\ndrop the hardcoded '' - '' separator in the title bar.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FIX : Field labels sentence-cased per DIGIT content standard (886 keys)\n\n- hcm-appconfiguration: 478 field/label-pair/component-name keys Title Case -> sentence case (buttons/CTAs untouched)\n- Campaign CMP-2026-08-25-004322 modules (inventory/registration/complaints): 408 field label keys\n- Scan-trigger labels (Team Code / Scan Delivery) kept Title Case since they render as buttons\n- Replay JSON captures final upserted values on hcm-demo\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FIX : Sentence-case field labels in all hcm-base-* template modules (6631 keys)\n\n- 49 base template modules (closehousehold/complaints/hfreferral/insidemonitoring/\n  inventory/lqa/permissionhandler/registration/stock/stockreconciliation/stockreports\n  x bednet/co-delivery/default/mr-dn/oncho/polio) swept on hcm-demo\n- Same rules as campaign fix: buttons/CTAs/headings/errors untouched, acronyms kept,\n  scan-trigger labels (Team Code / Scan Delivery) stay Title Case\n- New campaigns clone these templates, so future campaigns inherit correct casing\n- Existing campaigns keep their snapshots (per review decision: update base, not each campaign)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FIX : Cross-verify buttons against FormConfig templates; restore Title Case on 64 button keys\n\n- Walked all 71 HCM-ADMIN-CONSOLE.FormConfigTemplate records + campaign FormConfigs,\n  collected every code at button positions (footer, footerActions, primary/secondary\n  actions, scanner triggers) and verified resolved values are Title Case\n- Reverted 41 sweep-affected button keys (Save Filter, Clear Filter, Open Member Card,\n  Skip & Continue, Scan Child/Code, Close Out, View Stock Excess/Less Reports)\n- Fixed 10 more sweep-affected scanner/filter buttons (Delivery Team Code, Apply Filter)\n- Fixed 13 pre-existing violations (Back to Home, Create a New Transaction)\n- Re-verified: 0 button casing violations remain; 141 missing-key references are\n  pre-existing template gaps (INT-CAMP/IRS-mz/communityregistration/attendance)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FIX : Raw WAREHOUSE_MANAGER role code leaking into role-scoped field labels\n\n- Editor suffixes dropdownTemplate labels with t(role); DISTRIBUTOR resolved but\n  WAREHOUSE_MANAGER had no translation in hcm-base-inventory-default, new campaign\n  modules, or the hcm-appconfiguration fallback -> raw code rendered\n- Added WAREHOUSE_MANAGER=''Warehouse Manager'' to the three gaps; verified on\n  CMP-2026-08-26-004324: ''Transaction type - (Warehouse Manager)''\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore : Remove audit report and localization replay JSONs from PR\n\nFiles kept locally; localization changes are already applied on hcm-demo\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FIX : suppress fallback header caret when core renders its own arrow\n\nNewer digit-ui-module-core renders an SVG arrow (span.header-dropdown-arrow)\nin the tenant/language topbar dropdowns; the health-css fallback caret\n(label.cp::after, added when the old core rendered bare labels) then shows a\nsecond arrow. Hide the fallback via :has(+ .header-dropdown-arrow) so\nold-core builds keep their caret and new-core builds show exactly one.\nVerified against hcm-demo (new core) by injecting the rule live.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FIX : Single-flow categories (e.g. Revisit) now render with their category header\n\nThe flows side-nav flattened any category containing one flow into a bare item,\nso the polio Revisit (REDOSE) category showed ''Revisit Details'' dangling under\nDelivery with no group header. Every category now renders its collapsible header.\n(Category label fixed via localization: APP_CONFIG_CATEGORY_REDOSE=''Revisit'' in\nhcm-campaignmanager, which was overriding with ''Redose Category''.)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"43a419139c86071d1e6303e217c924b0fed488e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/git/trees/43a419139c86071d1e6303e217c924b0fed488e8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/git/commits/1fe4c93c62ad7849132ef51de9d453d5c66b401a","verification":{"payload":"tree 43a419139c86071d1e6303e217c924b0fed488e8\nparent abb2da1fb299cddb4664fa7c2eb4d93d58e80724\nauthor Naveen J <83631045+naveen-egov@users.noreply.github.com> 1787729316 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787729316 +0530\n\nFIX/HCMPRE-0000 : Design-system audit follow-up (tokens, layout, content standards) (#4334)\n\n* FIX : Error heading token and employeeCard disabled variant\n\nModule audits surfaced the app-config error heading using Material red\n#d32f2f (now error token #B91900) and the inventory Warehouse Details\npage''s disabled input hint using library #9E9E9E (now disabled token\n#C5C5C5 via the existing override group).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FIX : Token colors for campaign home badge and upload drag-drop area\n\nFull-sweep audit additions: campaign home count badge #F5F2F2 -> generic\nbg #EEEEEE, drag-drop hint text #b1b4b6 -> disabled token #C5C5C5, and\nthe upload container''s off-scale 5px radius -> 4px.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FIX : Hide campaign tag when no campaign name is available\n\nThe tag rendered as an empty pill above the Upload Microplan Data\nheading (and anywhere else the name is absent); skip rendering instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FIX : Keep upload-screen action buttons right-aligned without campaign tag\n\nThe header row uses space-between with [tag][buttons]; when the tag is\nhidden (no campaign name) the buttons jumped to the left. Anchor the\nbutton group with margin-left auto so alignment holds either way.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FIX : Anchor primary Search action to the right of the filter row\n\nThe library search bar renders [Search][Clear][Sort]; per the design\nsystem''s primary-action-right convention (footers, popups, wizards),\nreverse the row so Search sits right-most with Sort/Clear beside it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FIX : Pack search actions to the card''s right edge\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* DOCS : Design system audit report and content-audit localization changes\n\n- DESIGN_SYSTEM_AUDIT_REPORT.md: full audit scope, fixes, whitelists,\n  and upstream recommendations for DIGIT-UI-LIBRARIES.\n- localization-changes-2026-08-26-content-audit.json: the 97 en_DEMO\n  copy fixes applied on hcm-demo per the DIGIT content guidelines\n  (spelling, exclamation marks, double spaces, button Title Case,\n  heading sentence case), for replay on other environments.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* DOCS : Add Permission Handler casing fixes to the localization replay set\n\n29 entries (console modules, hcm-base-* templates, and the current\ncampaign) aligning the module/flow name to Title Case; the mixed casing\noriginated in the base templates themselves.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* DOCS : Add breadcrumb casing fix (VIEW_DETAILS) to localization replay set\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* DOCS : Breadcrumb audit fixes in localization replay set\n\n14 entries: 12 breadcrumbs normalized to sentence case, 2 missing\nbreadcrumb keys created (bulk stock upload, commodity campaigns) that\npreviously rendered as raw codes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Cl