parator in the title bar.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FIX : Field labels sentence-cased per DIGIT content standard (886 keys)\n\n- hcm-appconfiguration: 478 field/label-pair/component-name keys Title Case -> sentence case (buttons/CTAs untouched)\n- Campaign CMP-2026-08-25-004322 modules (inventory/registration/complaints): 408 field label keys\n- Scan-trigger labels (Team Code / Scan Delivery) kept Title Case since they render as buttons\n- Replay JSON captures final upserted values on hcm-demo\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FIX : Sentence-case field labels in all hcm-base-* template modules (6631 keys)\n\n- 49 base template modules (closehousehold/complaints/hfreferral/insidemonitoring/\n  inventory/lqa/permissionhandler/registration/stock/stockreconciliation/stockreports\n  x bednet/co-delivery/default/mr-dn/oncho/polio) swept on hcm-demo\n- Same rules as campaign fix: buttons/CTAs/headings/errors untouched, acronyms kept,\n  scan-trigger labels (Team Code / Scan Delivery) stay Title Case\n- New campaigns clone these templates, so future campaigns inherit correct casing\n- Existing campaigns keep their snapshots (per review decision: update base, not each campaign)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FIX : Cross-verify buttons against FormConfig templates; restore Title Case on 64 button keys\n\n- Walked all 71 HCM-ADMIN-CONSOLE.FormConfigTemplate records + campaign FormConfigs,\n  collected every code at button positions (footer, footerActions, primary/secondary\n  actions, scanner triggers) and verified resolved values are Title Case\n- Reverted 41 sweep-affected button keys (Save Filter, Clear Filter, Open Member Card,\n  Skip & Continue, Scan Child/Code, Close Out, View Stock Excess/Less Reports)\n- Fixed 10 more sweep-affected scanner/filter buttons (Delivery Team Code, Apply Filter)\n- Fixed 13 pre-existing violations (Back to Home, Create a New Transaction)\n- Re-verified: 0 button casing violations remain; 141 missing-key references are\n  pre-existing template gaps (INT-CAMP/IRS-mz/communityregistration/attendance)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FIX : Raw WAREHOUSE_MANAGER role code leaking into role-scoped field labels\n\n- Editor suffixes dropdownTemplate labels with t(role); DISTRIBUTOR resolved but\n  WAREHOUSE_MANAGER had no translation in hcm-base-inventory-default, new campaign\n  modules, or the hcm-appconfiguration fallback -> raw code rendered\n- Added WAREHOUSE_MANAGER=''Warehouse Manager'' to the three gaps; verified on\n  CMP-2026-08-26-004324: ''Transaction type - (Warehouse Manager)''\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore : Remove audit report and localization replay JSONs from PR\n\nFiles kept locally; localization changes are already applied on hcm-demo\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FIX : suppress fallback header caret when core renders its own arrow\n\nNewer digit-ui-module-core renders an SVG arrow (span.header-dropdown-arrow)\nin the tenant/language topbar dropdowns; the health-css fallback caret\n(label.cp::after, added when the old core rendered bare labels) then shows a\nsecond arrow. Hide the fallback via :has(+ .header-dropdown-arrow) so\nold-core builds keep their caret and new-core builds show exactly one.\nVerified against hcm-demo (new core) by injecting the rule live.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FIX : Single-flow categories (e.g. Revisit) now render with their category header\n\nThe flows side-nav flattened any category containing one flow into a bare item,\nso the polio Revisit (REDOSE) category showed ''Revisit Details'' dangling under\nDelivery with no group header. Every category now renders its collapsible header.\n(Category label fixed via localization: APP_CONFIG_CATEGORY_REDOSE=''Revisit'' in\nhcm-campaignmanager, which was overriding with ''Redose Category''.)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjpWkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJpIQABVBCnlt272LILL/PCvbAZYW\nHGlb5sQJk2rPMWgz/WpUMRBblL8hZnXvJN8THBWjZOAGOVrLULd2vo0pY0hKbThi\nliSRXqrG1+Mo0XzAgA/KHWMwI8TJPLzqiBkZ+NuoAdRUMsaMhX0PVMnn1eAimU89\nDbDYTx9b0zguCPCGuNza84e5SCnUKagISpeK9zuVCtHRP3akTflMciIBmb0X3qQp\npStHBbMqmubUAgiI7WUNBGh13cmd3Rc+8Q9fLnWCwKiwQJ/DgbOfIO9mqC+oq5TI\n5sm+ZQVZHh4IVGOqTIq8wmz6j+5VLsAbfz0cYZff2gylAjkyqoBB9xNdG4/2x51C\nN8ZMSjNfTWvb/y9KH5yBCFVKzCi1ksxKF8iB1ZQ9g1A7CedbIvked+SmAtINOcm4\ngsuYCHyVwSkiz+QZ7ho4NHA6zDQdIfBVhuzg4A8skHEcLAsY2Qtpt6NZH91w44QJ\nIN5UTXhhJK0gzLGyKoNzI80GhE5E859Yz0PqJlgd5kXuXfl0nbDIw/nxY0JCboJs\no/GLSdbSp4lADljSfLo/bT7Zj3YhLbbE6gRn/pNLtC+ZfdBLn7uFkb6zK8HMf35f\n5qmaZRNDbayPFl9r3bCrU7bVVPvfb9WdyenCHeRWEPdWckFRwYtDDIK2mhkvRRoQ\np3/KORet4i6sFbXBhWYK\n=yLMg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T07:28:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commit/1fe4c93c62ad7849132ef51de9d453d5c66b401a","node_id":"C_kwDOKSe0RtoAKDFmZTRjOTNjNjJhZDc4NDkxMzJlZjUxZGU5ZDQ1M2Q1YzY2YjQwMWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commit/abb2da1fb299cddb4664fa7c2eb4d93d58e80724","sha":"abb2da1fb299cddb4664fa7c2eb4d93d58e80724","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/abb2da1fb299cddb4664fa7c2eb4d93d58e80724"}],"sha":"1fe4c93c62ad7849132ef51de9d453d5c66b401a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/1fe4c93c62ad7849132ef51de9d453d5c66b401a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83631045?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/naveen-egov","id":83631045,"login":"naveen-egov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNjMxMDQ1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/naveen-egov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/abb2da1fb299cddb4664fa7c2eb4d93d58e80724/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T13:39:01Z","email":"83631045+naveen-egov@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Naveen J"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T13:39:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"FIX/HCMPRE-0000 : DIGIT design system compliance for HCM console (topbar carets + token colors) (#4333)\n\n* FIX : Show dropdown caret for tenant and language selectors in employee topbar\n\ndigit-ui-module-core passes showArrow only to the profile dropdown, so\nthe ChangeCity and ChangeLanguage custom-selector labels rendered as\nplain text. Add a scoped CSS caret to the header dropdown labels until\ncore passes showArrow for these dropdowns.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FIX : Align HCM console colors with DIGIT design system tokens\n\nAudited the app configuration editor (all flows/tabs) against\ndesign.digit.org and replaced every off-token color:\n\n- App config title bar #929292 -> primary-2 #0B4B66 (the white version\n  text failed WCAG AA contrast on the old grey)\n- Mistyped divider tokens #d6d5d5/#d6d4d5 -> #D6D5D4\n- Off-palette selection tints #E6EDF0/#EFF8FF -> info bg #DEEFFF\n- Fully-configurable tag #1C00BD/#EBECFE -> info #0057BD/#DEEFFF;\n  template tag #FFFCC0 -> library warning bg #FFF7D6\n- Text #333 -> text-primary #363636; drag-handle dots #d9d9d9,\n  icon fills #B1B4B6, disabled theme var -> disabled token #C5C5C5\n- Inline #e0e0e0 borders in campaign-manager JS -> divider #D6D5D4\n- Scoped overrides for library styles that ship off-token values:\n  input border #E0E0E0 -> #505A5F, switch track #BFBFBF -> #C5C5C5,\n  disabled header labels / input text #9E9E9E -> #C5C5C5\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FIX : Token colors for field-properties panel tooltip and disabled dropdown\n\nFound while auditing the Page Properties panel states: the custom\nhover tooltip used #333 (now text-primary #363636) and the disabled\nfield-type dropdown text used the library''s #9E9E9E (now disabled\ntoken #C5C5C5).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FIX : Accessible warning pair for rule-summary joiner tag and dropdown palette\n\nDeep audit of every flow/page''s Page Properties states surfaced the\nlogic rule-summary joiner tag using off-token #FFFDE7/#9E5F00; aligned\nit and MultiSelectDropdown''s local warning color with the library''s\naccessible warning pair #FFF7D6/#5C450A.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FIX : Disabled token for library Button''s inline #9E9E9E disabled state\n\nThe module-selection screen''s ''Upcoming'' buttons get an inline #9E9E9E\nfrom the library Button when disabled; a stylesheet !important rule\noutranks non-important inline styles, so align disabled secondary\nbuttons with the #C5C5C5 token.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FIX : Extend disabled-button token override to primary/tertiary variants\n\nThe campaign view-details screen''s disabled step buttons (primary\nvariant) carry the same inline #9E9E9E from the library Button; cover\nall button variants with the #C5C5C5 disabled token.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FIX : Campaign chip tint #EFF8FF -> info bg token #DEEFFF\n\nFound on setup-campaign step 3 (campaign date): the campaign-name chip\nused the off-palette #EFF8FF tint; aligned campaign.scss and the same\nvalue in payment.scss with the info bg token.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Updated css\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Swathi-eGov <137176788+Swathi-eGov@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Swathi-eGov <swathi.chatrathi@egovernments.org>","tree":{"sha":"9a498e534f120de9f6f2fd4b8679603c32787096","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/git/trees/9a498e534f120de9f6f2fd4b8679603c32787096"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/git/commits/abb2da1fb299cddb4664fa7c2eb4d93d58e80724","verification":{"payload":"tree 9a498e534f120de9f6f2fd4b8679603c32787096\nparent d06fe79bf7f5b5cd519e8b31db9cda543a8ef78d\nauthor Naveen J <83631045+naveen-egov@users.noreply.github.com> 1787665141 +05