dropdown palette\n\nDeep audit of every flow/page''s Page Properties states surfaced the\nlogic rule-summary joiner tag using off-token #FFFDE7/#9E5F00; aligned\nit and MultiSelectDropdown''s local warning color with the library''s\naccessible warning pair #FFF7D6/#5C450A.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FIX : Disabled token for library Button''s inline #9E9E9E disabled state\n\nThe module-selection screen''s ''Upcoming'' buttons get an inline #9E9E9E\nfrom the library Button when disabled; a stylesheet !important rule\noutranks non-important inline styles, so align disabled secondary\nbuttons with the #C5C5C5 token.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FIX : Extend disabled-button token override to primary/tertiary variants\n\nThe campaign view-details screen''s disabled step buttons (primary\nvariant) carry the same inline #9E9E9E from the library Button; cover\nall button variants with the #C5C5C5 disabled token.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* FIX : Campaign chip tint #EFF8FF -> info bg token #DEEFFF\n\nFound on setup-campaign step 3 (campaign date): the campaign-name chip\nused the off-palette #EFF8FF tint; aligned campaign.scss and the same\nvalue in payment.scss with the info bg token.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Updated css\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Swathi-eGov <137176788+Swathi-eGov@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Swathi-eGov <swathi.chatrathi@egovernments.org>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjZr1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAA18QAEwqWpNmkroquEOzUDMCdhpS\n3604c+vBBTKXG5RGkioGo4s7WE6dp0LmtQ3WBQyRfOdsrIOUmVY+OjmJlgUmcSqP\naZHbEAHO9yfBZgiHPTDxE4Py3LUHI4beYy5YzeRrpgFDYxC+wEvUChCYH3sQO5GD\n9qRWEPL1IMGT6Gvfh61OPb1X0p8fc8JqiHdb+kwFuXAJQNGmC8QbeXiZzFGQXpxD\n46AM7WPevJ5iGdV5KbjsIocspUXjMEIRaN68N1p8wAGnXpJs7BG7YDzW6UwKwXM4\nZJV/Avc5RsFM+zHc8