web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commit/2adc1a9d204c0b4baebdae6cb5843fab08303ede","node_id":"C_kwDOKSe0RtoAKDJhZGMxYTlkMjA0YzBiNGJhZWJkYWU2Y2I1ODQzZmFiMDgzMDNlZGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commit/bc82ff7aa3199bc35cf8041ad78657d4d11cf242","sha":"bc82ff7aa3199bc35cf8041ad78657d4d11cf242","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/bc82ff7aa3199bc35cf8041ad78657d4d11cf242"}],"sha":"2adc1a9d204c0b4baebdae6cb5843fab08303ede","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/2adc1a9d204c0b4baebdae6cb5843fab08303ede"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/137176788?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Swathi-eGov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Swathi-eGov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Swathi-eGov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Swathi-eGov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Swathi-eGov","id":137176788,"login":"Swathi-eGov","node_id":"U_kgDOCC0m1A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Swathi-eGov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Swathi-eGov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Swathi-eGov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Swathi-eGov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Swathi-eGov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Swathi-eGov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/commits/bc82ff7aa3199bc35cf8041ad78657d4d11cf242/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T12:28:53Z","email":"137176788+Swathi-eGov@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Swathi-eGov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T12:28:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"BUGFIX/HCMPRE-4232 : setup loader and delivery guards (#4234)\n\n* chore(hcm-react19): point index.html at the demo globalConfigs\n\nAll six index.html files under health/micro-ui-react19/web loaded the config\nvia the <%= REACT_APP_GLOBAL %> template parameter, which resolved to an empty\nstring unless REACT_APP_GLOBAL was exported. Hardcode the demo config so the\napp boots with the demo tenant out of the box:\n\n  https://hcm-demo-assets.s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/demo/globalConfigsWorkbenchDemo.js\n\nbuilds/payments-ui/public/index.html had no config script at all, so the tag is\nadded there rather than replaced.\n\nAlso adds web/public/globalConfigs.js as a local copy of the same demo config.\nNothing loads it today (the hardcoded S3 URL wins); it is checked in as a\nreference for running against a local config.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(campaign): drop the orphan asterisk on scanner fields in app config preview\n\nIn the app configuration preview, a required scanner field (e.g. Team Code on\nInventory > Record Stock Details > Warehouse Details) rendered a label row whose\nonly content was the red required asterisk, sitting above the scanner button.\n\nComponentToRender blanked `label` for scanner/checkbox fields because those\ncarry their own label, but left `withoutLabel` false while `required` stayed\ntrue, so FieldV1 still rendered the label row. Hoist the label resolution into\n`resolvedLabel` and drive `withoutLabel` off it, so any field that resolves to\nan empty label drops the row entirely.\n\nAlso matches the `qrScanner` spelling, which remoteConfigSlice.js:814 and\nmdmsToAppConfig.js:181,258 already treat as a scanner.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(campaign): one loader at a time in setup-campaign, and guard delivery rules\n\nSingle loader\n-------------\nClicking Next on a setup-campaign step put two full-screen loaders on screen at\nonce: the flow''s OverlayLoader (\"please wait while updating\") plus the newly\nmounted step''s own PageLoader, because the step advances while the save mutation\nis still in flight. Measured on the boundary step: 2 simultaneous loaders before,\n1 after.\n\n- CampaignSubmitContext (new): exposes `isSubmitting` for the hosting flow.\n- SetupCampaign: provides it as `loader || isUpdating || isDataCreating`. The\n  useMemo sits above the early returns so the hook always runs.\n- Step screens (BoundarySummary, CampaignDetailsSummary, CampaignSummary,\n  DataUploadSummary, DeliveryDetailsSummary, SelectingBoundariesDuplicate,\n  CycleConfiguration, deliveryRule) skip their own page loader while that\n  overlay is up.\n\nAlso fixes a pre-existing blank screen on the same transition: line 1225 read\n`{loader || (isUpdating && <Loader/>)}`, but `loader` holds a boolean, and React\nrenders `true` as nothing - so no overlay rendered at all for the whole window\nwhere `loader === true` (~800ms of blank). Now `{(loader || isUpdating) && ...}`,\nmatching CreateCampaign.js:587.\n\nDelivery rule guards\n--------------------\nA malformed (non-array) `deliveryRule` in session data crashed the delivery step\nwith \"deliveryRules.some is not a function\" and then \"data.map is not a\nfunction\". Make the consumers defensive:\n\n- hasInvalidMaxCountAttribute / checkAttributeValidity / handleValidate tolerate\n  a non-array instead of throwing (the `= []` default only covered undefined).\n- restructureData returns null for non-array input.\n- SetupCampaign checks Array.isArray before building the payload, and omits\n  deliveryRules entirely when the value is malformed so a bad shape cannot\n  overwrite the rules already saved on the draft.\n- deliveryRule/index.js ignores a non-array savedDeliveryRules so the step\n  rebuilds from the cycle config instead of carrying the bad shape forward.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(campaign): make the resource popup loader visible while products load\n\n\"Add Resources To Be Delivered\" appeared to show no loading feedback. The\nloading branch rendered a bare <Loader/> with no wrapper, so it collapsed to\nalmost nothing and was easy to miss while /product/v1/_search and\n/product/variant/v1/_search were in flight (~750ms-1.3s each).\n\nWrap it in a centered container with a min-height so it holds the popup''s\nlayout. Measured with the product calls delayed: the loader now renders 90x90\ninside a 115px-tall wrapper instead of collapsing.\n\nNote this only shows when there is an actual wait - the product list is usually\nalready cached from step load, in which case the popup opens immediately.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(campaign): confirm and show progress when creating resources\n\nThe \"Add new resource\" screen ran createProduct -> createProductVariant with no\nfeedback at all: no confirmation before creating, and no loader while the two\ncalls were in flight, so the button stayed clickable and repeat clicks created\nduplicate product variants.\n\n- Validated submit now opens a confirmation popup listing the resources to be\n  created (name - variant) with Back / Confirm.\n- Confirm shows an overlay loader using the existing, already-translated\n  HCM_CONFIRMING_RESOURCE_CREATION (\"Resource creation\").\n- The loader is cleared on every failure path (createProduct error, duplicate\n  variant guard, createProductVariant error); success navigates away as before.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(campaign): correct the module selection loader variant and text\n\nBoth module-selection screens rendered their loader as an early return - nothing\nis behind it - yet used variant \"OverlayLoader\", which is meant for covering\nexisting content while saving. That variant also selects the library''s six-dot\nanimation (Loader picks animationData from the variant), so the screen showed a\ndifferent loader from the rest of the flow.\n\nSwitch both to PageLoader, and use LOADING_MODULE (\"Loading module\") for the\ntext instead of SAVING_FEATURES_CONFIG_IN_SERVER, which describes a save rather\nthan a load. AppModule''s isCreatingModule overlay is left as OverlayLoader since\nit genuinely covers the selection grid.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(campaign): hide the delivery toggle when a cycle has one delivery\n\nThe delivery summary rendered a single-option toggle (\"Delivery 1\") for\ncampaigns with one cycle and one delivery, unlike the delivery screen it\nsummarises, which shows the condition directly.\n\nRender the toggle only when there is more than one delivery. The condition\ncontent was keyed off deliveries.find(active === true) - with no toggle nothing\nsets `active`, so it now falls back to the first delivery.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* BUGFIX/HCMPRE-4232 : Reverted globalConfig changes\n\n* Fixed delivery description issue\n\n* render app-config preview fields whose hidden is an expression\n\n* show the round tag before delivery rules exist\n\n* UX audit fixes: app config panel properties, button CTA rules, panel card toggles\n\n* default SMC to multi round on the campaign type step\n\n* Code rabbit fix\n\n* replace the Console privacy policy with the reviewed template\n\n* Updated core version\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: naveen-egov <naveen.j@egovernments.org>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Naveen J <83631045+naveen-egov@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"379340f37165c4fafd31000adfaede49a0e85783","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/git/trees/379340f37165c4fafd31000adfaede49a0e85783"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/egovernments/DIGIT-Frontend/git/commits/bc82ff7aa3199bc35cf8041ad78657d4d11cf242","verification":{"payload":"tree 379340f37165c4fafd31000adfaede49a0e85783\nparent c5626e66b557d5a8fa817bafe68c64e8e909cb95\nauthor Swathi-eGov <137176788+Swathi-eGov@users.noreply.github.com> 1786105733 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786105733 +0530\n\nBUGFIX/HCMPRE-4232 : setup loader and delivery guards (#4234)\n\n* chore(hcm-react19): point index.html at the demo globalConfigs\n\nAll six index.html files under health/micro-ui-react19/web loaded the config\nvia the <%= REACT_APP_GLOBAL %> template parameter, which resolved to an empty\nstring unless REACT_APP_GLOBAL was exported. Hardcode the demo config so the\napp boots with the demo tenant out of the box:\n\n  https://hcm-demo-assets.s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/demo/globalConfigsWorkbenchDemo.js\n\nbuilds/payments-ui/public/index.html had no config script at all, so the tag is\nadded there rather than replaced.\n\nAlso adds web/public/globalConfigs.js as a local copy of the same demo config.\nNothing loads it today (the hardcoded S3 URL wins); it is checked in as a\nreference for running against a local config.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(campaign): drop the orphan asterisk on scanner fields in app config preview\n\nIn the app configuration preview, a required scanner field (e.g. Team Code on\nInventory > Record Stock Details > Warehouse Details) rendered a label row whose\nonly content was the red required asterisk, sitting above the scanner button.\n\nComponentToRender blanked `label` for scanner/checkbox fields because those\ncarry their own label, but left `withoutLabel` false while `required` stayed\ntrue, so FieldV1 still rendered the label row. Hoist the label resolution into\n`resolvedLabel` and drive `withoutLabel` off it, so any field that resolves to\nan empty label drops the row entirely.\n\nAlso matches the `qrScanner` spelling, which remoteConfigSlice.js:814 and\nmdmsToAppConfig.js:181,258 already treat as a scanner.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(campaign): one loader at a time in setup-campaign, and guard delivery rules\n\nSingle loader\n-------------\nClicking Next on a setup-campaign step put two full-screen loaders on screen at\nonce: the flow''s OverlayLoader (\"please wait while updating\") plus the newly\nmounted step''s own PageLoader, because the step advances while the save mutation\nis still in flight. Measured on the boundary step: 2 simultaneous loaders before,\n1 after.\n\n- CampaignSubmitContext (new): exposes `isSubmitting` for the hosting flow.\n- SetupCampaign: provides it as `loader || isUpdating || isDataCreating`. The\n  useMemo sits above the early returns so the hook always runs.\n- Step screens (BoundarySummary, CampaignDetailsSummary, CampaignSummary,\n  DataUploadSummary, DeliveryDetailsSummary, SelectingBoundariesDuplicate,\n  CycleConfiguration, deliveryRule) skip their own page loader while that\n  overlay is up.\n\nAlso fixes a pre-existing blank screen on the same transition: line 1225 read\n`{loader || (isUpdating && <Loader/>)}`, but `loader` holds a boolean, and React\nrenders `true` as nothing - so no overlay rendered at all for the whole window\nwhere `loader === true` (~800ms of blank). Now `{(loader || isUpdating) && ...}`,\nmatching CreateCampaign.js:587.\n\nDelivery rule guards\n--------------------\nA malformed (non-array) `deliveryRule` in session data crashed the delivery step\nwith \"deliveryRules.some is not a function\" and then \"data.map is not a\nfunction\". Make the consumers defensive:\n\n- hasInvalidMaxCountAttribute / checkAttributeValidity / handleValidate tolerate\n  a non-array instead of throwing (the `= []` default only covered undefined).\n- restructureData returns null for non-array input.\n- SetupCampaign checks Array.isArray before building the payload, and omits\n  deliveryRules entirely when the value is malformed so a bad shape cannot\n  overwrite the rules already saved on the draft.\n- deliveryRule/index.js ignores a non-array savedDeliveryRules so the step\n  rebuilds from the cycle config instead of carrying the bad shape forward.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(campaign): make the resource popup loader visible while products load\n\n\"Add Resources To Be Delivered\" appeared to show no loading feedback. The\nloading branch rendered a bare <Loader/> with no wrapper, so it collapsed to\nalmost nothing and was easy to miss while /product/v1/_search and\n/product/variant/v1/_search were in flight (~750ms-1.3s each).\n\nWrap it in a centered container with a min-height so it holds the popup''s\nlayout. Measured with the product calls delayed: the loader now renders 90x90\ninside a 115px-tall wrapper instead of collapsing.\n\nNote this only shows when there is an actual wait - the product list is usually\nalready cached from step load, in which case the popup opens immediately.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(campaign): confirm and show progress when creating resources\n\nThe \"Add new resource\" screen ran createProduct -> createProductVariant with no\nfeedback at all: no confirmation before creating, and no loader while the two\ncalls were in flight, so the button stayed clickable and repeat clicks created\nduplicate product variants.\n\n- Validated submit now opens a confirmation popup listing the resources to be\n  created (name - variant) with Back / Confirm.\n- Confirm shows an overlay loader using the existing, already-translated\n  HCM_CONFIRMING_RESOURCE_CREATION (\"Resource creation\").\n- The loader is cleared on every failure path (createProduct error, duplicate\n  variant guard, createProductVariant error); success navigates away as before.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(campaign): correct the module selection loader variant and text\n\nBoth module-selection screens rendered their loader as an early return - nothing\nis behind it - yet used variant \"OverlayLoader\", which is meant for covering\nexisting content while saving. That variant also selects the library''s six-dot\nanimation (Loader picks animationData from the variant), so the screen showed a\ndifferent loader from the rest of the flow.\n\nSwitch both to PageLoader, and use LOADING_MODULE (\"Loading module\") for the\ntext instead of SAVING_FEATURES_CONFIG_IN_SERVER, which describes a save rather\nthan a load. AppModule''s isCreatingModule overlay is left as OverlayLoader since\nit genuinely covers the selection grid.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(campaign): hide the delivery toggle when a cycle has one delivery\n\nThe delivery summary rendered a single-option toggle (\"Delivery 1\") for\ncampaigns with one cycle and one delivery, unlike the delivery screen it\nsummarises, which shows the condition directly.\n\nRender the toggle only when there is more than one delivery. The condition\ncontent was keyed off deliveries.find(active === true) - with no toggle nothing\nsets `active`, so it now falls back to the first delivery.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* BUGFIX/HCMPRE-4232 : Reverted globalConfig changes\n\n* Fixed delivery description issue\n\n* render app-config preview fields whose hidden is an expression\n\n* show the round tag before delivery rules exist\n\n* UX audit fixes: app config panel properties, button CTA rules, panel card toggles\n\n* default SMC to multi round on the campaign type step\n\n* Code rabbit fix\n\n* replace the Console privacy policy with the reviewed template\n\n* Updated core version\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: naveen-egov <naveen.j@egovernments.org>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Naveen J <83631045+naveen-egov@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature"