ps://github.com/lazarv","id":1749493,"login":"lazarv","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDk0OTM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lazarv/react-server/commit/741d9bb3d96c847d7ebb2d343685fdeb67d65430","node_id":"C_kwDOKWnYDNoAKDc0MWQ5YmIzZDk2Yzg0N2Q3ZWJiMmQzNDM2ODVmZGViNjdkNjU0MzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lazarv/react-server/commit/1c22b36197088ead241ba1fefb9741e0e59d5a99","sha":"1c22b36197088ead241ba1fefb9741e0e59d5a99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lazarv/react-server/commits/1c22b36197088ead241ba1fefb9741e0e59d5a99"}],"sha":"741d9bb3d96c847d7ebb2d343685fdeb67d65430","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lazarv/react-server/commits/741d9bb3d96c847d7ebb2d343685fdeb67d65430"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1749493?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lazarv","id":1749493,"login":"lazarv","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDk0OTM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lazarv/react-server/commits/1c22b36197088ead241ba1fefb9741e0e59d5a99/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-29T12:54:19Z","email":"lazarv1982@gmail.com","name":"Viktor Lázár"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-29T12:54:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: use client no-ssr (#413)\n\n## Summary\n\nIntroduces a new react-server directive, `\"use client; no-ssr\"`, for\nclient components whose dependency graph only makes sense in the\nbrowser. A plain `\"use client\"` module still renders during SSR — its\nimports get bundled and evaluated on the server even though only the\ninteractivity ships to the client. For components that pull in WebGL\ncontexts, charting libraries, code editors, or anything else that\ntouches `window` at module scope, that means hundreds of KiB of\nJavaScript landing in the SSR/edge worker bundle to render an empty\nwrapper.\n\nThe new directive replaces the module with a null-rendering stub in the\nSSR build (no imports of the implementation graph at all) and emits a\nwrapper in the client build that imports the original through a virtual\nid and renders it inside `<ClientOnly>`. The two halves match up at\nhydration: SSR sends nothing, the client renders nothing on the first\npass, then transitions to the real component after `useEffect`. No\nhydration mismatch, no heavy code in the worker.\n\n## How it''s wired\n\nThe transform lives in `lib/plugins/use-client.mjs`. The RSC build\nbranch is unchanged (`registerClientReference`). The SSR branch, when it\nsees a no-ssr module, walks the AST for the default and named exports\nand emits stubs that all return `null`. The client branch, gated on\n`enforce: \"pre\"` in the build mode only, emits a `\"use client\"` wrapper\nmodule that imports the original via\n`virtual:no-ssr-original:<absolute-path>`. The corresponding\n`resolveId`/`load` pair on the same plugin returns the file content\nverbatim; an early-return at the top of the transform handler skips the\nvirtual id so the wrapper logic doesn''t recurse on itself.\n\nDirective matching is centralised in a new `lib/utils/directives.mjs`\nhelper, `parseClientDirective(directives)`. The grammar is permissive —\nit splits on `;` and trims segments — so `\"use client\"`, `\"use\nclient;no-ssr\"`, `\"use client; no-ssr\"`, `\"use client; no-ssr\"`, and\n`\"use client ; no-ssr\"` all parse to the same `{ isClient, isNoSSR }`\nshape. Every directive-aware site in the runtime now goes through the\nparser instead of enumerating string variants: `use-client.mjs`,\n`use-server.mjs`, `file-router/plugin.mjs` (`isClientPageSource` and\n`isClientSource`), and `build/server.mjs` root detection.\n`use-directive-inline.mjs` was extended so `skipIfModuleDirective` can\nbe a predicate, and `use-client-inline.mjs` switched to that form to\nhandle whitespace variants without enumeration. Substring fast-paths in\n`lib/utils/module.mjs` and `lib/build/server.mjs` had their closing\nquotes dropped (`''\"use client''` instead of `''\"use client\"''`) so any\nmodifier form is captured by the cheap pre-filter.\n\n## Demo: docs site\n\n`docs/src/components/ReactViteScene.jsx` was the canary. It previously\nrouted Three.js through dynamic `import()` inside `useEffect` to keep\n~520 KiB of WebGL out of the worker bundle. With the new directive in\nplace, the dynamic-import workaround is gone and the imports are static\nagain. Verified against the produced bundle: the Cloudflare worker\noutput (`.cloudflare/worker/.react-server/server/edge.mjs` and the\nsurrounding chunks) has zero references to `WebGLRenderer`,\n`MeshPhysicalMaterial`, `EffectComposer`, `UnrealBloomPass`,\n`PMREMGenerator`, `ACESFilmicToneMapping`, or any other Three.js\nidentifier — the SSR-side `ReactViteScene` chunk is the 116-byte null\nstub. The client bundle keeps the full 566 KiB Three.js chunk and only\nloads it on pages that actually mount the scene.","tree":{"sha":"d6987daaf4c82a08c976077037f0b1c8647cb120","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lazarv/react-server/git/trees/d6987daaf4c82a08c976077037f0b1c8647cb120"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lazarv/react-server/git/commits/1c22b36197088ead241ba1fefb9741e0e59d5a99","verification":{"payload":"tree d6987daaf4c82a08c976077037f0b1c8647cb120\nparent 6f0104d6d3fdb20ff9844b11ab96ecca1e9d8ae4\nauthor Viktor Lázár <lazarv1982@gmail.com> 1777467259 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777467259 +0200\n\nfeat: use client no-ssr (#413)\n\n## Summary\n\nIntroduces a new react-server directive, `\"use client; no-ssr\"`, for\nclient components whose dependency graph only makes sense in the\nbrowser. A plain `\"use client\"` module still renders during SSR — its\nimports get bundled and evaluated on the server even though only the\ninteractivity ships to the client. For components that pull in WebGL\ncontexts, charting libraries, code editors, or anything else that\ntouches `window` at module scope, that means hundreds of KiB of\nJavaScript landing in the SSR/edge worker bundle to render an empty\nwrapper.\n\nThe new directive replaces the module with a null-rendering stub in the\nSSR build (no imports of the implementation graph at all) and emits a\nwrapper in the client build that imports the original through a virtual\nid and renders it inside `<ClientOnly>`. The two halves match up at\nhydration: SSR sends nothing, the client renders nothing on the first\npass, then transitions to the real component after `useEffect`. No\nhydration mismatch, no heavy code in the worker.\n\n## How it''s wired\n\nThe transform lives in `lib/plugins/use-client.mjs`. The RSC build\nbranch is unchanged (`registerClientReference`). The SSR branch, when it\nsees a no-ssr module, walks the AST for the default and named exports\nand emits stubs that all return `null`. The client branch, gated on\n`enforce: \"pre\"` in the build mode only, emits a `\"use client\"` wrapper\nmodule that imports the original via\n`virtual:no-ssr-original:<absolute-path>`. The corresponding\n`resolveId`/`load` pair on the same plugin returns the file content\nverbatim; an early-return at the top of the transform handler skips the\nvirtual id so the wrapper logic doesn''t recurse on itself.\n\nDirective matching is centralised in a new `lib/utils/directives.mjs`\nhelper, `parseClientDirective(directives)`. The grammar is permissive —\nit splits on `;` and trims segments — so `\"use client\"`, `\"use\nclient;no-ssr\"`, `\"use client; no-ssr\"`, `\"use client; no-ssr\"`, and\n`\"use client ; no-ssr\"` all parse to the same `{ isClient, isNoSSR }`\nshape. Every directive-aware site in the runtime now goes through the\nparser instead of enumerating string variants: `use-client.mjs`,\n`use-server.mjs`, `file-router/plugin.mjs` (`isClientPageSource` and\n`isClientSource`), and `build/server.mjs` root detection.\n`use-directive-inline.mjs` was extended so `skipIfModuleDirective` can\nbe a predicate, and `use-client-inline.mjs` switched to that form to\nhandle whitespace variants without enumeration. Substring fast-paths in\n`lib/utils/module.mjs` and `lib/build/server.mjs` had their closing\nquotes dropped (`''\"use client''` instead of `''\"use client\"''`) so any\nmodifier form is captured by the cheap pre-filter.\n\n## Demo: docs site\n\n`docs/src/components/ReactViteScene.jsx` was the canary. It previously\nrouted Three.js through dynamic `import()` inside `useEffect` to keep\n~520 KiB of WebGL out of the worker bundle. With the new directive in\nplace, the dynamic-import workaround is gone and the imports are static\nagain. Verified against the produced bundle: the Cloudflare worker\noutput (`.cloudflare/worker/.react-server/server/edge.mjs` and the\nsurrounding chunks) has zero references to `WebGLRenderer`,\n`MeshPhysicalMaterial`, `EffectComposer`, `UnrealBloomPass`,\n`PMREMGenerator`, `ACESFilmicToneMapping`, or any other Three.js\nidentifier — the SSR-side `ReactViteScene` chunk is the 116-byte null\nstub. The client bundle keeps the full 566 KiB Three.js chunk and only\nloads it on pages that actually mount the scene.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp8f97CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzEIQADiJP18J8w3uFU0q0wqKlH4+\n9MC7Kx+OYUpelr5fCdy/l8c+Kz/JDZTn1GOlI4wNfqIiCXLOGA9hRaoQ7jvJqKgv\nM4TRH0TyCAHc1+iQDNX7aDLo9yDnc8TE1/fWKKs2TvGjBnESLzG2U/TGdIO4wR+y\n7xNc2MeOn4R0aQOsqax7lOnSoKMBJfHsZ3ZOOiA8t6Nap1/jQBkBaQfVtIA3KZRh\n2h/FrAzeSsy/TmxTimaReyPRXlv0BWA8lFYHCRr2NuUXreSSwqFlG9r/sNEx+Ni6\nYyNDhhT6G906s2xD+/G+KRdKqknWJqLkRS8d/+RYmIM29C5LRLX4bK7yrzELUkZr\nViF+vxI5anV7Jtv4uJtJNP/cBI8x/U9opfJkkI+53B4xrTomn4BbWFYoRLdJCB5l\nqihLHAN9eh+u+Wv7kAovFTbMYBD6QGukNaSPy/s6rpcrSePZtdYrjZcKkk5mgugz\noRrzNiztG9dDOB9b5RRRph5Y3oOXbHzL6cIVtZBHTF5NsiFYi3HGjWXx9KonkkrX\nUxq39yNEQHeX+wCYZRjULqUGKgvcdiwscBHk7nFs7iWHwvGLFeTcRqxq8kuesrA8\nv6OSEaaZI0wqhJ7rzSPfkX+OJpgmlt6CRtzP6tN0dS7JVXHa7WItcjBHwUNLnUUP\n3CnSLOEE+FfsIDiPNKL9\n=l2Ot\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-29T12:54:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.