m/repos/lazarv/react-server/commits/5353c12fb5bda51dfe2243ca4eb19da8662c5c4e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1749493?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lazarv","id":1749493,"login":"lazarv","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDk0OTM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lazarv/react-server/commits/84abefcfbbb163d8d1391d5ef5a5af3f2dc8838f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-28T13:18:30Z","email":"lazarv1982@gmail.com","name":"Viktor Lázár"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-28T13:18:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: backpressure (#408)\n\nHardens `react-server start` for production deployment behind a load\nbalancer or a k8s/Docker orchestrator. The Node HTTP server now ships\nwith sensible slow-loris and idle-connection timeouts, signals propagate\ncorrectly through the cluster master, workers drain in-flight requests\non `SIGTERM` instead of dropping them, and a crash-loop guard prevents\nfork-bombing the host on a deterministic boot failure. A new readiness\nendpoint reports worker liveness so external probes can route around a\ndead worker before the kernel reaps the socket.\n\nThe headline addition is an **adaptive admission controller** built on\n`performance.eventLoopUtilization()` with an AIMD update loop. Under\nload it expands the in-flight limit while ELU stays below target and\ncontracts multiplicatively when the loop saturates, holding tail latency\nwell below the unbounded baseline. Admission is FIFO across the wait\nqueue so requests don''t starve, and a fast-path release skips the EWMA\nbookkeeping on the hot path. Backpressure is opt-in by default and\nauto-enables only under `react-server start` cluster mode — the feature\nis meaningful on Node, not on edge or serverless, and the import chain\nis gated accordingly. Both `REACT_SERVER_BACKPRESSURE` and a\n`backpressure.enabled` config key override the default in either\ndirection.\n\nThe static-asset handler was rewritten to use async `stat()` with\nin-flight coalescing, a bounded pending map, and a bounded miss set, so\na flood of unique paths can''t blow the libuv thread pool or the heap.\nHit/miss decisions stay synchronous in the steady state via a\nmicrotask-elision pattern that avoids a `Promise.resolve` round-trip on\nevery request.\n\nWhile exercising the HTTPS path under HTTP/2, two pre-existing bugs\nsurfaced and were fixed in the same branch since the HTTPS surface is on\nthe critical path. Building a WHATWG `Request` from `req.headers` under\nNode''s HTTP/2 compat layer threw `TypeError: Key\nSymbol(sensitiveHeaders) ... cannot be converted to a ByteString`\nbecause Node tags headers with an internal symbol and adds\n`:method`/`:path`/`:authority`/`:scheme` pseudo-headers; the middleware\nnow copies only string keys that don''t begin with `:`. Separately,\nHTTP/1.1''s `keepAliveTimeout`/`headersTimeout`/`requestTimeout` don''t\napply to HTTP/2 sessions, so an HTTP/2 slow-loris would have hung the\nworker indefinitely; a session-level `setTimeout` closes the gap. A\nrelated discovery — Node''s default 30s `connectionsCheckingInterval`\nsilently masks the configured timeouts — is fixed by passing a 5s\ninterval to `createServer()` and exposing it as a config option.\n\nThe runtime had no defenses against partial requests, no graceful\nshutdown story under k8s (the master is PID 1; the OS doesn''t propagate\nsignals to workers), no concurrency ceiling under burst load, and no way\nfor an orchestrator to learn that a worker had died before the listener\nsocket closed. Each gap was independently capable of producing dropped\nrequests, runaway latency, or a thundering crash-loop in production.\nThis branch closes all of them and lays the groundwork for the\nload-shedding behavior that the upcoming docs page describes.","tree":{"sha":"210b81821a4bf2e9c93a06551fd24346219ea063","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lazarv/react-server/git/trees/210b81821a4bf2e9c93a06551fd24346219ea063"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lazarv/react-server/git/commits/84abefcfbbb163d8d1391d5ef5a5af3f2dc8838f","verification":{"payload":"tree 210b81821a4bf2e9c93a06551fd24346219ea063\nparent 4d5d2b7009c089533d83bb0e6336f9a24f13245f\nauthor Viktor Lázár <lazarv1982@gmail.com> 1777382310 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777382310 +0200\n\nfeat: backpressure (#408)\n\nHardens `react-server start` for production deployment behind a load\nbalancer or a k8s/Docker orchestrator. The Node HTTP server now ships\nwith sensible slow-loris and idle-connection timeouts, signals propagate\ncorrectly through the cluster master, workers drain in-flight requests\non `SIGTERM` instead of dropping them, and a crash-loop guard prevents\nfork-bombing the host on a deterministic boot failure. A new readiness\nendpoint reports worker liveness so external probes can route around a\ndead worker before the kernel reaps the socket.\n\nThe headline addition is an **adaptive admission controller** built on\n`performance.eventLoopUtilization()` with an AIMD update loop. Under\nload it expands the in-flight limit while ELU stays below target and\ncontracts multiplicatively when the loop saturates, holding tail latency\nwell below the unbounded baseline. Admission is FIFO across the wait\nqueue so requests don''t starve, and a fast-path release skips the EWMA\nbookkeeping on the hot path. Backpressure is opt-in by default and\nauto-enables only under `react-server start` cluster mode — the feature\nis meaningful on Node, not on edge or serverless, and the import chain\nis gated accordingly. Both `REACT_SERVER_BACKPRESSURE` and a\n`backpressure.enabled` config key override the default in either\ndirection.\n\nThe static-asset handler was rewritten to use async `stat()` with\nin-flight coalescing, a bounded pending map, and a bounded miss set, so\na flood of unique paths can''t blow the libuv thread pool or the heap.\nHit/miss decisions stay synchronous in the steady state via a\nmicrotask-elision pattern that avoids a `Promise.resolve` round-trip on\nevery request.\n\nWhile exercising the HTTPS path under HTTP/2, two pre-existing bugs\nsurfaced and were fixed in the same branch since the HTTPS surface is on\nthe critical path. Building a WHATWG `Request` from `req.headers` under\nNode''s HTTP/2 compat layer threw `TypeError: Key\nSymbol(sensitiveHeaders) ... cannot be converted to a ByteString`\nbecause Node tags headers with an internal symbol and adds\n`:method`/`:path`/`:authority`/`:scheme` pseudo-headers; the middleware\nnow copies only string keys that don''t begin with `:`. Separately,\nHTTP/1.1''s `keepAliveTimeout`/`headersTimeout`/`requestTimeout` don''t\napply to HTTP/2 sessions, so an HTTP/2 slow-loris would have hung the\nworker indefinitely; a session-level `setTimeout` closes the gap. A\nrelated discovery — Node''s default 30s `connectionsCheckingInterval`\nsilently masks the configured timeouts — is fixed by passing a 5s\ninterval to `createServer()` and exposing it as a config option.\n\nThe runtime had no defenses against partial requests, no graceful\nshutdown story under k8s (the master is PID 1; the OS doesn''t propagate\nsignals to workers), no concurrency ceiling under burst load, and no way\nfor an orchestrator to learn that a worker had died before the listener\nsocket closed. Each gap was independently capable of producing dropped\nrequests, runaway latency, or a thundering crash-loop in production.\nThis branch closes all of them and lays the groundwork for the\nload-shedding behavior that the upcoming docs page describes.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp8LOmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASEkQAKlOb28FBecdbtrMHej4HjyY\n/jIs4XorXNvoarH5LuO0J93/g4XsZNVc8Ub+KxeMKxAc4qlcqNG/C9ggg1E+2xLW\nmFK5YD03AgCy0j+PTvQnkj/0WAKixkD9Q8NS5NlSzImgNKe+U6utPSELi4TxFjnh\nZglqrXruAwGRELiLtlelHAHpdRR9Rkc0GKz5wzzT0bKZKLLg5T6qyAOu5l5zGwc4\nXY8eIQkLrlCbmJeX7txu6CjcXtio9+8r8fCVpgwX7kB3F2D0Fe49snaSYQqEac5d\nUYAtdZoxyYWuv5QZ+2ry3a0K6L1+eFQwN1abKXantB3Du56Tr5z6Lpa1KID3B41+\nna5oKcB/qSzStU1RammLyNL9yKtD/CknZCp31dmauo43XUmaBsrv8N4VRA3LVqBI\nGdgLcZ7Jda8i/4T8DISQKQQVQnu/TP9mtOZRobVYkmMDZW6hvZ3oudwLDLVwI1h2\nbArS9YQj6hc9/nDXwldBZppmXFlAVpQXsjFrh5hB8zkYzGwUUZuY7Gx6P0/gZdhk\n46/wjJvHt1Hj6eRxIy0ZTdbvPlhOhZSdkFgfYefgJIlUBpBUP2T/eOVeAI0DDW9N\nelS2d45qkl6K+/QU6Ztt7Fm7W17mfmA4cWXF8JgtvSKnj6xxCXvfoSzcXwzeCgzq\nqHYKQhZGIVfX5vin6+Q+\n=RXaL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-28T13:18:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com