ollowers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lazarv","id":1749493,"login":"lazarv","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDk0OTM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lazarv/react-server/commit/8c91d411f37a5ece48486de6c8ded1016f4e300a","node_id":"C_kwDOKWnYDNoAKDhjOTFkNDExZjM3YTVlY2U0ODQ4NmRlNmM4ZGVkMTAxNmY0ZTMwMGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lazarv/react-server/commit/280f54ef9eb3a78e0eba0e1aa7d93b426eb975c5","sha":"280f54ef9eb3a78e0eba0e1aa7d93b426eb975c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lazarv/react-server/commits/280f54ef9eb3a78e0eba0e1aa7d93b426eb975c5"}],"sha":"8c91d411f37a5ece48486de6c8ded1016f4e300a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lazarv/react-server/commits/8c91d411f37a5ece48486de6c8ded1016f4e300a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1749493?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lazarv","id":1749493,"login":"lazarv","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDk0OTM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lazarv/react-server/commits/280f54ef9eb3a78e0eba0e1aa7d93b426eb975c5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-24T20:36:58Z","email":"lazarv1982@gmail.com","name":"Viktor Lázár"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-24T20:36:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: api reference (#405)\n\nAdds an API reference section to the docs, generated on demand from the\nTypeScript definitions of `@lazarv/react-server`. Previously the docs\nonly covered concepts and guides; users reaching for \"what does this\nsubpath export and how is it typed\" had to read the source. This branch\nwalks every public subpath''s `.d.ts` with the TypeScript compiler API,\nextracts each symbol''s signature plus its JSDoc description, `@param`,\n`@returns`, `@example`, `@deprecated`, and `@see` tags, and renders it\nthrough the same MDX pipeline the rest of the docs use — so the output\npicks up `rehype-highlight`, `rehype-mdx-code-props`, the\n`mdx-components` overrides, and fits the existing visual language\nwithout new primitives.\n\nNothing is generated to disk. The data source lives at\n`docs/src/lib/api-reference.mjs`, the dynamic `/api/:slug` page compiles\nMDX at request time with `@mdx-js/mdx` and caches compiled components by\n`(slug, locale, max .d.ts mtime)`, and a small rehype plugin walks every\n`<code>` in the compiled tree to linkify identifiers that match the\ncross-file symbol registry — so type references inside signatures and\ninline code spans become clickable anchors on the same page or\ncross-page links into `/api/<target-slug>`. SSG enumeration comes from a\nsibling `[slug=apiSlug].static.mjs`, and the `[slug=apiSlug]` filename\nalias wires a `matchers` export on the page into the file-router so\nunknown slugs fall through to the site-wide 404 natively — no validator\nmiddleware required. The landing page uses the existing `<dl>` TOC style\nwith sections grouping subpaths by role.\n\nAround the feature, a handful of housekeeping items: the `.md` variants\nserved to AI consumers pick up the same API pages via a\n`renderApiReferencePageMarkdown` branch in the existing `/md/[...slug]`\nhandler; `api_translation_banner` and `api_landing_title` are added to\nthe paraglide catalog so the \"not translated\" notice is a\nsingle-source-of-truth message instead of a hardcoded string; six\nmalformed JSDoc blocks in the runtime''s `.d.ts` files (missing closing\nfences on `@example` code blocks) are fixed, cleaning up editor hover\ntooltips as a side effect; and a long-standing race in `DarkModeSwitch`\nwhere the mount-time effect overwrote the cookie to `dark=0` before the\nsibling read-effect could call `setDark` is patched by guarding the\nwriter on the sentinel `null` initial state, so the theme cookie now\nactually persists across refreshes.","tree":{"sha":"cabf4e75308d57c9fbfd8897891e1b54e4a6e204","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lazarv/react-server/git/trees/cabf4e75308d57c9fbfd8897891e1b54e4a6e204"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lazarv/react-server/git/commits/280f54ef9eb3a78e0eba0e1aa7d93b426eb975c5","verification":{"payload":"tree cabf4e75308d57c9fbfd8897891e1b54e4a6e204\nparent 09d92970763aeb82c82672ce42deebca123a6776\nauthor Viktor Lázár <lazarv1982@gmail.com> 1777063018 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777063018 +0200\n\ndocs: api reference (#405)\n\nAdds an API reference section to the docs, generated on demand from the\nTypeScript definitions of `@lazarv/react-server`. Previously the docs\nonly covered concepts and guides; users reaching for \"what does this\nsubpath export and how is it typed\" had to read the source. This branch\nwalks every public subpath''s `.d.ts` with the TypeScript compiler API,\nextracts each symbol''s signature plus its JSDoc description, `@param`,\n`@returns`, `@example`, `@deprecated`, and `@see` tags, and renders it\nthrough the same MDX pipeline the rest of the docs use — so the output\npicks up `rehype-highlight`, `rehype-mdx-code-props`, the\n`mdx-components` overrides, and fits the existing visual language\nwithout new primitives.\n\nNothing is generated to disk. The data source lives at\n`docs/src/lib/api-reference.mjs`, the dynamic `/api/:slug` page compiles\nMDX at request time with `@mdx-js/mdx` and caches compiled components by\n`(slug, locale, max .d.ts mtime)`, and a small rehype plugin walks every\n`<code>` in the compiled tree to linkify identifiers that match the\ncross-file symbol registry — so type references inside signatures and\ninline code spans become clickable anchors on the same page or\ncross-page links into `/api/<target-slug>`. SSG enumeration comes from a\nsibling `[slug=apiSlug].static.mjs`, and the `[slug=apiSlug]` filename\nalias wires a `matchers` export on the page into the file-router so\nunknown slugs fall through to the site-wide 404 natively — no validator\nmiddleware required. The landing page uses the existing `<dl>` TOC style\nwith sections grouping subpaths by role.\n\nAround the feature, a handful of housekeeping items: the `.md` variants\nserved to AI consumers pick up the same API pages via a\n`renderApiReferencePageMarkdown` branch in the existing `/md/[...slug]`\nhandler; `api_translation_banner` and `api_landing_title` are added to\nthe paraglide catalog so the \"not translated\" notice is a\nsingle-source-of-truth message instead of a hardcoded string; six\nmalformed JSDoc blocks in the runtime''s `.d.ts` files (missing closing\nfences on `@example` code blocks) are fixed, cleaning up editor hover\ntooltips as a side effect; and a long-standing race in `DarkModeSwitch`\nwhere the mount-time effect overwrote the cookie to `dark=0` before the\nsibling read-effect could call `setDark` is patched by guarding the\nwriter on the sentinel `null` initial state, so the theme cookie now\nactually persists across refreshes.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp69RqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPRIQALAsn+TKL44eem18WH0OdpXJ\nz+YMJrZxH1XZtbtLkLhLf7Uk2l0+ggiM4pFmMeNmqdFjyCvplEqCh/QRUHlTD7hK\nQh7+1kAjW7DGcHWmIFCef0KzXrUmsQVoVyX5jWwwqV91ytdhQRxe2KBBep82712Q\nW+o6z2GoeaAO3pm0nx9YUNi4A9vQDQu/bxykB1sGu6yGHKbZLOLkx2ki+u/2Hs9s\nXbScnyWL3URAS2SdMU5aztr2YaH7/XEerskQiVoMWXpILIeyiWVV4Gy28nv+WEHn\na4VsdTD5mWcyRU/Go7cbSf+Ld4mNina3LPCE6guOMnTn22fkPdph+BP+R4FebG2o\nGlq+hMMgRzDnN2CMrrdJhQJds8tQHUza7WR/d4Tespth0jGDy7PwfL/7+6n9an0v\nUz7BknOp2GaPa2wI5ltaQJSM5kOvYozqIxqm7FGSNhVWXffKO2VxyxmTy6rm3q5P\nRqcZtw+7nx+Kmmzet8ffTP8mRhSppzeiZbzF5XYNjnxh2WjBS0Fat3+fOenmER3B\nXNe5Vu5lVNljqtlDIvCEtnnfzScmSTdTz1bcHMYuA3zzSaoU1Mg+VTJn4I7Ia3FJ\nDykYgEqPUs/M+N4XRdIp3UzwdkiHUF43My73lNOXop7UGvH5V5+OEh0b99mm1f6B\nNqhM8ql9D+U02xb1JIkX\n=RIdP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-24T20:36:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lazarv/react-server/commit/280f54ef9eb3a78e0eba0e1aa7d93b426eb975c5","node_id":"C_kwDOKWnYDNoAKDI4MGY1NGVmOWViM2E3OGUwZWJhMGUxYWE3ZDkzYjQyNmViOTc1YzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lazarv/react-server/commit/09d92970763aeb82c82672ce42deebca123a6776","sha":"09d92970763aeb82c82672ce42deebca123a6776","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lazarv/react-server/commits/09d92970763aeb82c82672ce42deebca123a6776"}],"sha":"280f54ef9eb3a78e0eba0e1aa7d93b426eb975c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lazarv/react-server/commits/280f54ef9eb3a78e0eba0e1aa7d93b426eb975c5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1749493?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lazarv","id":1749493,"login":"lazarv","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDk0OTM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lazarv/react-server/commits/09d92970763aeb82c82672ce42deebca123a6776/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-24T16:36:18Z","email":"lazarv1982@gmail.com","name":"Viktor Lázár"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-24T16:36:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: router matchers (#404)\n\nThe file-router''s underlying `match()` primitive has long supported\nnamed parameter matchers via `[param=alias]` syntax, but the file-router\nitself never exposed a way for a dynamic page to actually register its\nown matcher predicates. This branch closes that gap: a page (or\nmiddleware or API route) can now `export const matchers =\ndescriptor.createMatchers({ alias: (value) => … })` and the runtime\napplies those predicates during routing — before any page code loads.\nThis lets sibling routes divide the same parameter slot by shape, for\nexample pairing `/product/[sku=uppercase]` with a bare `/product/[sku]`\nfallback so that rejected SKUs fall through instead of 404ing. Matchers\nare a strictly routing-layer concern and complement the existing\n`validate` export, which only runs after a route has already been\nselected.\n\nAlong the way `buildHref` turned out to have its own latent bug: its\nregex used `\\w+` inside the bracket, so it silently skipped both\n`[name=alias]` and every optional form (`[[name]]`, `[[...name]]`),\nleaving the raw bracket literal in the emitted URL. The replacement uses\nan explicit four-alternative regex with the alias suffix as an optional\ntrailing group per form, strips the alias (it''s a routing-time concern,\nnot a URL concern), and collapses any `//` introduced by empty optional\nsubstitutions. Documentation in both English and Japanese, the\ntyped-file-router example, and integration tests covering both required\nand catch-all matchers with their fall-through behavior are included so\nthe whole story is reachable from the nav of the running example.","tree":{"sha":"98c27f71b249b897ce91f0b5fd91fc001dd501d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lazarv/react-server/git/trees/98c27f71b249b897ce91f0b5fd91fc001dd501d5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lazarv/react-server/git/commits/09d92970763aeb82c82672ce42deebca123a6776","verification":{"payload":"tree 98c27f71b249b897ce91f0b5fd91fc001dd501d5\nparent eef0e2d559e003ce26bfa56aeeb997b8dd191f7c\nauthor Viktor Lázár <lazarv1982@gmail.com> 1777048578 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777048578 +0200\n\nfeat: router matchers (#404)\n\nThe file-router''s underlying `match()` primitive has long supported\nnamed parameter matchers via `[param=alias]` syntax, but the file-router\nitself never exposed a way for a dynamic page to actually register its\nown matcher predicates. This branch closes that gap: a page (or\nmiddleware or API route) can now `export const matchers =\ndescriptor.createMatchers({ alias: (value) => … })` and the runtime\napplies those predicates during routing — before any page code loads.\nThis lets sibling routes divide the same parameter slot by shape, for\nexample pairing `/product/[sku=uppercase]` with a bare `/product/[sku]`\nfallback so that rejected SKUs fall through instead of 404ing. Matchers\nare a strictly routing-layer concern and complement the existing\n`validate` export, which only runs after a route has already been\nselected.\n\nAlong the way `buildHref` turned out to have its own latent bug: its\nregex used `\\w+` inside the bracket, so it silently skipped both\n`[name=alias]` and every optional form (`[[name]]`, `[[...name]]`),\nleaving the raw bracket literal in the emitted URL. The replacement uses\nan explicit four-alternative regex with the alias suffix as an optional\ntrailing group per form, strips the alias (it''s a routing-time concern,\nnot a URL concern), and collapses any `//` introduced by empty optional\nsubstitutions. Documentation in both English and Japanese, the\ntyped-file-router example, and integration tests covering both required\nand catch-all matchers with their fall-through behavior are included so\nthe whole story is reachable from the nav of the running example.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp65wCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACaIQAD3O+ak5wFNsEDVSZi05uEFp\n6vy+AG7gT1j0XHN+WzUzmzqqBvNYVRNcZi5rR43/+XTvG7isZXtBBTha6nRY0um/\nHUB9N/3qit6L5a0jdI1Hf0QSQ4QstrtbI+t4NIoDKcTb/0SxzzNOTLQ25g7d0PXv\