30ae0bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lazarv/react-server/commits/4fb7cfcfa3dc84ce3bdcecdfa9908fecb30ae0bd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1749493?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lazarv","id":1749493,"login":"lazarv","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDk0OTM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lazarv/react-server/commits/a0c7b6386c782f0e6faa490e0d4b20fd4b7a0403/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-15T13:22:44Z","email":"lazarv1982@gmail.com","name":"Viktor Lázár"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-15T13:22:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: rsc reply (#393)\n\nThis PR brings `@lazarv/rsc`''s reply path up to parity with React''s\npost-CVE hardening and completes the wire format on the client → server\ndirection. Two things were missing: our `encodeReply`/`decodeReply` only\nhandled synchronous values (plain objects, arrays, typed arrays, maps,\nsets, files, server refs), and the decoder had no resource ceilings, so\na hostile or oversized payload could push the process into unbounded\nwork before any server action ran. Both are addressed here, and the\nsecurity model is documented so hosts know what the protocol does and\ndoesn''t defend against.\n\nOn the protocol side, the client encoder now pre-resolves Promises,\n`ReadableStream`s, `AsyncIterable`s, and sync `Iterator`s into outlined\n`FormData` rows (`$@`, `$r`, `$b`, `$x`, `$X`) before the synchronous\nwalker runs, with cycle-safe visit tracking and back-reference\nreservation so a resolved value containing the same thenable doesn''t\nrecurse. The server side is a new reply decoder that matches React''s\nstructural defenses: `__proto__`/`constructor`/`prototype` stripped\nduring `JSON.parse`, reference path walks pinned to\n`Object.prototype`/`Array.prototype` with own-property checks, `then`\nfunctions scrubbed to `null`, and callables restricted to the\nserver-reference allowlist and temporary-reference proxy — no `eval`, no\n`new Function` on decoded bytes. Errors are redacted to digests in\nproduction via an `onError` hook on the host.\n\nThe PR provides seven configurable resource ceilings on top of those\nstructural defenses (`maxRows`, `maxDepth`, `maxBytes`, `maxBoundArgs`,\n`maxBigIntDigits`, `maxStringLength`, `maxStreamChunks`), wired through\n`serverFunctions.limits` in `react-server.config.mjs` and surfaced in\nboth `schema.d.ts` and `schema.json`. Defaults match React''s upstream;\nbreaches throw a tagged `DecodeLimitError` before the server function\nruns, so operators get per-limit observability and zero side effects on\nrejection. The docs commit adds a Security section to the\nbundler-agnostic RSC serialization page and a new\n`server-function-limits` feature page in both English and Japanese,\ncovering the threat model, the always-on structural barriers, the\nconfigurable ceilings, and explicitly what remains the host''s\nresponsibility (authn/z, CSRF, rate limiting, transport integrity).","tree":{"sha":"f45af9c8828423a819844664f15d73ce962d31dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lazarv/react-server/git/trees/f45af9c8828423a819844664f15d73ce962d31dc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lazarv/react-server/git/commits/a0c7b6386c782f0e6faa490e0d4b20fd4b7a0403","verification":{"payload":"tree f45af9c8828423a819844664f15d73ce962d31dc\nparent b7d51adc30710337ae5de01465092e49c4c14eb2\nauthor Viktor Lázár <lazarv1982@gmail.com> 1776259364 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776259364 +0200\n\nfeat: rsc reply (#393)\n\nThis PR brings `@lazarv/rsc`''s reply path up to parity with React''s\npost-CVE hardening and completes the wire format on the client → server\ndirection. Two things were missing: our `encodeReply`/`decodeReply` only\nhandled synchronous values (plain objects, arrays, typed arrays, maps,\nsets, files, server refs), and the decoder had no resource ceilings, so\na hostile or oversized payload could push the process into unbounded\nwork before any server action ran. Both are addressed here, and the\nsecurity model is documented so hosts know what the protocol does and\ndoesn''t defend against.\n\nOn the protocol side, the client encoder now pre-resolves Promises,\n`ReadableStream`s, `AsyncIterable`s, and sync `Iterator`s into outlined\n`FormData` rows (`$@`, `$r`, `$b`, `$x`, `$X`) before the synchronous\nwalker runs, with cycle-safe visit tracking and back-reference\nreservation so a resolved value containing the same thenable doesn''t\nrecurse. The server side is a new reply decoder that matches React''s\nstructural defenses: `__proto__`/`constructor`/`prototype` stripped\nduring `JSON.parse`, reference path walks pinned to\n`Object.prototype`/`Array.prototype` with own-property checks, `then`\nfunctions scrubbed to `null`, and callables restricted to the\nserver-reference allowlist and temporary-reference proxy — no `eval`, no\n`new Function` on decoded bytes. Errors are redacted to digests in\nproduction via an `onError` hook on the host.\n\nThe PR provides seven configurable resource ceilings on top of those\nstructural defenses (`maxRows`, `maxDepth`, `maxBytes`, `maxBoundArgs`,\n`maxBigIntDigits`, `maxStringLength`, `maxStreamChunks`), wired through\n`serverFunctions.limits` in `react-server.config.mjs` and surfaced in\nboth `schema.d.ts` and `schema.json`. Defaults match React''s upstream;\nbreaches throw a tagged `DecodeLimitError` before the server function\nruns, so operators get per-limit observability and zero side effects on\nrejection. The docs commit adds a Security section to the\nbundler-agnostic RSC serialization page and a new\n`server-function-limits` feature page in both English and Japanese,\ncovering the threat model, the always-on structural barriers, the\nconfigurable ceilings, and explicitly what remains the host''s\nresponsibility (authn/z, CSRF, rate limiting, transport integrity).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp35ElCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4HsQAHRa4W8ZOkoDjx6Ss+btDi6e\nNq89h6xwXobbcIayJnt88KrJ12UjbGk4wGbgQbceKBV3ro4+G0Jc18S0NK4QlXYv\nosVc9sJRtlhPz48lpF/Q+SwD+MOp4EysOGk96S+8CczBxIbStbzkCl12Iwrukb84\n7gwayGIM2y8Q6Nv2ClVQFha6tVrBu71zCJ3ZvGh1bTdmWe0C87bjlaUknbRWYSxl\n+b8JTXPkKvRz3g1o+Osz8BTc2JOPAPFW4RwRzkx4wV3QVJYaqSALvja96BT+2bhw\npQOi44navJ5BUJrBVpFJXnBuuqxsW91o0X8ZnYmeM2xQNaUHl3gE+WYwELSDEgOI\nm7HXa2qmxsB+Bn2sijIV4uqp5/6a4z445w0YM2Tn7BIWVV1gzknBE422DWUdr7mk\n6veqPebEjq5WAiJTISf6y/nscsS5Q30G7mxp9ID8+tgKa4N+RZqp3dJyHOXWnd7X\nyOVvFj+etYPBxH8xvoWK/lLiI+PBOsWzSDaCL2S+Gla8CDT7UiGZJ4VfBJY2BUgF\n9HdA1Y9MMRZpWd70ZBuO3YujnWkItnt8vNst6lZjRc77/liIjLvzCrsfuIWU3DLv\nCnPzrFeOOuTT8euLWGwH6MI9HUWB66vl86yFxHmbdkF9cQgKtj2SZBlqLW90rgei\nlOAgbnguZFZyuH5KdPz7\n=mQvb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-15T13:22:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"w