0d059c73b187dbce946f830409d6bf84f3e5c6db","sha":"0d059c73b187dbce946f830409d6bf84f3e5c6db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lazarv/react-server/commits/0d059c73b187dbce946f830409d6bf84f3e5c6db"}],"sha":"464b5a565362fb254a6291cf57c24f86839dfc31","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lazarv/react-server/commits/464b5a565362fb254a6291cf57c24f86839dfc31"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1749493?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lazarv","id":1749493,"login":"lazarv","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDk0OTM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lazarv/react-server/commits/0d059c73b187dbce946f830409d6bf84f3e5c6db/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-10T14:34:42Z","email":"lazarv1982@gmail.com","name":"Viktor Lázár"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-10T14:34:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: use cache plugin (#387)\n\nThe `use-cache-inline` plugin had several bugs in how it tracks closure\nvariables and handles exported cached functions. The root cause was a\nflat `locals` array that accumulated variable names from all function\nscopes without any scoping — variables declared inside one function\nwould leak into the closure capture list of completely unrelated sibling\nfunctions. This caused the plugin to emit invalid `.bind()` calls on\nmodule-level exported cached functions, producing parse errors like\n`export __cache_name__.bind(null, src, selector, isolate)` during\nproduction builds.\nThe fix replaces the flat `locals` array with a proper scope stack. Each\nnon-cached function pushes a scope entry on enter and pops it on leave,\nso only variables from actual enclosing lexical scopes are considered\nfor closure capture. Module-level cached functions now correctly see an\nempty scope stack and skip `.bind()` entirely.\n\nAdditional fixes included in this change: destructured binding patterns\n(`ObjectPattern`, `ArrayPattern`, `AssignmentPattern`, `RestElement`)\nare now properly walked when collecting local variable names. Function\nparameters in enclosing scopes are tracked for nested cached function\nclosure capture. Identifiers in non-reference positions (object property\nkeys, member expression properties, declaration ids, function names) are\nexcluded from closure matching — this was necessary because the JSX\ntransform runs before the cache plugin, turning JSX attribute names into\nregular Property key Identifiers that would otherwise be falsely\ncaptured. Exported cached functions are now wrapped in\n`__react_cache__()` at module level and get correct\n`CACHE_KEY`/`CACHE_PROVIDER` assignments using scoping-aware target\nresolution.","tree":{"sha":"d505aecfa9c36a5564ff2ab1e364df4f85066a2f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lazarv/react-server/git/trees/d505aecfa9c36a5564ff2ab1e364df4f85066a2f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lazarv/react-server/git/commits/0d059c73b187dbce946f830409d6bf84f3e5c6db","verification":{"payload":"tree d505aecfa9c36a5564ff2ab1e364df4f85066a2f\nparent 1c4cca103d00a0eeb090eb0ebbc1a9685e0fa6de\nauthor Viktor Lázár <lazarv1982@gmail.com> 1775831682 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1775831682 +0200\n\nfix: use cache plugin (#387)\n\nThe `use-cache-inline` plugin had several bugs in how it tracks closure\nvariables and handles exported cached functions. The root cause was a\nflat `locals` array that accumulated variable names from all function\nscopes without any scoping — variables declared inside one function\nwould leak into the closure capture list of completely unrelated sibling\nfunctions. This caused the plugin to emit invalid `.bind()` calls on\nmodule-level exported cached functions, producing parse errors like\n`export __cache_name__.bind(null, src, selector, isolate)` during\nproduction builds.\nThe fix replaces the flat `locals` array with a proper scope stack. Each\nnon-cached function pushes a scope entry on enter and pops it on leave,\nso only variables from actual enclosing lexical scopes are considered\nfor closure capture. Module-level cached functions now correctly see an\nempty scope stack and skip `.bind()` entirely.\n\nAdditional fixes included in this change: destructured binding patterns\n(`ObjectPattern`, `ArrayPattern`, `AssignmentPattern`, `RestElement`)\nare now properly walked when collecting local variable names. Function\nparameters in enclosing scopes are tracked for nested cached function\nclosure capture. Identifiers in non-reference positions (object property\nkeys, member expression properties, declaration ids, function names) are\nexcluded from closure matching — this was necessary because the JSX\ntransform runs before the cache plugin, turning JSX attribute names into\nregular Property key Identifiers that would otherwise be falsely\ncaptured. Exported cached functions are now wrapped in\n`__react_cache__()` at module level and get correct\n`CACHE_KEY`/`CACHE_PROVIDER` assignments using scoping-aware target\nresolution.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp2QqCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAq5gQABBHjDCmvRLyLeXioqIRmFX/\ntnzneLtwqecwz6ZjbiWlVW4jnRTOaH4+YJqRnKca7kxbKkkfc3AwHuk47NeOr96y\nm+wJUgVMHRD400yU2mrcMWIHs1p8LEC4Vq7Acnodmu5cGuQLt08rt87YfzlxLacj\nmEhsCzTQjEhqGxoUgS