om/lazarv/react-server/commit/b7f5f45a9033b8ed754cff40f01290d03a0aa079","sha":"b7f5f45a9033b8ed754cff40f01290d03a0aa079","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lazarv/react-server/commits/b7f5f45a9033b8ed754cff40f01290d03a0aa079"}],"sha":"6e54637463da3f6f44b73d5bf7b06397d234751b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lazarv/react-server/commits/6e54637463da3f6f44b73d5bf7b06397d234751b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1749493?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lazarv","id":1749493,"login":"lazarv","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDk0OTM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lazarv/react-server/commits/b7f5f45a9033b8ed754cff40f01290d03a0aa079/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-02T14:43:43Z","email":"lazarv1982@gmail.com","name":"Viktor Lázár"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-02T14:43:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: enhanced router (#372)\n\nA major evolution of the `@lazarv/react-server` router, introducing a\nfully typed routing system, a resource abstraction for data management,\nscroll restoration, and client-only page support in the file router.\nThis is a foundational change that brings the router closer to feature\nparity with — and in several areas beyond — framework-level routers like\nNext.js App Router and TanStack Router.\n                                                  \n- **Typed Router** — Define routes with full TypeScript type safety for\npath params, search params, and navigation. Includes path/search param\nparsers, encoders/decoders, and validator schema support (single or\nmultiple validators). New\n`Route`, `Link`, and hook APIs (`useParams`, `useSearchParams`,\n`useNavigate`) are fully type-aware.\n- **Resources** — A new `@lazarv/react-server/resources` export\nintroducing a data resource primitive. Resources can be defined as\nclient-side, server-side, or both, with file-system conventions\n(`.resource.ts`) in the file router. Supports\nCRUD-style operations with automatic cache integration.\n- **Scroll Restoration** — Comprehensive scroll restoration system\nsupporting both `auto` and `manual` modes. Tracks scroll positions\nacross navigations with configurable selectors, smooth scrolling, and\nhash fragment support. Fully\nclient-driven with no server round-trips.\n- **Client-Only Pages** — The file router now supports client-only pages\nthat render entirely on the client without a server component\ncounterpart. Includes proper loading/fallback component support for\nclient-only routes.\n- **Virtual Routes** — Programmatically define routes in\n`react-server.config.mjs` without corresponding files on disk. Enables\ndynamic route registration from plugins or configuration.\n- **Scoped Fallback Routes** — Fallback (catch-all) routes can now be\nscoped to specific route subtrees rather than only matching globally.\n- **Functional Search Param Updaters** — `setSearchParams` now accepts a\nfunction `(prev) => next` for atomic updates based on current state, in\naddition to the existing object form.","tree":{"sha":"94f4d90e86b1415f21e19728af441293b680b056","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lazarv/react-server/git/trees/94f4d90e86b1415f21e19728af441293b680b056"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lazarv/react-server/git/commits/b7f5f45a9033b8ed754cff40f01290d03a0aa079","verification":{"payload":"tree 94f4d90e86b1415f21e19728af441293b680b056\nparent 8be293dcde58b8f3d7ce1127ce68b95a54c72f7f\nauthor Viktor Lázár <lazarv1982@gmail.com> 1775141023 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1775141023 +0200\n\nfeat: enhanced router (#372)\n\nA major evolution of the `@lazarv/react-server` router, introducing a\nfully typed routing system, a resource abstraction for data management,\nscroll restoration, and client-only page support in the file router.\nThis is a foundational change that brings the router closer to feature\nparity with — and in several areas beyond — framework-level routers like\nNext.js App Router and TanStack Router.\n                                                  \n- **Typed Router** — Define routes with full TypeScript type safety for\npath params, search params, and navigation. Includes path/search param\nparsers, encoders/decoders, and validator schema support (single or\nmultiple validators). New\n`Route`, `Link`, and hook APIs (`useParams`, `useSearchParams`,\n`useNavigate`) are fully type-aware.\n- **Resources** — A new `@lazarv/react-server/resources` export\nintroducing a data resource primitive. Resources can be defined as\nclient-side, server-side, or both, with file-system conventions\n(`.resource.ts`) in the file router. Supports\nCRUD-style operations with automatic cache integration.\n- **Scroll Restoration** — Comprehensive scroll restoration system\nsupporting both `auto` and `manual` modes. Tracks scroll positions\nacross navigations with configurable selectors, smooth scrolling, and\nhash fragment support. Fully\nclient-driven with no server round-trips.\n- **Client-Only Pages** — The file router now supports client-only pages\nthat render entirely on the client without a server component\ncounterpart. Includes proper loading/fallback component support for\nclient-only routes.\n- **Virtual Routes** — Programmatically define routes in\n`react-server.config.mjs` without corresponding files on disk. Enables\ndynamic route registration from plugins or configuration.\n- **Scoped Fallback Routes** — Fallback (catch-all) routes can now be\nscoped to specific route subtrees rather than only matching globally.\n- **Functional Search Param Updaters** — `setSearchParams` now accepts a\nfunction `(prev) => next` for atomic updates based on current state, in\naddition to the existing object form.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpzoCfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwuIQADvJHR5k5XW/GaYp9/NgtykZ\nonHgNZUviD/nsCsGIIBkTiGE5ZSfvqCPP/uWZHKcGmG5OaPb5KhvmYN8L5a65dUH\nEAF0CaJbsc/i/7JGmewozf5Xx9t/fNrfWCdynzgrkDFpxG1z6NgepjOzn/6GzEJx\n0FzmW5iPOOK5CKdicl2JaMB3Q28uj4M8GmPGtmw5h3Ke8LTGeesOLXkc+vwU793/\nQS8nOLuuZqdzkL9cuSQyMiGyZhkUlJhD8UgjkU7IAAiWGg5XW7xFYGiFQy3Car4b\nfZt8YQF5EWlAr6lJBZ1GKzCLBah4jL89eNryIz+QCKrlr9pp14AOuiL76d2n2r3+\npzjy1RK/VUolO6Soon5cFvMMU7gQq4mtwhke+MQp/Hp8tZz9cFrddTqk3hg5tuxh\ngOZ9c4SXoJz0uHpGDzQwMgED0uyzWkXrvhQfcsXEZoFS6EVbdGbqxUz5x/9A4cO6\nZDeH7D6FFg9G3Dg/grvbsuDLMmcagnzyaCuQd7zZgi50h5/R6FoOY4tZ+tWyiPUR\n/rmEjVf++5d/mAw7Zj/F8WWKTeoeKJRHEIzAl9xN5SksEVTPEL/rJcGrQY5rd77c\nur3ZhPLTNKM8qjhA8Iq775MoCT2Je3O80mVQdiz4EexaUjJOvfRNI+sVh3KUmXmL\nvplrEM8yz+bbyAeJxO8n\n=70Il\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-02T14:43:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/recei