eceived_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/lazarv/react-server/commit/ce3bf6062b5eb8e4c498281aae6ad28cd28dec05","node_id":"C_kwDOKWnYDNoAKGNlM2JmNjA2MmI1ZWI4ZTRjNDk4MjgxYWFlNmFkMjhjZDI4ZGVjMDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/lazarv/react-server/commit/639d8ef59943573c4a40166092a4372954d67243","sha":"639d8ef59943573c4a40166092a4372954d67243","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lazarv/react-server/commits/639d8ef59943573c4a40166092a4372954d67243"}],"sha":"ce3bf6062b5eb8e4c498281aae6ad28cd28dec05","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lazarv/react-server/commits/ce3bf6062b5eb8e4c498281aae6ad28cd28dec05"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1749493?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lazarv","id":1749493,"login":"lazarv","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDk0OTM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazarv","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lazarv/react-server/commits/639d8ef59943573c4a40166092a4372954d67243/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-06T21:05:23Z","email":"lazarv1982@gmail.com","name":"Viktor Lázár"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-06T21:05:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: config schema validation (#341)\n\nThis PR brings the `react-server.config.*` validation schema to full\nparity with Vite 8, marks internally-hardcoded options as forbidden with\nclear error messages, and adds a `--no-validation` CLI flag as an escape\nhatch.\n\n### Problem\n\nThe config validation schema was missing many Vite options (e.g.\n`server.ws`, `server.strictPort`, `server.allowedHosts`, etc.), causing\nfalse validation errors when users set legitimate Vite configuration.\nAdditionally, several Vite options that react-server hardcodes\ninternally (like `appType`, `build.target`, `json`) were silently\naccepted but then overwritten at runtime, leading to confusing behavior.\n\n### Changes\n\n#### Schema parity with Vite 8\n\nAdded validators, TypeScript types, JSON Schema definitions, and\ndescriptions for all previously missing Vite config options across every\nsection.\n\n#### Forbidden options\n\nIntroduced a `forbidden()` validator that produces clear error messages\nexplaining **why** an option is forbidden and **what to use instead**.\nThe following options are now forbidden because react-server hardcodes\nthem internally:\n\n#### `--no-validation` CLI flag\n\nAdded `--no-validation` to both `dev` and `build` commands as an escape\nhatch. When set, config validation is completely skipped. This is useful\nif validation incorrectly rejects a valid configuration or when users\nintentionally need to bypass a forbidden option.\n\n#### Documentation (EN + JA)\n\n- **CLI docs**: Added `--no-validation` documentation under both\ndevelopment server and build option sections\n- **Configuration docs**: Added a new \"Config validation\" section\nexplaining the validation behavior and how to disable it","tree":{"sha":"3bfeb8788c0e7f20dbae5e711b14d88afab43dc1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lazarv/react-server/git/trees/3bfeb8788c0e7f20dbae5e711b14d88afab43dc1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lazarv/react-server/git/commits/639d8ef59943573c4a40166092a4372954d67243","verification":{"payload":"tree 3bfeb8788c0e7f20dbae5e711b14d88afab43dc1\nparent 04f2240731c2afbd012747670f694eb74385d9ad\nauthor Viktor Lázár <lazarv1982@gmail.com> 1772831123 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1772831123 +0100\n\nfix: config schema validation (#341)\n\nThis PR brings the `react-server.config.*` validation schema to full\nparity with Vite 8, marks internally-hardcoded options as forbidden with\nclear error messages, and adds a `--no-validation` CLI flag as an escape\nhatch.\n\n### Problem\n\nThe config validation schema was missing many Vite options (e.g.\n`server.ws`, `server.strictPort`, `server.allowedHosts`, etc.), causing\nfalse validation errors when users set legitimate Vite configuration.\nAdditionally, several Vite options that react-server hardcodes\ninternally (like `appType`, `build.target`, `json`) were silently\naccepted but then overwritten at runtime, leading to confusing behavior.\n\n### Changes\n\n#### Schema parity with Vite 8\n\nAdded validators, TypeScript types, JSON Schema definitions, and\ndescriptions for all previously missing Vite config options across every\nsection.\n\n#### Forbidden options\n\nIntroduced a `forbidden()` validator that produces clear error messages\nexplaining **why** an option is forbidden and **what to use instead**.\nThe following options are now forbidden because react-server hardcodes\nthem internally:\n\n#### `--no-validation` CLI flag\n\nAdded `--no-validation` to both `dev` and `build` commands as an escape\nhatch. When set, config validation is completely skipped. This is useful\nif validation incorrectly rejects a valid configuration or when users\nintentionally need to bypass a forbidden option.\n\n#### Documentation (EN + JA)\n\n- **CLI docs**: Added `--no-validation` documentation under both\ndevelopment server and build option sections\n- **Configuration docs**: Added a new \"Config validation\" section\nexplaining the validation behavior and how to disable it","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpq0GTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtFcQAE7smYHO1uPr6WTUoQrD1ytu\nrgNgfyB0hBENf9e7PjrUjVZPreuqwObzdMxjwZJkY2eadtFfIH90b0K6kphKnunY\n07QBzmOSumMFfNOgjhuMYYM4NXL16yQ5elTEIFdSejWeNvyJbhFDokvZGfVW5bxB\nw8Lehtt7+k2zRlKlBK013HaBuZRdnR58BdPVKwKOwZXZGx4cnyC5QDEkPJtLQNsl\n9Lc/vlZFP8KaR8Fl+Zqqws0rCQP791lkTqFqfFZqKOxg5QoTMq5hy4A5pFJbriYh\nXz5BosTLD7aKKJ7eMkx4PJ7h0j/z2BBSJmuAfqgh3cshwO1yHpLDHkvK8dRuY624\n5ULKBTOe3KjEF8je+ULv2YSckMhP8puTkPbwXn+oPzQ8LSFq6SXSDU0M3/A7JkIU\nm4qeHRChdRH1rGdShubic9fq0rmJqziR5yzEV/yNQPzgv8JrNDdGtQJBcoGLkfA7\nO8+JLCW9h0WPyJeXSgVc7/l8R5Xp6QK3EtHmT4mm4QW+B10Igpl2Aytt7G/A9yLG\nYxe97gmnSMzGrnaWjx4v9XgqSS01b8WAWety9pNubdh7VOG4tvCZo7V74gBV7QJd\nYgsNESzzCHXSi9GLApNg5H0naA/FDbVL5OWqA1jwtmYfQ9yeYX9um1UGlnFMOybl\nVD933VQ4cy1HFR8MTgbX\n=aAlb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-06T21:05:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/w